<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="870" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-870-802-a-01" revdate="20260617">
<title>Description</title>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The set has twenty-eight business class passenger
positions which is divided into twenty-four Standard (STD) row and
four Elite Front Row (EFR) passenger positions.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The front row suites are referred as EFR
suites. Each outboard row has one elite front row passenger position
and six standard business class passenger positions. Each inboard
row has one elite front row passenger position and six standard business
class passenger positions. There are two outboard rows and two inboard
rows.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Each suite contains of furniture assembly
with suite slide door, meal table assembly, cocktail table assembly,
full drop privacy screen assembly, dot door installation, armrest
assembly, upper console stowage assembly and IFE system.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The seat assembly is controlled by the ECU
in response to passenger commands from the PCU.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Each furniture assembly has PCU, IUL, RJU,
handset, monitor, USB, ECU, reading light, ambient light, TTL light,
footwell light and RGBW ambient lights.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Each furniture assembly has a meal table,
stowed below the monitor. The meal table is operated manually to the
deployed position and is moved manually by the passenger to the necessary
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Each suite has an In Flight Entertainment
(IFE) system to watch TV and movies with the use of airlines Audio
and Video On Demand (AVOD) system. There is also a 110V AC power outlet
and USB ports for each passenger.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Override Controls:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Manual override controls are given to enable
the seat to be returned to the TTL position in the event of failure
of all or any of the electrical actuators which provides the seat
movement functions.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<?pb?>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="870" seq="803"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-870-803-a-01" revdate="20260617">
<title>Operation</title>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Seat Movement:</para>
<note><para>Information about the business class seat is given in
Safran Seats GB Limited CMM 25-26-61.</para></note>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Seat movement is controlled by the Passenger
Control Unit (PCU).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Movement of the seat is provided by an actuation
system contains tracking, recline, and legrest actuators.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>In case of power failure, each seat movement
has a manual override, which is actuated with override levers, installed
on the seatpan assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the TTL button on the main
PCU to move the seat to the TTL position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the Bed button on the main
PCU to move the seat to the Bed position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the Dine button on the main
PCU to move the seat to the Dine position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push the Attendant Call button on the main
PCU and make sure that the attendant call light comes ON.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Privacy Screen:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the UP button on the privacy
PCU and make sure that the privacy screen rises to the fully deployed
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the DOWN button on the privacy
PCU and make sure that the privacy screen lowers to the fully stowed
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Manual operation (Ref Fig 8):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Two persons are necessary, to manually operate
the privacy screen. One person to operate the manual override lever
and one person to deploy and stow the privacy screen with two hands
on the privacy screen for support.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For EFR and standard row E/F suites: Disengage
the ball studs to lift the top cap (26-240) from the suite adjacent
to the privacy screen and get access to the privacy screen manual
override lever.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For standard row D/G suites: Access to the
privacy screen manual override lever is through the access hole on
the bottom of the G suites.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE PRIVACY SCREEN IS LEVEL AND PARALLEL
TO THE FLOOR WHEN YOU LIFT OR STOW THE PRIVACY SCREEN. IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT CAN OCCUR.</para></caution>
<para>Operate the privacy screen manual override lever. Lift the privacy
screen with two hands on the furthest aft section of privacy screen,
where the privacy screen is mounted to the suite. Make sure that the
privacy screen rises to the fully deployed position.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Operate the privacy screen manual override
lever. Stow the privacy screen with two hands on the furthest aft
section of privacy screen, where the privacy screen is mounted to
the suite. Make sure that the privacy screen lowers to the fully stowed
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Meal Table Assembly Deployment and Stowage:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push the meal table and move forward to release.
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deploy the meal table.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Move the meal table forwards and backwards.
Make sure that the table moves smoothly.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Stow the meal table and make sure that the
meal table latches in the stowed position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Lifevest Assembly:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>To open the lifevest door, pull the lifevest
door pull tab to disengage the press stud from the receptacle and
release the lifevest door.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Pull the external strap and open the lifevest
door.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Put the end of the external strap through
the slot in the lifevest door and close the lifevest door.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>RGBW Ambient Lights:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The ambient lighting system contains of RGBW
strip lights interfaced to seat control system to give control of
the RGBW lighting system to create lighting scenes and transitions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The RGBW strip lights are installed at inner
lower canopy, rear upper canopy, aisle canopy, cocktail strip light,
upper stowage feature light and footwell light.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>All lights are controllable for colour through
the cabin IFE only, and in suite lights (not canopy lighting) turned
ON and OFF through the PCU.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that all ambient lights are ON
when you apply power to the suite.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Open the stowage door and make sure that
the upper stowage light goes dim.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Close the stowage door and make sure that
the upper stowage light brightens.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Reading Lights:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The reading light has a simple ON and OFF
function.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>A faceplate tilt and turn feature lets the
lamp to be switched ON and OFF, while also lets the direction of light
to be adjusted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that the reading light is stowed,
do a check of the lens is not visible and the light is flush with
the surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deploy the reading light (by tilt the face
of the light) and make sure that the reading light comes ON.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Turn the reading light through full movement
and do a check of the reading light direction can be redirected.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Stow the reading light and make sure that
the reading light goes OFF.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Full Height Dropping Privacy Screen Locking
Feature:</para>
<note><para>Applicable to front row centre suites only.</para></note>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Locking procedure (Ref Fig 9):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Make sure that the privacy screen is at the
fully deployed position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the ball studs to lift the two
top caps (26-240, 26-240A) from the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Locking steps as shown in Ref Fig 9, Sheet
2:</para></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Move the adjustable slider aft, out of the
slot on the locking pin (STEP 1).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Turn the locking pin clockwise to lock the
privacy screen in position (STEP 2).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Move the adjustable slider forward in to
the slot on the locking pin (STEP 3).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Full Height Dropping Privacy Screen is now
locked at full height (STEP 4).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the ball studs to attach the two top
caps (26-240, 26-240A) to the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Unlocking procedure (Ref Fig 9):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the ball studs to lift the two
top caps (26-240, 26-240A) from the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Make sure that the Full Height Dropping Privacy
Screen is locked at full height.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Unlocking steps as shown in Ref Fig 9, Sheet
3:</para></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Move the adjustable slider aft, out of the
slot on the locking pin (STEP 1).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Turn the locking pin anti-clockwise to lock
the privacy screen in position (STEP 2).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Move the adjustable slider forward in to
the slot on the locking pin (STEP 3).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Full Height Dropping Privacy Screen is now
unlocked (STEP 4).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the ball studs to attach the two top
caps (26-240, 26-240A) to the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>EPF System:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The EPF system is a safety feature to make
sure that the door can be stowed in the event of a failure in the
primary sliding mechanism of the door assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>In the event of a failure in the primary
sliding mechanism the door will operate in the same way to stow for
TTL.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>When the primary sliding mechanism fails
the main carriage will separate from the EPF bracket which will activate
the EPF button on the outside of the door. The door will then run
on a roller to make sure that the door stowed for TTL.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Wireless Charging Unit:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The wireless charging unit is fitted to the
suites, this must only be used to charge mobile telephones with wireless
charging capability.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Do not keep any other electronic devices
or metallic items, on the wireless charging unit.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Suite Door Operation (Ref Fig 10):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Stowed Position:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>The suite door in stowed position, initial
is moved back and latched for TTL position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>If the door isn&rsquo;t latched correctly,
there will be red indicators shown on the latches.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Open Position:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>If necessary, the suite door can be moved
to the open position to fully forward against the magnetic stop by
passenger.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>In the open position, the suite door is fully
moved to the FWD position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Suite Door Latch Operation:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Get access to the bottom safety latch.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Move and hold the bottom latch in the up
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Hold the bottom latch, move each of the top
latches down, then move the door to forward position.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Move the door forward until it reaches the
magnetic stop.</para>
<note><para>The door is fully open.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>To stow the door, move the door backward
until it reaches to the latch plate.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push each of the, top latches down and move
them over the latch plate.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release the latches and make sure that the
door is locked correctly in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<?pb?>
