<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-1000" revdate="20260318">
<title>TESTING AND FAULT ISOLATION</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="700" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-700-801-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>General</title>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If faults occur when you test the unit, refer
to Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-005-a01">table-25-26-62-99a-005-a01
</refint> for fault isolation and corrective action.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Refer to the history report for possible
faults recorded in service.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Defective or damaged items must be repaired
or replaced for serviceable items.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use the <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="task-25-26-62-99f-805-a01"></refint> to record and report unit
faults to Safran Seats GB Limited.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="700" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-700-802-a-01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Electrical Operation Tests</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To do a test on the electrical equipment.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Tools, Fixtures and Equipment:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="99A" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" id="table-25-26-62-99a-009-a01"><?Pub Lcl
_tabindent="1">
<title>Tools, Fixtures and Equipment</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="left" charoff="50" char="">
<?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="12.00in"?>
<colspec colname="col1">
<colspec colname="col2">
<colspec colname="col3">
<thead valign="bottom">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>REFERENCE AND/OR PART NUMBER</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>DESCRIPTION AND/OR SPECIFICATION</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>SUPPLIER CAGE CODE OR NAME AND ADDRESS</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody valign="top">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Electrical supply for suites</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>115 Volts AC, 400 Hz</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Local purchase</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Electric testing</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Multimeter (Amp, Volt, Ohm)</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Local purchase</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Biddle 247001-47</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Bonding Test Meter</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Local purchase</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Consumables:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect Power:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Connect Power:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>high VOLTAGES. Obey ALL WARNINGS AND CAUTIONS IN THIS
MANUAL. IF YOU DO NOT obey THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK of injury
or DEATH.</para></warning>
<warning><para>DO THE PROCEDURES IN AN ESD AREA. WEAR MANUFACTURER'S
RECOMMENDED WRIST STRAP WHICH IS CONNECTED TO A SOFT GROUND. MAKE
SURE THAT THE WRIST STRAP TOUCHES THE SKIN. OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<para>Connect a 115 Volt AC, 400 Hz, three-phase power supply to the
suites.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Reading Lights:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The reading light has a simple ON and OFF
function.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>A faceplate tilt and turn feature lets the
lamp to be switched ON and OFF, while also lets the direction of light
to be adjusted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Make sure that the reading light is stowed,
make sure that the lens is not visible and the light is flush with
the surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deploy the reading light (by tilt the face
of the light) and make sure that the reading light comes ON.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Turn the reading light through full movement
and do a check of the reading light direction can be redirected.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Stow the reading light and make sure that
the reading light goes OFF.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>RGBW Ambient Lights:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The ambient lighting system contains of RGBW
strip lights interfaced to seat control system to give control of
the RGBW lighting system to create lighting scenes and transitions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The RGBW strip lights are installed at inner
lower canopy, rear upper canopy, aisle canopy, cocktail strip light,
upper stowage feature light and footwell light.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>All lights are controllable for colour through
the cabin IFE only, and in suite lights (not canopy lighting) turned
ON and OFF through the PCU.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Make sure that all ambient lights are ON
when you apply power to the suite.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Open the stowage door and make sure that
the upper stowage light goes dim.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Close the stowage door and make sure that
the upper stowage light brightens.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Attendant Call:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Push the Attendant Call Light button on the
main PCU and make sure that the attendant call light comes ON.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Push the Attendant Call Light button again
on the main PCU and make sure that the attendant call light goes OFF.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="700" seq="803"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-700-803-a-01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Mechanical Operation Tests</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To do a test on the mechanical equipment.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Suite Actuation Movement:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Seat Movement:</para>
<note><para>Information about the business class seat is given in
Safran Seats GB Limited CMM 25-26-61.</para></note>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Seat movement is controlled by the Passenger
Control Unit (PCU).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Movement of the seat is provided by an actuation
system contains tracking, recline, and legrest actuators.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>In case of power failure, each seat movement
has a manual override, which is actuated with override levers, installed
on the seatpan assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the TTL button on the main
PCU to move the seat to the TTL position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the Bed button on the main
PCU to move the seat to the Bed position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the Dine button on the main
PCU to move the seat to the Dine position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push the Attendant Call button on the main
PCU and make sure that the attendant call light comes ON.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Privacy Screen:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the UP button on the privacy
PCU and make sure that the privacy screen rises to the fully deployed
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push and hold the DOWN button on the privacy
PCU and make sure that the privacy screen lowers to the fully stowed
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Manual override operation:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Two persons are necessary, to manually operate
the privacy screen. One person to operate the manual override lever
and one person to deploy and stow the privacy screen with two hands
on the privacy screen for support.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For EFR and standard row E/F suites: Disengage
the ball studs to lift the top cap (26-240) from the suite adjacent
to the privacy screen and get access to the privacy screen manual
override lever.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For standard row D/G suites: Access to the
privacy screen manual override lever is through the access hole on
the bottom of the G suites.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE PRIVACY SCREEN IS LEVEL AND PARALLEL
TO THE FLOOR WHEN YOU LIFT OR STOW THE PRIVACY SCREEN. IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT CAN OCCUR.</para></caution>
<para>Operate the privacy screen manual override lever. Lift the privacy
screen with two hands on the furthest aft section of privacy screen,
where the privacy screen is mounted to the suite. Make sure that the
privacy screen rises to the fully deployed position.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Operate the privacy screen manual override
lever. Stow the privacy screen with two hands on the furthest aft
section of privacy screen, where the privacy screen is mounted to
the suite. Make sure that the privacy screen lowers to the fully stowed
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Meal Table Assembly Deployment and Stowage:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Push the meal table and move forward to release.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deploy the meal table.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Move the meal table forwards and backwards.
Make sure that table moves smoothly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Stow the meal table and make sure that the
meal table latches in the stowed position.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Lifevest Stowage:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To open the lifevest door, pull the lifevest
door pull tab to disengage the press stud from the receptacle and
release the lifevest door.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pull the external strap and open the lifevest
door.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Put the end of the external strap through
the slot in the lifevest door and close the lifevest door.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="700" seq="804"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-700-804-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Electrical Bonding Test</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To do an electrical bonding test on the unit.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>THE ELECTRICAL BONDING PROCEDURE MUST BE DONE ON ANY
BONDING/GROUNDING POINTS THAT HAVE BEEN REMOVED. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THESE INSTRUCTIONS, DAMAGE TO THE UNIT CAN OCCUR.</para></caution>
<para>Measure the bonding resistance of any removed electrical bonding
point, after assembly.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that the configuration of the ground
tag, pressure washer and locking nut etc. are in accordance with the
original stud configuration (See IPL Fig 30 for Ref).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For LRU connectors that have been removed,
do a visual inspection for pushed back, corroded, unseated or misaligned
pins/sockets before you connect the connector. This is to make sure
that the bonding system has been reconnected through correct mating
of the pin/sockets.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Do an Electrical Bonding Test (Ref Fig 1001):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Make sure that the test current is one ampere.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Make sure that the correct test range is
selected on the Bonding Test Meter.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Put one Test Lead from the Bonding Test Meter
on the structure to which the Ground Stud is installed and not the
ground stud itself. This must be approximately 0.25 in (6.35 mm) from
the installed Ground Stud.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Put the second Test Lead in position on the
tag of the Ground Stud lead.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>The measurement taken is to be less than
1 m&ohm;.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="99B" seq="130"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-26-62-99b-130-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Lcl
_grphctype="0">
<title>ELECTRICAL BONDING TEST</title>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-TFI-1001-01-00.cgm" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-130-a01-1" revdate="20260318"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<?pb?>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="700" seq="805"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-700-805-a-01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Fault Isolation</title>
<topic>
<title>General:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use the <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="task-25-26-62-99f-805-a01"></refint> to record and report unit
faults to Safran Seats GB Limited.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For continued fault reports on the same issue,
contact Safran Seats GB Limited for a Technical Event number.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If applicable, make sure that the Technical
Event number is filled in on each Technical Event Notification Sheet
related to the same issue, to keep continuity between reports.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To find faults in the unit&rsquo;s components.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Fault Isolation:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="99A" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" id="table-25-26-62-99a-005-a01"><?Pub Lcl
_tabindent="1">
<title>Fault Isolation</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="left" charoff="50" char="">
<?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="12.00in"?>
<colspec colname="col1" align="center" colwidth="1.00*">
<colspec colname="col2" align="center" colwidth="1.00*">
<colspec colname="col3" align="center" colwidth="1.00*">
<thead valign="bottom">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>FAULT</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>POSSIBLE CAUSE</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>ACTION</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody valign="top">
<row>
<entry morerows="2" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Suite does not move.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Mechanical connection faulty.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of the seat release levers and cables. Repair or
replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of slide alignment.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Repair or replace</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Electrical connection faulty.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of the harness connection, reconnect or replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="2" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>In-Flight Entertainment (IFE) does not work.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Broken wire, loose connection or no power.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of the aircraft supply and connect power. If none
of these refer to the related supplier.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Faulty electronics box.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Fault in monitor.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Reading light does not work.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Loose electrical connections.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of the harness connections from the reading light
to the ECU, connect or replace harness.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Reading light unit unserviceable.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Replace the reading light.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="2" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>RGBW, Ambient light does not work.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Light unit damaged.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Repair or replace the light unit.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>No power to suite.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Connect power to the suite.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Disconnected or faulty power supply harness.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Find the fault in power supply harness and repair.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>DND light does not work.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Loose electrical connections.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of the harness connections from DND light to ECU,
connect or replace harness.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>DND light unit unserviceable.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Replace DND light.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="3" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Privacy Screen does not move.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Mechanical connection faulty.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of the suite release levers and the cables. Repair
or replace.</para>
<para>Make sure that the actuator attached correctly to the suite
structure.</para>
<para>Make sure that there is no interference between the suite structure
and the actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of the slide alignment.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Repair or replace.</para>
<para>Do a check of the axle at anti-rotation rod end and actuator
s anchoring point are attached correctly.</para>
<para>Do a check of the actuator must be adjusted correctly with the
suite structure to make sure of full movements of the privacy screen.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Mechanical connection faulty.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check of the suite release levers and cables. Repair or
replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Deleted.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Deleted.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Meal table does not deploy or movement is rough.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Rail assembly out of alignment or unserviceable.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Repair or replace table rail assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Latch assembly unserviceable.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Replace the table latch assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="2" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Reversed mating of cable assemblies to the AC Outlet Unit.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="2" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Non-field repairable failure of the In-Seat Power Supply when
power is turned on and a load is applied to the Outlet Unit.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check, when mating the AC Outlet Unit connector to the
In-Seat cable assembly, make sure that the latching mechanism is aligned
before the mating.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Connectors must mate easily and completely until latch mechanism
is engaged.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="left">
<para>Do a check, if connectors are reversed, partial engagement can
be achieved.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="700" seq="806"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-700-806-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Privacy Screen Calibration</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To calibrate the privacy screen after ECU
or actuator replacement.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Seat Calibration:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For seat calibration procedure, refer to
Safran Seats GB Limited, CMM 25-26-61, Business Class Seat, Testing
and Fault Isolation Section.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Privacy Calibration Procedure:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that the suite is connected to
the Electronic Control Unit (ECU).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that the Passenger Control Unit
(PCU) backlight is ON.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>To enter the calibration mode on the PCU,
do the steps as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push and hold the TTL button and the BED
button at the same time on the Main PCU. Hold the buttons until the
Main PCU backlight flashes quickly.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release the TTL button and the BED button.
The Main PCU backlight will stop the quick flash and will pulse slowly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push and hold the TTL button and the BED
button at the same time again within 2 seconds. Hold the buttons until
the Main PCU backlight flashes quickly.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release the TTL button and the BED button.
The Main PCU backlight will stop the quick flash and will pulse slowly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Do a check, make sure that the privacy screen
actuator backlight flashes amber.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>To get access to the manual override switch,
do the steps as follow:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the ball studs to lift the two
top caps (26-240, 26-240A) from the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Get access and use the manual override to
move the privacy screen to the maximum and minimum positions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>To calibrate the privacy screen, do the steps
as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Depress the manual override adjacent to the
privacy screen.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Operate the privacy screen to approximately
12.00 in (304.80 mm) from the top capping.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Operate the privacy screen upward until the
mechanical stop contacts the privacy screen capping.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Hold this position for 2 seconds.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Operate the privacy screen to a position
approximately 12.00 in (304.80 mm) below the top capping.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release the manual override.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Exit from Calibration Mode:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push and hold the TTL button and the BED
button at the same time on the Main PCU. Hold the buttons until the
Main PCU backlight flashes quickly.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release the TTL button and the BED button.
The Main PCU backlight will stop the quick flash and will pulse slowly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push and hold the TTL button and the BED
button at the same time again within 2 seconds. Hold the buttons until
the Main PCU backlight flashes quickly.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release the TTL and Bed buttons. Make sure
that the main PCU backlight stops blinking and turn OFF.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Wait 10 seconds and make sure that the main
PCU backlight turns ON.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Make sure that the privacy screen actuator
backlight flashes green. This shows that the system is out of the
calibration mode.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="2000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-2000" revdate="20261016">
<title>SCHEMATICS AND WIRING DIAGRAMS</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="878" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="2000" chg="r"
key="task-25-26-62-878-801-a-01" revdate="20261016">
<chgdesc>CHANGED SCHEMATICS AND WIRING DIAGRAMS</chgdesc>
<title>General</title>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The schematic and wiring diagrams are detailed
as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Refer to Figure 2001 for the Actuation System
Schematic and Block Diagram.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Refer to Figure 2002 for the Grounding and
Bonding Diagram.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26"
subjnbr="62" func="99B" seq="128" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="2000" chg="u" key="graphic-25-26-62-99b-128-a01"
revdate="20261016">
<title>ACTUATION SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAM</title>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SW-2001-01-00.cgm" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-128-a01-1" revdate="2026020"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SW-2001-02-00.cgm" sheetnbr="2" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-128-a01-2" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SW-2001-03-00.cgm" sheetnbr="3" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-128-a01-3" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SW-2001-04-00.cgm" sheetnbr="4" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-128-a01-4" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<revst>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SW-2001-05-00.cgm" sheetnbr="5" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-128-a01-5" revdate="20261016"></sheet>
<revend>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SW-2001-06-00.cgm" sheetnbr="6" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-128-a01-6" revdate="2026020"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SW-2001-07-00.cgm" sheetnbr="7" chg="u"
