<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="3000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-3000" revdate="20261016">
<title>DISASSEMBLY</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="000" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-000-801-a01" revdate="20260617">
<title>General</title>
<topic>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM
THE ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY approved PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE
INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>DO THE PROCEDURES IN AN ESD AREA. WEAR MANUFACTURER'S
RECOMMENDED WRIST STRAP WHICH IS CONNECTED TO A SOFT GROUND. MAKE
SURE THAT THE WRIST STRAP TOUCHES THE SKIN. OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS
ARE TO BE WORN DURING disassembly. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION
THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>DO NOT push or pull the unit ACROSS FLOOR
SURFACES. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE
TO THE UNIT OR to THE floor SURFACES.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING disassembly,
IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE
UNIT.</para></caution>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do not disassemble the unit more than is
necessary to complete the maintenance task.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Before disassembly record the position of
components and attaching parts to be disassembled. This will help
during assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Examine all removed components and attaching
parts for wear or damage. Replace parts as necessary.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For adjustment procedures and the identification
of damage or function failure refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-26-62-1000"></refint>.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For LRU removal procedures refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-26-62-12000"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do not remove pre-installed Earth Stud assemblies
unless damaged.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The numbers in brackets, for example (125),
refer to an item number in the IPL. The figure of the IPL is given
at the start of each section.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Where the numbers in brackets have a number
before the item, for example (10-125), this refers to an item number
in a different figure in the IPL. For this example, &ldquo;10&rdquo;
refers to the IPL figure and &ldquo;125&rdquo; to the item in that
figure.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="000" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="r"
key="task-25-26-62-000-802-a-01" revdate="20261016">
<chgdesc>CHANGED DISASSEMBLY PROCEDURE</chgdesc>
<title>Disassemble the Unit</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To get access to components for maintenance
procedures.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Tools, Fixtures and Equipment:</para>
<note><para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="vendlist-25-26-62">
vendlist-25-26-62</refint> for vendor addresses.</para></note>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="99A" seq="029"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" id="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"><?Pub Lcl
_tabindent="1">
<title>Tools, Fixtures and Equipment</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="left" charoff="50" char="">
<?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="12.00in"?>
<colspec colname="colspec1">
<colspec colname="col2">
<colspec colname="col4">
<thead valign="bottom">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="middle" align="center">
<para>REFERENCE AND/OR PART NUMBER</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="middle" align="center">
<para>DESCRIPTION AND/OR SPECIFICATION</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="middle" align="center">
<para>SUPPLIER CAGE CODE OR NAME AND ADDRESS</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody valign="top">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="middle">
<para>D8-316-007-969</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="middle">
<para>DZUS Tamper Resistant stud key</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="middle">
<para>VU4447</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Consumables:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do a check of the History or Record Card.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Where used, do a check of the history or
record card to find defective areas which must be looked at.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-001-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the EFR Suite GA (Ref. IPL Fig. 2):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the ETSO assembly (5) from the inboard
and outboard EFR suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to CMM 25-26-61 for the ETSO Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the inboard and outboard EFR furniture
assembly (10) from the inboard and outboard EFR suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 5 IPL for the Inboard and Outboard EFR Furniture
Assembly details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the placard kit assembly (15) from
the inboard and outboard EFR suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 4 IPL for the Placard Kit Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the data plates kit assembly (20)
from the inboard and outboard EFR suite GA.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the data plates kit assembly
(20):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive medium
RFID high memory label (25) from the data plates kit assembly (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive continuation
label (30) from the data plates kit assembly (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive furniture
label (35) from the data plates kit assembly (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove two self-adhesive serial
no and mods labels (40) from the data plates kit assembly (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the loose items kit (45) from the
inboard and outboard EFR suite GA.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-002-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the STD Row Suite GA (Ref. IPL Fig. 3):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the ETSO assembly (5) from the inboard
and outboard STD row suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to CMM 25-26-61 for the ETSO Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the inboard and outboard STD row furniture
assembly (10) from the inboard and outboard STD row suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 6 IPL for the Inboard and Outboard STD Row
Furniture Assembly details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the placard kit assembly (15) from
the inboard and outboard STD row suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 4 IPL for the Placard Kit Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the data plates kit
assembly (20) from the inboard and outboard STD row suite GA.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the data plates kit assembly
(20):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive medium
RFID high memory label (25) from the data plates kit assembly (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive continuation
label (30) from the data plates kit assembly (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive furniture
label (35) from the data plates kit assembly (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove two self-adhesive serial
no and mods labels (40) from the data plates kit assembly (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the loose items kit (45) from the
inboard and outboard STD row suite GA.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-003-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Placard Kit Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 4):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H and 1J:
If necessary, remove the self-adhesive central divider placard (5)
from the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For assembly 1: If necessary, remove the
self-adhesive central divider placard (10) from the placard kit assembly.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive cubby
seal indicator placard (15) from the placard kit assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive door
close and latch placard (20) from the placard kit assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive max
stowage placard (25) from the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B and 1C: If necessary,
remove the self-adhesive fasten seat belt placard (30) from the placard
kit assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive seat
indicator placard (35) from the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: If necessary,
remove the self-adhesive dot panel placard (40) from the placard kit
assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive door
slide placard (45) from the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the self-adhesive door
open placard (50) from the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H,
1J, 1K, 1L, 1M, 1N, 1P and 1Q: If necessary, remove the self-adhesive
furniture indicator placard (55) from the placard kit assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: If necessary, remove the self-adhesive fasten seat
belt placard (60) from the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: If necessary, remove the self-adhesive literature
only placard (65) from the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5792: For assembly 1, 1A, 1B and
1C: If necessary, remove the self-adhesive do not occupy placard (70)
from the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-004-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the EFR Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the EFR electrical installation (5)
from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 7 IPL for the EFR Electrical Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the ottoman cushion
installation (10):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (20,
30) and collect two support brackets (15, 25).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove eight countersunk head screws (40)
and collect two ottoman hinge assemblies (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the ottoman hinge assembly (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the hinge pin (50), retaining ring
(55) and collect the hinge plates (45, 60).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the ottoman support
assembly (65):</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fastener (70) from the
ottoman support assembly (65).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove six countersunk head screws (80, 85)
and collect the bonded part cladding (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect two magnets (90) and the
hinge panel (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the transfer tapes (98)
from the hinge panel (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the ottoman cushion
cover assembly (100):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the ottoman cover (102)
and ottoman foam (104) from the ottoman cushion cover assembly (100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the electrical brackets installation
(105) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 9 IPL for the Electrical Brackets Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the vertical caps installation (110)
from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 26 IPL for the Vertical Caps Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove the privacy screen
assembly (115) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 13 IPL for the Privacy Screen Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove the closeout
panel installation (120) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 14 IPL for the Closeout Panel Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove the outboard
bridge installation (125) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 19 IPL for the Outboard Bridge Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the seat recess claddings installation
(130) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 22 IPL for the Seat Recess Claddings Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the canopy installation (135) from
the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 28 IPL for the Canopy Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the sliding door installation (140)
from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 16 IPL for the Sliding Door Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the upper console stowage installation
(145) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 17 IPL for the Upper Console Stowage Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cocktail table assembly (150)
from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 12 IPL for the Cocktail Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the meal table assembly (155) from
the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 11 IPL for the Meal Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the FWD fascia installation (160)
from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 20 IPL for the FWD Fascia Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove the folding
armrest installation (165) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 18 IPL for the Folding Armrest Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the underseat drip tray assembly (170)
from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 25 IPL for the Underseat Drip Tray Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bed infill installation
(175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (185), two
flat washers (190) and collect the cushion assembly (180).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disassemble the cushion
assembly (180):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><revst><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(195) and collect the cushion (200).</para></prcitem><revend></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove three hexagon
head screws (210), three flat washers (215) and collect the support
bracket assembly (205).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassembly the support bracket assembly
(205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><revst><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(220) and collect the support bracket (225).</para></prcitem><revend>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the lifevest box assembly (230) from
the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 21 IPL for the Lifevest Box Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the N-aisle claddings installation
(235) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 24 IPL for the N-aisle Claddings Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove the dot door
installation (240) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 15 IPL for the Dot Door Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove and disassemble
the bump strip installation (245):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove five hexagon head screws (255), five
flat washers (260) and collect the IUL-DND-TTL bracket assembly (250).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the IUL-DND-TTL bracket assembly
(250):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bumper electrical
assembly (265):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the IUL (270) and TTL
indicator (275).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (285), two
flat washers (290) and collect the bumper (280).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (300), two
flat washers (305) and collect the clip (295).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the kickstrip and seals cladding installation
(310) from the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 23 IPL for the Kickstrip and Seals Cladding
Installation details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the foot fitting kit
installation (315):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (325), two
spreaders (330) and collect two foot fitting spacers (320).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two screws (335) from the foot fitting
kit installation (315).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (345), two
nuts (350), four flat washers (355) and collect the rear RH foot fitting
(340).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (365), two nuts (370), four flat washers (375), two bearing
bushes (380) and collect the EQ foot fitting assembly (360).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ foot fitting assembly
(360):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tape (385) from
the EQ foot fitting assembly (360).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove two hexagonal
head screws (395), two nuts (400), four flat washers (405), two bearing
bushes (410) and collect the EQ foot fitting assembly (390).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ foot fitting assembly
(390):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tape (415) from
the EQ foot fitting assembly (390).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (425), two
bushes (430) and collect two equipped spacer assemblies (420).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Dissemble the equipped spacer assemblies
(420):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tapes (435) from
the equipped spacer assemblies (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two screws (440) from the foot fitting
kit installation (315).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (450), two
nuts (455), four flat washers (460) and collect the EQ foot fitting
assembly (445).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ foot fitting assembly
(445):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tape (465) from
the EQ foot fitting assembly (445).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (475), two nuts (480), four flat washers (485), two bearing
bushes (490) and collect the EQ foot fitting assembly (470).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ foot fitting assembly
(470):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tape (495) from
the EQ foot fitting assembly (470).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove two hexagon
head screws (505), two nuts (510), four flat washers (515), two bearing
bushes (520) and collect the EQ foot fitting assembly (500).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disassemble the EQ
foot fitting assembly (500):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tape (525) from
the EQ foot fitting assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the transition track fitting
(530) and e-nut fitting bolt (535).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the composite integration (540) from
the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 27 IPL for the Composite Integration details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-005-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the STD Row Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the STD row electrical installation
(5) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 8 IPL for the STD Row Electrical Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R and 1S: Remove and disassemble the ottoman
cushion installation (10):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (20,
30) and collect two support brackets (15, 25).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove eight countersunk head screws (40)
and collect two ottoman hinge assemblies (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the ottoman hinge assembly (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the hinge pin (50), retaining ring
(55) and collect the hinge plates (45, 60).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the ottoman support
assembly (65):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fasteners (70) from the
ottoman support assembly (65).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove six countersunk head screws (80, 85)
and collect the bonded part cladding (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect two magnets (90) and the
hinge panel (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the transfer tapes (98)
from the hinge panel (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the ottoman cushion
cover assembly (100):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the ottoman cover (102)
and ottoman foam (104) from the ottoman cushion cover assembly (100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the electrical brackets installation
(105) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 10 IPL for the Electrical Brackets Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the vertical caps installation (110)
from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 26 IPL for the Vertical Caps Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A and 1B: Remove the privacy
screen installation (115) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 13 IPL for the Privacy Screen Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E and 1F:
Remove the closeout panel installation (120) from the STD row furniture
assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 14 IPL for the Closeout Panel Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L, 1M, 1N,
1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Remove the outboard bridge installation (125)
from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 19 IPL for the Outboard Bridge Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the seat recess claddings installation
(130) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 22 IPL for Seat Recess Claddings Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the canopy installation (135) from
the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 28 IPL for the Canopy Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the sliding door installation (140)
from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 16 IPL for the Sliding Door Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the upper console stowage installation
(145) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 17 IPL for the Upper Console Stowage Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cocktail table assembly (150)
from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 12 IPL for the Cocktail Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R and 1S: Remove the meal table assembly (155)
from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 11 IPL for the Meal Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R and 1S: Remove the FWD fascia installation
(160) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 20 IPL for the FWD Fascia Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Remove the folding armrest installation
(165) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 18 IPL for the Folding Armrest Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the under seat drip tray assembly
(170) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 25 IPL for the Under Seat Drip Tray assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bed infill installation
(175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Remove and collect the cushion assembly
(180).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1E and 1F: Remove two
hexagon head screws (185), two flat washers (190) and collect the
cushion assembly (180).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cushion assembly (180):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Disengage the self-adhesive duotec
fasteners (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the cushion (200).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Remove five hexagon head screws (210),
five flat washers (215) and collect the support bracket assembly (205).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(220) and collect the support bracket (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the N-aisle cladding installation
(230) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 24 IPL for the N-aisle Cladding Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1E: Remove the dot door
installation (235) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 15 IPL for the Dot Door Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Remove and disassemble the
bump strip installation (240):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon head screws (250), three
flat washers (255) and collect the IUL-DND-TTL bracket assembly (245).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the IUL-DND-TTL bracket assembly
(250):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bumper electrical
assembly (260).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the IUL (265) and the
TTL indicator (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1K, 1L, 1M, 1R, 1S
and 1T: Remove four hexagon head screws (280, 285), four flat washers
(290, 295) and collect the bumper (275).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1N, 1P and
1Q: Remove two hexagon head screws (285), two flat washers (295) and
collect the bumper (275).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1K, 1L, 1M, 1R, 1S
and 1T: Remove two hexagon head screws (305), two flat washers (310)
and collect the clip (300).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1N, 1P and
1Q: Remove six hexagon head screws (305), six flat washers (310) and
collect three clips (300).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the kickstrip and seals cladding installation
(315) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 23 IPL for the Kickstrip and Seals Cladding
Installation details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1F, 1M and 1T: Remove the
rear row closeout assembly (320) from the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 29 IPL for the Rear Row Closeout Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5745: For Assembly 1G, 1H, 1J,
1N, 1P and 1Q: Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fastener (321) from
the STD row furniture assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5745: For Assembly 1G, 1H, 1J,
1N, 1P and 1Q: Remove and disassemble the cover assembly (322) from
the STD row furniture assembly:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(323) and collect the cover bracket (324) from the cover assembly
(322).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1N, 1P and 1Q: Remove and disassemble the closeout pad installation
(325):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two or five countersunk head screws
(335) and collect the bracket assembly (330).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (330):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(345) and collect the bracket (340).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the cushion assembly
(350):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(360) and collect the support (355).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fastener (365) from the
cushion assembly (350).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the foot fitting kit
installation (370):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (380), one
spreader (385) and collect each of two foot fitting spacer (375).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two screws (390) from the foot fitting
kit installation (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (400), two
nuts (405), four flat washers (410) and collect the front foot fittings
(395).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (420), two
nuts (425), four flat washers (430), two bearing bushes (435) and
collect the EQ foot fitting assembly (415).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ foot fitting assembly
(415):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tape (440) from
the EQ foot fitting assembly (415).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (420), two
nuts (425), four flat washers (430), two bearing bushes (435) and
collect the EQ foot fitting assembly (390).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (450), one
bearing bush (455) and collect each of two spacers (445).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two screws (460) from the foot fitting
kit installation (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the spacer (445):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tape (465) from
the spacer (445).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (475), two
nuts (480), four flat washers (485), two bearing bushes (490) and
collect the EQ foot fitting assembly (470).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ foot fitting assembly
(470):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tapes (495) from
the EQ foot fitting assembly (470).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (505), two
nuts (510), four flat washers (515) and collect the EQ foot fitting
assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ foot fitting assembly
(500):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive tape (520) from
the EQ foot fitting assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the transition track fitting
(525) and the e-nut fitting bolt (530).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the composite integration (535) from
the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 27 IPL for the Composite Integration details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-006-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Suite EFR Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL
Fig. 7):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Cut the tie wraps (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove three socket head screws (15), disconnect
and collect the reading light (10) at connector P30.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one socket head screw (25), one hexagon
nut (30), disconnect and collect the hall effect sensor (20) at connector
P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (40), two flat
washers (45), disconnect and collect the main PCU (35) at connector
J1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Disconnect the cable LRU
interface (31) at connector P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cable protection (50) from the
EFR Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Remove the cable
protection (55) from the EFR Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect and collect the harness assembly
(60) at connectors J5, J3, P100, P2, P3, P4, D03P and P1 from the
EFR Electrical Installation Suite.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect four RGBW lights (70,
75, 80, 85) and two mood lights (90, 95) at each connector P1.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cable protections (100, 105) from
the Suite EFR Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disconnect the harness
assembly (110) at connectors J12 and P11.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (120),
two flat washers (125) and disconnect the harness assembly (115) at
connectors D15J, J8, J9, J10, J11 and P3.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (135),
two flat washers (140) and disconnect the harness assembly (130) at
connectors J6, D16J and J4.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (150)
and collect the euphony microphone (145) at connector P1A6.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the euphony harness (155) at connectors
P1A5, P4 and P1A2.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect three fixing bases (160).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the next premium handset
(165).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the next premium cradle
(170) at connector J2.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the IFE harness (175) at connectors
P5B and P11.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the smart audio adapter
(220), remote jack (225), outlet unit (230) and next triple pin audio
RJM (235) at connectors J1, J2, J1, P7, P14 and P1.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the conduct (240) and disconnect the
IFE harness assembly (245) at connectors P1 and P12.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the IFE harness (250) at connectors
P13, P1 and P10.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cable protection (255) from the
Suite EFR Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (265)
and disconnect the IFE harness (260) at connectors P4B and J10.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four socket head screws (275) and
collect the monitor (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the peripheral bar (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (290)
and disconnect the IFE harness (285) at connectors J10 and P10.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the lighting controller
box (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one nut (305), one washer (310) and
disconnect the bonding assembly (300) at connector GD06.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (320),
two flat washers (325) and disconnect the harness assembly (315) at
connectors D14J and D15P.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (335)
and disconnect the IFE harness (330) at connectors P7-1, P14, P7,
P3 and J10.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove twelve or ten nuts (345), twelve or
ten flat washers (350) and disconnect the bonding assemblies (340)
at connectors GD03B, GD07A, GD15, GD03C, GD08, GD07A, GD01B, GD01A,
GD03A, GD13, GD19, GD05, GD16, GD07B and GD09.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the bonding assembly (355) at
connectors GD01B, GD06 and P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two nuts (365), two flat washers (370)
and disconnect three bonding assemblies (360) at connectors GD05,
GD02 and J1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the nuts (380), the washers (385)
and disconnect the bonding assemblies (375) at connectors GD04, GD05,
GD10, GD11A, GD14A, GD03A, GD08, GD14B and GD03C.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two nuts (395), two flat washers (400)
and disconnect two or one bonding assemblies (390) at connectors GD10,
GD03, GD10 and GD03B.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect three bonding assemblies (405,
410) at connectors GD04, GD03, GD02 and GD17.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two or three nuts (420), two or three
flat washers (425) and disconnect two bonding assemblies (415) at
connectors GD02, GD03, GD03A, GD03B, GD13 and GD18.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect two bonding assemblies (430, 435)
at connectors GD03A, GS-1, GD03A, GD18, GD10 and GD11B.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two or three countersunk head screws
(445) and collect two or three tie bases (440).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the cover assemblies
(450, 465):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(455, 470) from the cover assemblies (450, 465).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the covers (456, 471) from the cover
assemblies (450, 465).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the harness assemblies (480, 485,
490, 505) at connectors S01, D10J, P2, J1, P800, D10P, P10, P1S, P1,
P8, P2, P1 and P21.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For assembly 1 and 1A: Remove the conduct
(491) and disconnect the harness assembly (495) at connectors P10,
P1S, P1 and P8.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove two countersunk head
screws (501), two flat washers (502) and disconnect the harness assembly
(500B) at connector J15, P200, P204 and J1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two dust caps (510), one flight cap
(515) and collect the next premium expansion unit (520).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two protective covers (550) and collect
the ISPS (555).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove eight countersunk
head screws (565) and disconnect the IFE harness (560) at connectors
P2, P1, J1A, J2A and P1G.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove four countersunk
head screws (575) and disconnect the IFE harness (570) at connectors
P6B and J6B.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove four countersunk
head screws (577) and disconnect the IFE harness (576) at connectors
P4A and J10.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two dust caps (580) and collect the
seat box (585).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (670), one
flat washer (675) and collect one cable clamp (665).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (685), one
flat washer (690) and collect one cable clamp (665) with one spacer
(695).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (705), two
flat washers (710) and collect two cable clamps (700) with two cable
clamps (715).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (725), one
flat washer (730) and collect one cable clamp (720) with one spacer
(735).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove one hexagon head screw
(745), one flat washer (750) and collect one cable clamp (740) with
one spacer (755).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove four hexagon
head screws (765), four flat washers (770) and collect four cable
clamps (760).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (780), two
flat washers (785) and collect two cable clamps (775) with one spacer
(790).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A and 1C: Remove two or
three hexagon head screws (800), two or three flat washers (805) and
collect two or three cable clamps (795) with one spacer (810).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B: Remove one hexagon head
screw (820), one flat washer (825), one spacer (830) and collect one
cable clamp (815) with three cable clamps (835).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one or two hexagon head screws (845),
one or two flat washers (850) and collect one or two cable clamps
(840).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove one hexagon
head screw (860), one flat washer (865) and collect two cable clamps
(855).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-007-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Suite STD Row Electrical Installation (Ref.
IPL Fig. 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Cut the tie wraps (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove three socket head screws (15) and
collect the reading light (10) at connector P30.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one socket head screw (25), one hexagon
nut (30) and collect the hall effect sensor (20) at connector P1</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1B: Disconnect the cable
LRU interface (35) at connector P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (45), two flat
washers (50) and collect the main PCU (40) at connector J1.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cable protection (55) from the
suite STD electrical installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M and 1N: Remove the cable protection (60) from the suite STD
electrical installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (70),
two flat washers (75) and disconnect the harness assembly (65) at
connectors J5, J3, D23, P204, P1, J17, J15, J18, D03P, D039, P100,
P2, P3, P4, J1, J2 and J100A.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect four RGBW lights (80,
85, 90, 95) and two mood lights (100, 105) at connector P1.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cable protections (110, 115) from
the suite STD electrical installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1H, 1J, 1M and 1N:
Disconnect the harness assembly (120) at connectors J12 and P11.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1J, 1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Remove two countersunk head screws (130), two
flat washers (135) and disconnect the harness assembly (125) at connectors
D15J, J9, J11, J8, J10 and P3.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (145),
two flat washers (150) and disconnect the harness assembly (140) at
connectors J6, D16J and J4.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (160)
and collect the euphony microphone (155) at connector P1A6.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the euphony harness (165) at connectors
P1A5, P4 and P1A2.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the fixing base (170).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove five hexagon head screws (175, 180,
185), five flat washers (190) and collect seven cable clamps (195,
200) with one or two spacers (205).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the smart audio adapter
(210), the remote jack (215), the outlet pin (220) and the next triple
pin audio RJM (225) at connectors J1, J2, P1, P7 and P14.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the conducts (230) and disconnect
the harness assembly (235) at connectors P1 and P2.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the IFE harness (240) at connectors
P13, P1 and P10.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cable protections (245) from the
suite STD electrical installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (255)
and disconnect the IFE harness (250) at connectors P4B and J10.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M and 1N: Remove four socket head screws (265) and collect the
monitor (260).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M and 1N: Remove and collect the peripheral bar (270).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M and 1N: Remove four countersunk head screws (280) and disconnect
the IFE harness (275) at connectors J10 and P10.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the controller box (285).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one nut (295), one washer (300) and
disconnect the bonding assembly (290) at connector GD06.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Remove two countersunk head screws (310), two flat
washers (315) and disconnect the harness assembly (305) at connectors
D14J and D15P.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk screws (325) and disconnect
the IFE harness (320) at connectors P7-1, P14, P7, P3 and J10.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the nuts (335), flat washers (340)
and disconnect the bonding assembly (330) at connectors GD03B, GD07A,
GD06, GD03C, GD08, GD7A, GD01B, GD05, GD16, GD07B, GD09, GD01A, GD03A,
GD13, GD19 and GD15.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the bonding assembly (345) at
connectors GD1B, GD06 and P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the nuts (355), flat washers (360)
and disconnect the bonding assemblies (350) at connectors GD05, GD02,
GD03C and J1</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the nuts (370), flat washers (375)
and disconnect the bonding assemblies (365) at connectors GD04, GD05,
GD11A, GD14A, GD03A, GD08, GD14B, GD03C, GD10, GD11B, GD14, GD03C,
E1 and ECCB GND.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1L, 1M,
1N and 1P: Remove two nuts (385), two flat washers (390) and disconnect
the bonding assembly (380) at connectors GD10, GD03, GD05 and GD17.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Disconnect the bonding assemblies (395) at
connectors GD04 and GD03B.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the bonding assemblies (400) at
connectors GD02 and GD17.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one or two nuts (410), one or two
flat washers (415) and disconnect one or two bonding assembly (405)
at connectors GD02, GD03A, GD03B and GD13.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the bonding assemblies (420) at
connectors GD03A, GD03B, GS-1, GD11A, GD02 and GD18.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N and 1P: Disconnect the bonding assemblies (425) at connectors
GD03A and GD18.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Remove and collect the tie bases (430).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (440)
and collect two tie bases (435).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the cover assemblies
(445, 460):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(450, 465) from the cover assemblies (445, 460).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the covers (446, 461) from the cover
assemblies (445, 460).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the harness assemblies (475, 480,
485, 490, 495, 500, 505) at connectors S01, D10J, P2, J1, P800, D10P,
P10, P1S, P1, P8, P200, P204, J13, P2, P1, P21, D24J, P101, P201 and
P100A.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two dust caps (510) and one flight
cap (515) and collect the next premium expansion unit (520).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (525), one
flat washer (530) and collect two clamps (535) with one spacer (540).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the IFE harness (545) at connectors
P3, P2 and P20.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two protective covers (550) and collect
the ISPS (555).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1D, 1J and 1N: Remove eight
countersunk head screws (565) and disconnect the IFE harness (560)
at connectors P2, P1, J1A, J2A and P1G.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1M, 1N
and 1P: Remove four countersunk head screws (575) and disconnect the
IFE harness (570) at connectors P4A and J10.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six dust caps (576, 577, 580) and
collect the seat box (585).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (590), one
flat washer (595) and collect the clamps (605) with spacers (610).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (620), one
flat washer (625) and collect the clamps (615).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (635) and
collect the tie base (630).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (645), two
flat washers (650) and collect the cable clamps (640).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1G and 1L: Remove the
hexagon head screws (660, 665) and flat washers (670) and collect
the cable clamps (655) with spacers (680).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1G and 1L: Remove two hexagon
head screws (690), two flat washers (695) and collect two cable clamps
(685).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-008-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Suite EFR Electrical Brackets Installation
(Ref. IPL Fig. 9):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (10), two self-locking nuts (15), four flat washers (20)
and collect the reading light sup bracket assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the reading light sup bracket
assembly (5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><revst><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(25) from the reading light bracket (40).</para></prcitem><revend>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tape (30) from the
reading light bracket (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the reading light bracket (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove two hexagon head screws
(50), two flat washers (55) and collect the support bracket (45).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove one countersunk
head screw (65), one spacer (66) and collect the cable tie (60).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend><revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove one hexagon
head screw (75), one flat washer (80), one spacer (81) and collect
the reading light bracket assembly (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the reading light bracket assembly
(70):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(86) from the reading light bracket assembly (70).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the reading light bracket (90) from
the reading light bracket assembly (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (100), two
flat washers (105) and collect the support bracket (95).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (115), two
flat washers (120) and collect the support bracket (110).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (130), two
flat washers (135) and collect the disconnect bracket (125).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket (125):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (145), one
flat washer (150) and collect the cable clamp (140) from the disconnect
bracket (185).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (160), one
flat washer (165) and collect the cable clamp (155) from the disconnect
bracket (185).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (175)
from the disconnect bracket (185).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fastener (180) from the
disconnect bracket (185).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (185).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (195), one
flat washer (200) and collect the cable clamp (190).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the support box plate
assembly (205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (210)
from the support box plate (220).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release two quarter turn screws (225), two quarter turn retainers
(230) and collect the box support plate (220).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (240), four
flat washers (245) and collect the support bracket assembly (235).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(235):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (255), one
flat washer (260) and collect the connector support (250).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Drill out ten pop rivets (270) and collect
the disconnect bracket assembly (265).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the disconnect bracket
assembly (265):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (280), four
flat washers (285) and collect four cable clamps (275) from the disconnect
bracket (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (290)
from the disconnect bracket (310).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Drill out four pop rivets (305) and collect
two quarter turn receptacles (300) from the disconnect bracket (310).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (310).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the disconnect bracket
assembly (315):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(320) from the disconnect bracket (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (330).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (340), two flat washers (345) and collect the support
bracket assembly (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(335):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (355), one
flat washer (360) and collect the cable clamp (350) from the support
bracket (365).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the support bracket (365).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (375), two flat washers (380) and collect the disconnect
bracket assembly (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(370):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (390), one
flat washer (395) and collect the cable clamp (385) from the disconnect
bracket (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (405)
from the disconnect bracket (410).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (410).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (420), one
flat washer (425) and collect the cable clamp (415).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (435), two
flat washers (440), two nylon spacers (445) and collect the disconnect
bracket assembly (430).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(430):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two or one hexagon head screws (455),
two or one flat washers (460) and collect four or two cable clamps
(450) from the disconnect bracket (565).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two or one hexagon head screws (470),
two or one flat washers (475), two or one spacers (480) and collect
six or three cable clamps (465) from the disconnect bracket (565).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove one hexagon
head screw (490), one flat washer (495), one spacer (500) and collect
four cable clamps (485) from the disconnect bracket (565).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1D: Remove one hexagon
head screw (510), one flat washer (515), one spacer (520) and collect
four cable clamps (505) from the disconnect bracket (565).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1D: Remove one hexagon
head screw (530), one flat washer (535) and collect the cable clamp
(525) from the disconnect bracket (565).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three earth/ground stud assemblies
(540) from the disconnect bracket (565).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (555), two flat washers (560) and collect the support
bracket (550) from the disconnect bracket (565).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (565).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (575), two
flat washers (580) and collect the disconnect bracket assembly (570).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(570):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (585)
from the disconnect bracket (590).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (590).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the support bracket assembly (595)
from the electrical bracket installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (605, 610),
six flat washers (615) and collect the next HPS box assembly (600).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the next HPS box assembly (600):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the HPS box assembly
(620):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (625)
from the HPS bracket (630).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two nylatch plungers (635), two nylatch
grommets (640) and collect the HPS bracket (630).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Drill out eight pop rivets (650) and collect
four quarter turn fasteners (645) from the HPS bracket (630).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the HPS bracket assembly
(655):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (660)
from the HPS bracket (665).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the HPS bracket (665).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the support bracket (670) from the
electrical bracket installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the support plate
equipped assembly (675):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (680)
from the Panasonic next plate (700).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Drill out eight pop rivets (695) and collect
four quarter turn receptacle fasteners (690) from the Panasonic next
plate (700).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four nylatch plungers (705), four
nylatch grommets (710) and collect the Panasonic next plate (700).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (720), two
flat washers (725) and collect the electrical bracket assembly (715).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the electrical bracket
assembly (715):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (730)
from the structure electrical bracket (735).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the structure electrical bracket
(735).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove five hexagon
head screws (745, 750), five flat washers (755) and collect the harness
support bracket assembly (740).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove and
disassemble the harness support bracket assembly (740):</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Drill out four pop rivets (765) and collect
the disconnect bracket assembly (760).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(760):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (770)
from the disconnect bracket assembly (760).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove and disassemble the support
bracket assembly (775):</para><revend></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon head screws (785), three
flat washers (790) and collect three cable clamps (780).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (795)
from the support bracket (800).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the support bracket (800).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove the support
bracket (805) from the electrical bracket installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two or one hexagon head screws (815),
two or one flat washers (820) and collect the electrical bracket assembly
(810).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the electrical bracket assembly
(810):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two earth/ground stud assemblies (825)
from the structure electrical bracket (830).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the structure electrical bracket
(830).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (840), two
flat washers (845) and collect the switch bracket assembly (835).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the switch bracket assembly (835):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the switch bracket (855)
from the switch bracket assembly (835).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend></prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (865), four
flat washers (870) and collect the ISPS bracket assembly (860).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the ISPS bracket assembly (860):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (875)
from the ISPS bracket (880).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the ISPS bracket (880).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (890), two flat washers (895) and collect the harness
support bracket assembly (885).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the harness support bracket assembly
(885):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (910), two
flat washers (905) and collect two cable clamps (900) from the harness
support bracket (920).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two earth/ground stud assemblies (915)
from the harness support bracket (920).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the harness support bracket (920).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove two hexagon
head screws (930), two flat washers (935) and collect the disconnect
bracket (925).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket (925):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two earth/ground stud assembly (940)
from the disconnect bracket (945).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (945).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove the bracket
(950) from the electrical bracket installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (960), two
flat washers (965) and collect the TPCU disconnect bracket (955).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-009-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Suite STD Row Electrical Brackets Installation
(Ref. IPL Fig. 10):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1M, 1N
and 1P: Remove one countersunk head screw (10) and collect the cable
tie (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1M, 1N
and 1P: Remove one hexagon head screw (20), one flat washer (25) and
collect the reading light bracket assembly (15).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Remove two hexagon
head screws (40), two self-locking nuts (45) four flat washers (50)
and collect the reading light sup bracket assembly (35).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the reading light sup bracket
assembly (35):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(55) from the reading light bracket detail (70).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tape (60) from the
reading light bracket detail (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the reading light bracket detail
(70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove two hexagon head
screws (80), two flat washers (85) and collect the support bracket
assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1K and 1L: Remove two
hexagon head screws (95), two flat washers (100) and collect the reading
light bracket assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the reading light bracket assembly
(90):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(105) from the reading light bracket (115).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the reading light bracket (115).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (125), two
flat washers (130) and collect the support bracket (120).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove two hexagon head screws
(140), two flat washers (145) and collect the support bracket (135).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (155), two
flat washers (160) and collect the support bracket (150).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (170), two
flat washers (175) and collect the disconnect bracket assembly (165).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the disconnect bracket
assembly (165):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (185), one
flat washer (190) and collect the cable clamp (180) from the disconnect
bracket (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (200), one
flat washer (205) and collect the cable clamp (195) from the disconnect
bracket (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (215)
from the disconnect bracket (225).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (220) from the disconnect
bracket (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (225).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the support box plate
assembly (230).</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (235)
from the box support plate (245).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release two quarter turn studs (250), two quarter turn retainers (255)
and collect the box support plate (245).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (265), one
flat washer (270) and collect the cable clamp (260).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (280), four
flat washers (285) and collect the support bracket assembly (275).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the support bracket
assembly (275):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (295), one
flat washer (300) and collect the connector support (290).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Drill out ten pop rivets (310) and collect
the disconnect bracket assembly (305).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(305):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (320), four
flat washers (325) and collect four cable clamps (315) from the disconnect
bracket (350).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (330)
from the disconnect bracket (350).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four pop rivets (345) and collect
two quarter turn receptables (340) from the disconnect bracket (350).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (350).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the disconnect bracket
assembly (355):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(360) from the disconnect bracket (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (370).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Remove two hexagon
head screws (380), two flat washers (385) and collect the support
bracket assembly (375).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(375):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (395), one
flat washer (400) and collect the cable clamp (390) from the support
bracket (405).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the support bracket (405).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Remove two hexagon
head screws (415), two flat washers (420) and collect the disconnect
bracket assembly (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(410):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (430), one
flat washer (435) and collect the cable clamp (425) from the disconnect
bracket (450).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (445)
from the disconnect bracket (450).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (450).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1K and 1L: Remove two
hexagon head screws (460), two flat washers (465) and collect the
disconnect bracket assembly (455).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(455):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (475) and
collect the cable mount tie (470) from the disconnect bracket (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (480)
from the disconnect bracket (485).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (495), one
flat washer (500) and collect the cable clamp (490).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (510), two
flat washers (515), two spacers (520) and collect the disconnect bracket
assembly (505).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(505):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1M, 1N and 1P: Remove two hexagon head screws (530, 531), two flat
washers (535), two or one spacers (540) and collect the eight or four
clamps (525) from the disconnect bracket (640).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1M, 1N and 1P: Remove three or one hexagon head screws (550), three
or one flat washers (555) and collect six or two clamps (545) from
the disconnect bracket (640).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Remove four or one hexagon head screws (565),
four or one flat washers (570), four or one spacers (575) and collect
twelve or three clamps (560) from the disconnect bracket (640).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1K and 1L: Remove one
hexagon head screw (585), one flat washer (590), one spacer (595)
and collect two clamps (580) from the disconnect bracket (640).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Remove one hexagon head screw (605), one flat
washer (610) and collect the cable clamp (600) from the disconnect
bracket (640).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Remove two hexagon
head screws (620), two flat washers (625) and collect the support
bracket (615) from the disconnect bracket (640).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three earth/ground stud assembly (630)
from the disconnect bracket (640).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (640).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="032"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-032-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Suite STD Row Electrical Brackets Installation
(Ref. IPL Fig. 10A):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (10), two
flat washers (15) and collect the disconnect bracket assembly (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (20)
from the disconnect bracket (25).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the disconnect bracket (25).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the support bracket (30).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (40, 45),
six flat washers (50) and collect the next HPS box assembly (35).</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the next HPS box assembly (35):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the HPS box assembly
(55):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (60)
from the HPS bracket (65).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two nylatch plungers (70), two nylatch
grommets (75) and collect the HPS bracket (65).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Drill out eight pop rivets (85) and collect
four quarter turn fasteners (80).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the HPS box assembly
(90).</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (95)
from the HPS bracket (100).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the HPS bracket (100).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect two support brackets (105).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the support plate
equipped assembly (110):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (115)
from the Panasonic next plate (135).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Drill out eight pop rivets (130) and collect
four quarter turn fasteners (125).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four nylatch plungers (140), four
nylatch grommets (145) and collect the Panasonic next plate (135).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (155), two
flat washers (160) and collect the electrical bracket assembly (150).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the electrical bracket assembly
(150):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (165)
from the electrical structure bracket (170).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the electrical structure bracket
(170).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1M and 1N:
Remove five hexagon head screws (180, 185), five flat washers (190)
and collect the harness support bracket assembly (175).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the harness support bracket assembly
(175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Drill out six or four pop rivets (200) and
collect the disconnect bracket assembly (195).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(195):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (205)
from the disconnect bracket assembly (195).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Figure 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the support bracket
assembly (210).</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (215)
from the support bracket (235).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon head screws (225), three
flat washers (230) and collect three cable clamps (220) from the support
bracket (235).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the support bracket (235).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1M and 1N:
Remove and collect the support bracket (240).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two or one hexagon head screws (250),
two or one flat washers (255) and collect the electrical bracket assembly
(245).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the electrical bracket assembly
(245):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (260)
from the electrical bracket structure (265).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the structure electrical bracket
(265).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (275), two
flat washers (280) and collect the switch bracket assembly (270).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the switch bracket assembly (270):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the switch bracket (290) from the
switch bracket assembly (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Remove one hexagon
head screw (300), one flat washer (305) and collect the support bracket
assembly (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(295):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (315), one
flat washer (320) and collect the cable clamp (310) from the support
bracket (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the support bracket (325).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Remove one hexagon
head screw (335), one flat washer (340) and collect the cable clamp
(330).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1K
and 1L: Remove one hexagon head screw (350), one flat washer (355)
and collect the harness support bracket assembly (345).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the harness support bracket assembly
(345):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (365), two
flat washers (370) and collect two cable clamps (360) from the harness
support bracket (380).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (375)
from the harness support bracket (380).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the harness support bracket (380).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (390), four
flat washers (395) and collect the ISPS bracket assembly (385).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the ISPS bracket assembly (385):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (400)
from the ISPS bracket (405).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the ISPS bracket (405).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Remove two hexagon
head screws (415), two flat washers (420) and collect the sub bracket
assembly (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the sub bracket assembly (410):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (425)
from the sub bracket assembly (410).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (435), two
flat washers (440) and collect the disconnect TPCU bracket (430).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1G, 1H, 1J, 1M, 1N and 1P: Remove
two hexagon head screws (450), two flat washers (455) and collect
the disconnect bracket assembly (445).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(445):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (460)
from the disconnect bracket assembly (445).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Figure 30 Parts List for Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1J and 1P: Remove four hexagon
head screws (475), four flat washers (480) and collect the bracket
assembly (470).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(470):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two earth/ground stud assembly (485)
from the bracket assembly (470).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Figure 30 Parts List for Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C: Remove three hexagon head
screws (495), three flat washers (500) and collect the bracket assembly
(490).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(490):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bracket assembly
(505):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one earth/ground stud assembly (510)
from the support bracket (530).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (520), four
flat washers (525) and collect the clamp cable (515).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four covers (545, 550), two hexagon
head screws (540) and collect two cable clamps (535).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the support bracket (530).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-001-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Meal Table Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 11) from
the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the meal table installation
(5-155, 6-155).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the meal table installation (5-155,
6-155) from the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 11 IPL for the Meal Table Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-010-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Meal Table Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 11):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove seven countersunk head screws (10,
15), three socket head screws (20), three flat washers (25) and collect
the meal table assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the meal table assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon head screws (35), three
flat washers (40) and collect the block latch assembly (30).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the block latch assembly (30):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (50) and
collect the retaining plate (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (60) and
collect the touch latch (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><revst><prcitem><para>Remove the plunger (65), bearing (66),
spring (70) and collect the block latch (75).</para></prcitem><revend>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove twenty socket head screws (85) and
collect the base plate assembly (80).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the base plate assembly (80):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (95) and
collect the bracket (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (105)
and collect two rear supports (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (115),
four compression springs (120) and collect two friction pads (125)
with two guide cam followers (110).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove five countersunk head screws (135)
and collect the block cam follower (130) with the base plate (140)
and stop pad (136).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove twenty socket head screws (150) and
collect the arm lower assembly (145).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the arm lower assembly (145):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one special head screw (160), one
flat washer (165) and collect the arm latch assembly (155).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disassemble the arm latch assembly (155):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two cam followers (175), two flat
washers (180), one bolt (185) and collect the arm latch (170).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one spring (190) and one bolt (195)
from the arm latch assembly (155).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (205)
and collect two pad retainers (200).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect two springs (210) and
two friction pads (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect four carriages (220, 225).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY IS REMOVED, MAKE SURE THAT
THE SLIDES DO NOT DISCONNECT FROM THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY RAIL. IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE SLIDES AND RAIL WILL OCCUR.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove twenty-two socket head screws (235) and collect two rails
(230).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (245)
and collect the block latch (240).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect two bonded part covers
(250), one bonded part friction pad (255) and five stop pads (256).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the lower arm (260).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (270)
and collect the meal table handle (265).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (280)
and collect the arm leaf support (275).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part arm leaf support pad
(285) from the arm leaf support (275).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove ten socket head screws (295), one
hexagon nut (300), one flat washer (305) and collect the middle arm
assembly (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the middle arm assembly (290):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove three countersunk head screws (315)
and collect the cover plate (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one special head screw (325), one
flat washer (330) and collect the front arm latch assembly (320).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disassemble the front arm latch assembly
(320):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two cam followers (340), two flat
washers (345), bolt (350) and collect the front arm latch (335).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the stop pad (351).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bolt (360), spring
(355) from the middle arm assembly (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect six carriages (365, 370).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY IS REMOVED, MAKE SURE THAT
THE SLIDES DO NOT DISCONNECT FROM THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY RAIL. IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE SLIDES AND RAIL WILL OCCUR.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove eighteen socket head screws (380) and collect two rails
(375).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY IS REMOVED, MAKE SURE THAT
THE SLIDES DO NOT DISCONNECT FROM THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY RAIL. IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE SLIDES AND RAIL WILL OCCUR.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove nine socket head screws (390) and collect the rail (385).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the spring plunger (395)
and middle arm (400).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect six stop pads (401, 402).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove eight socket head screws (410) and
collect the arm leaf mounting assembly (405).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the arm leaf mounting assembly
(405):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (420)
and collect the pad retainer (415).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect two compression springs
(425) and one pad friction (430).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect two bonded part support
leafs (435).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the arm leaf (440).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the film (445) and transfer tapes
(450) from the meal table assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the leaf table assembly
(455):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove eight countersunk head screws (465)
and collect the guide cam follower (460).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (475)
and collect the end guide cam follower (470).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the V-Groove track (480).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove twelve pan head screws (490), twelve
flat washers (495) and collect the tray table cover (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove eight countersunk head screws (505)
and collect the bearing (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the leaf table (510).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bonded part stopper
(515).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-002-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Cocktail Table Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 12) from
the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the cocktail table assembly
(5-150, 6-150).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the cocktail table assembly (5-150,
6-150) from the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 12 IPL for the Cocktail Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="030"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-030-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Cocktail Table Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 12):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (10), two flat
washers (15) and collect the footwell panel assembly (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the footwell panel assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon self-locking nuts (25),
three flat washers (30) and collect the bracket assembly (20) from
the trim panel assembly (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagonal head screws (45, 50)
and three flat washers (55) from the armrest assembly (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the placard indicator
backrest (58) from the armrest assembly (40).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the armrest assembly (40):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the bonded part armrest
foam (60) from the armrest assembly (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the bonded part trim
leather (65) from the armrest assembly (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the armrest assembly (70):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon head screws (80) three
flat washers (85) and collect the bracket assembly (75).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove eight hexagon head screws (95), eight
flat washers (100) and collect the cocktail table equipped (90).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cocktail table equipped (90):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (110), four
flat washers (115) and collect two cocktail table brackets (105).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two countersunk
head screws (125) and collect the flap closeout assembly (120).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Disassemble the flap
closeout assembly (120):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two pins (135) and collect the block
hinge (130).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two springs (140, 145) and collect
the closeout assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disassemble the closeout assembly (150):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded part hinge blocks (151,
152) from the closeout assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the closeout flap (153) from the
closeout assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagonal head screws (160), two
flat washers (165) and collect the bracket assembly (155).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagonal head screws (175),
four flat washers (180) and collect the cover (170).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one bracket assembly (185), one threaded
rod (190) from the cocktail table equipped (90).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (200), two
flat washers (205) and collect the bracket assembly (195).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (195):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (215),
one flat washer (220) and collect the cable clamp (210).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part edging grommet (225)
from the bracket assembly (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one pan head screw (235), one flat
washer (240) and collect the button assembly (230).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagonal head screws (250), two
flat washers (255) and collect the bracket assembly (245).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (265)
and collect the capping assembly (260).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (275),
four hexagon head screws (280, 285), four flat washers (290, 292)
and collect the cocktail table trim assembly (270).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cocktail table trim assembly
(270):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (300),
two flat washers (305) and collect the bracket assembly (295).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (315), two flat
washers (320) and collect the capping assembly (310).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove three pan head screws (330), three
flat washers (335) and collect the capping assembly (325).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one pan head screw (345), one flat
washer (350) and collect the capping assembly (340).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (360),
two flat washers (365) and collect the trim assembly (355).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the trim assembly
(355):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the trim assembly (400) from the cocktail
table trim assembly (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagonal head screws (375), two
flat washers (380) and collect the bracket assembly (370).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the earth stud (390), bonded part
edging grommet (395) from the feature strip assembly (385).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Figure 30 Parts List for Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three pan head screws (410), three
flat washers (415) and collect the light diffuser (405).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one light diffuser (420) and one cocktail
table rim assembly (425) from the cocktail table equipped (90).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (435), two flat washers (440) and collect the bracket
assembly (430).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-003-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Privacy Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13) from
the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the privacy screen assembly
(5-115, 6-115).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the privacy screen assembly (5-115,
6-115) from the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 13 IPL for the Privacy Screen Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="012"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-012-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Privacy Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Cut four or one tie wraps (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove one countersunk head
screw (15) and collect the cable tie (10).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Remove one hexagon
head screw (25), one flat washer (30) and collect the manual override
assembly (20).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Disassemble the manual
override assembly (20):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (40) and collect
the manual override cable (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bracket (45).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Remove and disassemble
the actuator assembly (50):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (60) and collect
the actuator bracket (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>HOLD THE ACTUATOR DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove one countersunk head screw (70), two flat washers (75),
one self-locking nut (80) and collect the actuator (65).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove and collect the belt
(85) from the privacy screen assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove two hexagon head
screws (95), two flat washers (100) and collect the bracket (90).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove three countersunk
head screws (110, 115), three hexagon head screws (120), three flat
washers (125), one self-locking washer (130) and collect the actuator
assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Disassemble the actuator
assembly (105):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (140) and collect
the manual override cable (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bracket (145) from
the actuator assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (155),
four flat washers (160) and collect the belt bracket (150).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bracket assembly (165)
from the actuator assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (175),
one flat washer (180) and collect the stopper bracket (170).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bracket (185) from the actuator
assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the privacy actuator assembly
(190) from the actuator assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the privacy actuator assembly
(190):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head bolts (200), two
hexagon self lock nuts (205) and collect the actuator bracket (195).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one flat head screw (215) and collect
the drive pulley (210).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two cap head screws (225) and collect
the gearbox (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>HOLD THE ACTUATOR DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove and collect the actuator (230) from the privacy actuator
assembly (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove two countersunk flat
head screws (240) and collect the bracket assembly (235).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For assembly 1A: Disassemble the bracket
assembly (235):</para><revend></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>For Assembly 1A: Disassemble the self-adhesive hook fasteners
(245) from the bracket assembly (235).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove two hexagon head
screws (255), two flat washers (260) and collect the stopper bracket
(250).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove two hexagon head screws
(270), two flat washers (275) and collect the solenoid assembly (265).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Disassemble the solenoid
assembly (265):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four cap head screws (285), four flat
washers (290) and collect the solenoid bracket (280).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the privacy electrical
installation (295):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Cut two tie wraps (300) from the privacy
electrical installation (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the slotted spring pin (315) and collect
the spring (305) from the privacy electrical installation (295).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the shaft (310) from the privacy electrical
installation (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the spacing sleeve (320) from the
privacy electrical installation (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove spacer (325) from the privacy electrical
installation (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one cap head screw (335), one flat
washer (340) and collect the harness assembly (330).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove two hexagon head screws
(350), two flat washers (355) and collect the disconnect bracket (345).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove eight countersunk
head screws (365), eight countersunk finishing washers (370) and collect
the rail assembly (360).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Disassemble the rail assembly
(360):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (380),
two hexagon self-locking nuts (385) and collect the stopper (375).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (395)
and collect the pin (390).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the pop rivet (405), two flat washers
(410) and collect the torsion strip (400).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5742:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (420)
and collect the attachment support (415).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5742, Pre SB25-5769:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (420)
and collect the attachment support (415A).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5769:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (420)
and collect the joggle panel (415B).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one belt (425) from the rail assembly
(360).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (435),
one self-locking nut (440) and collect the attachment support (430).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (450),
one hexagon self-locking nut (455) and collect the attachment bracket
(445).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove ten countersunk head screws (465),
ten hexagon self-locking nuts (470) and collect the rail assembly
(460).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the rail support bracket (475) from
the rail assembly (360).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the closing cover (480) from the rail
assembly (360).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend></prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove two hexagon head
screws (490), two flat washers (495) and collect the bracket (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove ten or seven hexagon head screws (505),
ten or seven flat washers (510) and collect the belt assembly (500).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the belt assembly (500):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Remove three hexagon
head screws (520), three flat washers (525) and collect the rail support
bracket (515).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Remove two hexagon
head screws (535), two flat washers (540) and collect the rail support
bracket (530).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Remove three hexagon
head screws (550), three flat washers (555) and collect the rail support
bracket (545).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove two hexagon head screws
(565), two flat washers (570) and collect the attachment bracket (560).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B: Remove two hexagon head
screws (580), two flat washers (585) and collect the stopper (575).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B: Remove two cap head screws
(595), two flat washers (600) and collect the stopper (590).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove the bobbin pin (605)
from the belt assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Remove the drive belt
assembly (610) from the belt assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove the t-piece (615)
from the belt assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B: Remove and collect the bobbin
pin (620).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove eight countersunk
head screws (630), eight flat washers (635) and collect the lower
privacy panel (625).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Disassemble the lower privacy
panel (625):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove seven countersunk head screws (645)
and collect the armrest support (640).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (650) from the
lower privacy panel (625).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the lower privacy panel (655) from
the lower privacy panel (625).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove eight countersunk
head screws (665), eight flat washers (670) and collect the lower
privacy panel (660).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Disassemble the lower privacy
panel (660):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove seven countersunk head screws (680)
and collect the armrest support (675).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (685) from the
lower privacy panel (660).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the lower privacy panel (690) from
the lower privacy panel (660).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove ten countersunk head
screws (700), ten flat washers (705) and collect the middle privacy
panel (695).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Disassemble the middle privacy
panel (695):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (715)
and collect two stop blocks (710).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (720) from the
middle privacy panel (695).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the middle privacy panel (725) from
the middle privacy panel (695).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove ten countersunk head
screws (735), ten flat washers (740) and collect the middle privacy
panel (730).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Disassemble the middle privacy
panel (730):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (750)
and collect two stop blocks (745).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (755) from the
middle privacy panel (730).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the middle privacy panel (760) from
the middle privacy panel (730).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5750:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove nine hexagon head
screws (770, 775, 775A), twelve flat washers (780, 785), nine hexagon
self-locking nuts (790, 795) and collect the upper privacy panel (765).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5750:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove nine hexagon head
screws (770, 775, 775B), twelve flat washers (780, 785), nine hexagon
self-locking nuts (790, 795) and collect the upper privacy panel (765)
with two closeout brackets (761, 762).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Disassemble the upper privacy
panel (765):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (805)
and collect four stop blocks (800).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (810) from the
upper privacy panel (765).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the upper privacy panel (815) from
the upper privacy panel (765).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Remove and disassemble the
locking bracket assembly (820):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon self-locking nut (830),
one washer (835) and collect the locking pin (825).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the locking pin (840) from the locking
bracket assembly (820).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the adjustable slider (845) from the
locking bracket assembly (820).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the spring (850) from the locking
bracket assembly (820).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove manual override (855) from the locking
bracket assembly (820).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="031"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-031-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Privacy Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13A):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove five hexagon screws
(10, 15), five flat washers (20, 25) and collect the privacy screen
assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Disassemble the privacy
screen assembly (5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the privacy electrical
installation (30):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Cut ten tie wraps (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Cut the cable tie (40).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disconnect the harness assembly
(45) from the privacy electrical installation (30) at connectors P1
and J4.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the protection cable (50) from the
privacy electrical installation (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the LRU interface cable (55) from
the privacy electrical installation (30) at connector P1.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (65), two hexagon
self-locking nuts (70) and collect the bracket (60).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (80), two hexagon
self-locking nuts (85) and collect the cat-track assembly (75).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cat-track assembly (75):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the chain mounting bracket (90) from
the cat-track assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove thirty-two chains (95) from the cat-track
assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the chain mounting bracket (100) from
the cat-track assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (110),
two flat washers (115) and collect the electrical bracket (105).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (125),
two flat washers (130) and collect the stopper bracket (120).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (140),
one flat washer (145) and collect the top capping assembly (135).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the top capping assembly (135):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (155),
two flat washers (160) and collect the cap attachment bracket (150).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (170)
and collect two fixing hook cappings (165).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the top capping (180).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (190)
and collect two cable mounting brackets (185).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (200),
one flat washer (205), one self-locking nut (210) and collect the
end capping retainer (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three countersunk head screws (220),
three flat washers (225), three self-locking nuts (230) and collect
the interface bracket (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the privacy screen assembly
(235) from the privacy screen assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B: Remove three hexagon head
screws (245), three flat washers (250) and collect the privacy screen
EQ panel (240).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="013"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-013-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Closeout Panel Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
14):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove eight countersunk
head screws (10) and collect the lower edge capping privacy (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C and 1E: Remove six
countersunk head screws (20, 25, 30), two hexagon nuts (35), two flat
washers (40) and collect the angled bracket (15).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove eight countersunk
head screws (50), eight finishing countersunk washers (55) and collect
the attachment bracket (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove six countersunk
head screws (65, 70), six finishing countersunk washers (75, 80) and
collect the attachment bracket (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove twelve countersunk
head screws (90, 95), twelve finishing countersunk washers (100) and
collect the attachment bracket (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove eight countersunk
head screws (110), eight finishing countersunk washers (115) and collect
the attachment bracket (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove two hexagon
head screws (125), two flat washers (130) and collect the spigot assembly
(120).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Disassemble the spigot
assembly (120):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fastener (135) from the
spigot assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bushing (140), pin console alignment
(145) and block (150) from the spigot assembly (120).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove two hexagon
head screws (160), two flat washers (165) and collect the spigot assembly
(155).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Disassemble the spigot
assembly (155):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fastener (170) from the
spigot assembly (155).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bushing (175), pin console alignment
(180) and block (185) from the spigot assembly (155).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove two hexagon
head screws (195), two flat washers (200) and collect the bracket
(190).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove and disassemble
the lower middle cladding assembly (205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part two magnets (210)
from the lower middle cladding assembly (205).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part bracket (215) from
the lower middle cladding assembly (205).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B and 1D: Remove one
countersunk head screw (225), two socket head screws (230), one finishing
countersunk washer (245), two flat washers (250) and collect the closeout
panel assembly (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove five countersunk
head screws (235, 240), five flat washers (255) and collect the closeout
panel assembly (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the closeout panel assembly (220):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C and 1E: Remove the
bonded part four or three magnets (260) from the closeout panel assembly
(220).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove the closeout
panel (261) from the closeout panel assembly (220).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove the seat surround
cladding (262) from the closeout panel assembly (220).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Remove two hexagon
head screws (270), two flat washers (275) and collect the spigot assembly
(265).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Disassemble the spigot
assembly (265):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fastener (280) from the
spigot assembly (265).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bushing (285), pin console alignment
(290) and block (295) from the spigot assembly (265).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Remove two hexagon
head screws (305), two flat washers (310) and collect the spigot assembly
(300).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Disassemble the spigot
assembly (300):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fastener (315) from the
spigot assembly (300).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bushing (320), pin console alignment
(325) and block (330) from the spigot assembly (300).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Remove closeout panel
(335) from the closeout panel assembly (220).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove and collect
elite panel (340) from the closeout panel installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove and collect
the forward panel (345) from the closeout panel installation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Remove and collect
the fixed privacy panel (350) from the closeout panel installation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-004-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Dot Door Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 15) from the
Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the dot door installation (5-240,
6-235).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the dot door installation (5-240,
6-235) from the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 15 IPL for the Dot Door Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="014"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-014-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Dot Door Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 15):</title>
<prclist1><revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (10), two flat
washers (15) and collect the bumper assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bumper assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part lateral bumper support
(20) and bumper cover (25) from the bumper assembly (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six socket head screws (35), six flat
washers (40) and collect the support bracket assembly (30).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(30):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bumper electrical
assembly (45):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disconnect the harness and collect the IUL
(50) at connector P8 from the support bracket assembly (30).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disconnect the harness and collect the TTL
indicator (55) at connector D43P from the support bracket assembly
(30).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part attachment spacer
(56) from the support bracket assembly (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four socket head screws (65), four
flat washers (70) and collect one clip (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one socket head screw (80) and collect
the toggle switch assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the toggle switch assembly (75):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the hinge pin (90), ball plunger (95)
and collect the latch toggle (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the toggle switch outer
case (100) from the toggle switch assembly (75).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the latch cover assembly
(105):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(110) from the latch cover assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part cover bracket (115)
from the latch cover assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Drill out the pop rivet (125), washer (130)
and collect the cord lanyard assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the latch cover (135).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one pan head screw (145), one socket
head screw (150), two flat washers (155, 160) and collect the bracket
assembly (140).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5781: Remove one socket head screw
(150A), one flat washer (160) and collect the bracket assembly (140).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5781: Remove one socket head screw
(150B), one flat washer (160) and collect the bracket assembly (140).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (140):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove eight pan head screws (170) and collect
two receptacles (165).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bracket (175) from
the bracket assembly (140).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5781: Remove one socket head screw
(177), one flat washer (178) and collect the dot secure clamp (176).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5781: Remove one socket head screw
(177A), one flat washer (178) and collect the dot secure clamp (176).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (185), two
flat washers (190) and collect the support pin (180).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the dot panel assembly
(195):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four socket head screws (205) and
collect two wedge blocks (200).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (215) and collect
two wedge block (210).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (225), one
flat washer (230) and collect the dot latch assembly (220).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the dot latch assembly (220):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(235) from the dot latch assembly (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Drill out four pop rivets (245) and collect
two latches (240).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bracket (250) from
the dot latch assembly (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (260), two
flat washers (265) and collect the dot bumper assembly (255).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bonded part lateral
bumper support (270) from the dot panel assembly (195).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bumper cover (275)
from the dot panel assembly (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four socket head screws (285), four
flat washers (290) and collect two mounting brackets (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four socket head screws (300), four
flat washers (305) and collect two clips (295).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the dot top EQ inner
cladding (310):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fastener (315) from the
dot top EQ inner cladding (310).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (320) from
the dot top EQ inner cladding (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the dot upper inner cladding (321)
from the dot top EQ inner cladding (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the dot mid EQ inner
cladding (325):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (330) from the
dot mid EQ inner cladding (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the dot upper inner cladding (331)
from the dot mid EQ inner cladding (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the dot lower EQ lower
cladding (335):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (340) from the
dot inner EQ inner cladding (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the dot upper inner cladding (341)
from the dot inner EQ inner cladding (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the dot bottom EQ
inner cladding (345):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (350) from the
dot bottom EQ inner cladding (345).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Collect the dot upper inner cladding (351)
from the dot bottom EQ inner cladding (345).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four socket head screws (360, 365,
370), four flat washers (375) and collect the aft standard EQ cap
(355).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (385), two
flat washers (390) and collect the dot edge capping (380).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect tapered dowel (395) and
dot panel (400) from the dot panel assembly (195).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (410)
and collect the support pin (405).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (420), two
flat washers (425) and collect the clip (415).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-005-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Sliding Door Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 16) from
the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the sliding door installation
(5-140, 6-140).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the sliding door installation (5-140,
6-140) from the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 16 IPL for the Sliding Door Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="015"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-015-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Sliding Door Installation (Ref. IPL Fig 16):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (10), one flat
washer (15) and collect the top roller assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the top roller assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one pin (25) and collect the roller
(20).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the roller bracket (30) from the top
roller assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (40),
two flat washers (45) and collect the stopper assembly (35).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the top stopper assembly (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part seal (50) from the
top stopper assembly (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (60) and
collect the magnet (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the door stop assembly (65) from the
top stopper assembly (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (75), two
flat washers (80) and collect the support bracket assembly (70).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(70):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one self-adhesive duotec fastener
(85) from the support bracket assembly (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove eleven socket head screws (95) and
collect the top rail assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the top rail assembly (90):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove eight countersunk head screws (105)
and collect the carriage block assembly (100).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the carriage block assembly (100):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one set screw (115) and collect the
support pin (110).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one set screw (125) and collect the
support pin (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (135)
and collect the platine (130).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one slotted spring pin (145) and collect
the unlocking lever (140).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one spring (150) from the carriage
block assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one bracket (155) from the carriage
block assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>DO NOT REMOVE SLIDES FROM RAIL ASSEMBLY. IF YOU DO
NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE SLIDE AND RAIL WILL OCCUR.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove the rail (160) from the rail assembly (90).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (170,
175), two set screws (180) and collect the spigot block assembly (165).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the spigot block assembly (165):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four nuts (190) and collect two cam
followers (185).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one spigot block (195) from the spigot
block assembly (165).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove seven countersunk head screws (205,
210) and collect the closeout assembly (200).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (220),
two flat washers (225) and collect the striker plate (215).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove three countersunk head screws (235)
and collect the door guide assembly (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the door guide assembly (230):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (245)
and collect the door guide (240).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two pins (250), two flat washers (255)
and two rollers (260) from the door guide assembly (230).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four springs (265) from the door guide
assembly (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the roller support (270) from the
door guide assembly (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect nine plates (275, 280,
285).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bonded part collar
(290).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one set screw (300) and collect the
button assembly (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the button assembly (295):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one bonded part rod (305) from the
EPF button assembly (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one spacer (310) from the button assembly
(295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one spring (315) from the button assembly
(295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one button (320) from the button assembly
(295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bonded door panel
assembly (325):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bonded part edge
capping assembly (330):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one pin (335) and collect the edge
capping (340).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (350), two flat
washers (355) and collect the top edge capping (345).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bonded part edge
capping assembly (360):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two pins (365) and collect the edge
capping (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bonded part edge
capping assembly (375):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two pins (380) and collect the edge
capping (385).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (395)
and collect the handle (390).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bonded part edge
capping assembly (400):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one pin (405) and collect the edge
capping (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part edge capping (415)
from the bonded door panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three countersunk head screws (425)
and collect the latch cover plate (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the link (430) from the bonded door
panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble two latch hook assemblies
(435):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one ball plunger (445) and collect
the latch hook (440).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (455)
and collect the bezel assembly (450).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (465)
and collect the latch plate (460).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one link (470) from the bonded door
panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one spring (475) from the bonded door
panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one latch hook (480) from the bonded
door panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (490)
and collect the latch bezel assembly (485).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove bonded part two decorative door panels
(495, 500) from the bonded door panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one equipped internal door (505) from
the bonded door panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-006-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Upper Console Stowage Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
17) from the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the upper console stowage installation
(5-145, 6-145).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the upper console stowage installation
(5-145, 6-145) from the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and
Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 17 IPL for the Upper Console Stowage Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="016"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-016-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Upper Console Stowage Installation (Ref. IPL
Fig. 17):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (10), one
countersunk finishing washer (15) and collect the light panel assembly
(5).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the light panel assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (25) and collect
the light diffuser (20).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the light panel (30).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the trim panel assembly
(35):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the panel assembly
(40):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY NOT TO DAMAGE THE PRODUCT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (45) from the panel
assembly (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (55), two
flat washers (60) and collect the bracket (50).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove ten hexagon head screws (70, 75, 80),
ten flat washers (85) and collect the structure stowage assembly (65).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the structure stowage assembly
(65):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (95)
and collect the stowage door assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the stowage door assembly (90):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (105)
and collect two hinges (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (115)
and collect the latch cover (110).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the latch assembly
(120) from the stowage door assembly (90):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two latch shafts (130, 150), two circlips
(135, 155) and collect two latch hooks (125, 145).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two springs (140, 160) from the latch
assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the latch handle (165) from the latch
assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the latch frame (170) from the latch
assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (180) and collect
the bezel bracket (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part panel assembly (185)
from the stowage door assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part magnet (190) from
the stowage door assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the trimmed door assembly (195) from
the stowage door assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (205)
and collect the retainer striker (200).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (215)
and collect the striker plate (210).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the latch striker
assembly (220):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bumper (225) from the latch striker
assembly (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (235), two flat
washers (240) and collect the trim panel assembly (230).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the trim panel assembly (230):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bezel microphone (245) from the
trim panel assembly (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bezel microphone retainer (250)
from the trim panel assembly (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the upper stowage
panel assembly (255):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY NOT TO DAMAGE THE PRODUCT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (260) from the upper
stowage panel assembly (255).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (270) and
collect the bracket assembly (265).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (265):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(275) from the bracket assembly (265).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the microphone bracket
assembly (280):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release two nylatch plungers (285) and two
nylatch grommets (290) from the microphone bracket assembly (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(295) from the microphone bracket assembly (280).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (305),
two flat washers (310) and collect the bracket assembly (300).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (300):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY NOT TO DAMAGE THE PRODUCT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fastener (315) from the bracket
assembly (300).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the hall effect assembly
(320):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release two nylatch plungers (325) and two
nylatch grommets (330) from the hall effect assembly (320).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the spacer assembly
(335):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tape (340) from the
spacer assembly (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove nine pan head screws (350) and collect
the panel assembly (345).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the panel assembly (345).</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY NOT TO DAMAGE THE PRODUCT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (355) from the panel
assembly (345).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the spring plunger (360) from the
structure stowage assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the trim panel assembly
(365):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY NOT TO DAMAGE THE PRODUCT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (375) from the panel
assembly (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the trim panel assembly
(380):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY NOT TO DAMAGE THE PRODUCT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (390) from the panel
assembly (385).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the drip tray assembly
(395):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the drip tray bezel (400) from the
drip tray assembly (395).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the circlip (405) from the drip tray
assembly (395).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY NOT TO DAMAGE THE PRODUCT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage four self-adhesive hook fasteners (410) from the drip
tray assembly (395).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the transfer tape (411) and drip tray
(412).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the drip tray tube (415) from the
structure stowage assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the panel assembly
(420):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY NOT TO DAMAGE THE PRODUCT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (425).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(430).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-007-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Folding Armrest Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 18)
from the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the folding armrest installation
(5-165, 6-165).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the folding armrest installation (5-165,
6-165) from the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 18 IPL for the Folding Armrest Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="017"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-017-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Folding Armrest Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
18):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (10, 15),
four flat washers (20) and collect the folding armrest assembly (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the folding armrest assembly
(5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the RH and LH armrest mounting structure
(25, 30) and collect the armrest bottom cladding (35) from the folding
armrest assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the transfer tapes (40) and folding
armrest assembly (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the folding armrest assembly
(45):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the cover assembly (50) from the folding
armrest assembly (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded part folding armrest foams
(55) from the folding armrest assembly (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one armrest base structure assembly
(60) from the folding armrest assembly (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the armrest base structure assembly
(60):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (70) and
collect the armrest structure cap (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the armrest base structure (75) from
the armrest base structure assembly (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two pins (85) and collect the hinge
(80).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="018"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-018-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Outboard Bridge Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
19):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (10),
two flat washers (15) and collect the bridge assembly (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bridge assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove five or two pan head screws (25),
five or two flat washers (30) and collect the cover (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the electrical kit (35) from the bridge
assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the electrical kit (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Cut twenty-nine or twenty-eight or thirty
or thirty-one cable ties from the electrical kit (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F and 1G: Remove the fixing
base (45) from the electrical kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disconnect and remove the harness assembly
(50) from the electrical kit (35) at connectors D14P, D16P and D301P.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1G, 1L, 1M and 1N: Disconnect
and remove the harness assembly (55) from the electrical kit (35)
at connectors D23P, P201, P101 and P100A.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disconnect and remove the harness assembly
(60) from the electrical kit (35) at connectors P1A, P2A, P4A and
P10.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1M and 1N: Disconnect and remove the harness assembly (65)
from the electrical kit (35) at connectors P1, P1A, P2, P2A, J1C and
P1C.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1G, 1H and 1N: Remove four
pan head screws (70) and collect the harness assembly (65).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C and 1J: Disconnect
and remove the harness assembly (75) from the electrical kit (35)
at connectors P2, P6B and P6.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the roundit (80) from
the electrical kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1J, 1L,
1M and 1N: If necessary, remove the roundit (85) from the electrical
kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: If necessary, remove
the roundit (90) from the electrical kit (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1K,
1L 1M and 1N: If necessary, remove the roundit (91) from the electrical
kit (35)</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bridge assembly
(95):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1L, 1M and
1N: Remove one countersunk head screw (105) and collect the cable
tie mount (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1L, 1M and
1N: Remove one hexagon head screw (115) and collect the cable clamp
(110).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the end cap (116) from the electrical
kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1H,
1J, 1K, 1L and 1M: Remove two countersunk head screws (125), two flat
washers (130) and collect the support bracket assembly (120).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1H,
1J, 1K, 1L and 1M: Disassemble the support bracket assembly (120):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove one countersunk head screw
(140) and collect the foam bridge support dampener (135).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the support bracket (145) from the
support bracket assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="019"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-019-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the FWD Fascia Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 20):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (10) and
collect the bracket assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (20),
four flat washers (25) and collect four spacers (15).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part edging grommets (30)
from the bracket assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the monitor bracket (35)
from the bracket assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (45), two
flat washers (50) and collect the locking bracket (40).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (60) and
collect the trim panel assembly (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the trim panel assembly (55):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two circlips (70) and collect the
logo (65) from the trim panel assembly (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the panel assembly (75)
from the trim panel assembly (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the panel assembly (75):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove four self-adhesive loop fasteners (80) from the
trim panel assembly (75).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the trim panel (81) from the
panel assembly (75).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the trim (82) from the trim
panel assembly (55).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (90), four
flat washers (95) and collect the literature pocket assembly (85).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the literature pocket assembly
(85):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (105),
four flat washers (110) and collect two literature pockets (100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bracket assembly (115)
from the literature pocket assembly (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (115):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive four hook fasteners (120) from
the bracket assembly (115).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the fascia panel (125)
from the furniture assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the trim assembly
(130):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the panel assembly
(135) from the trim assembly (130):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(140) from the panel assembly (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the trim assembly
(145):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the panel assembly
(150) from the trim assembly (145):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(155) from the panel assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (165), six
flat washers (170) and collect three brackets (160).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (180), six
flat washers (185) and collect three brackets (175).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the capping (190) from the fascia
Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (200), six
flat washers (205) and collect three brackets (195).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (195):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the low friction tape (210) from the
bracket assembly (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (220), two
flat washers (225) and collect the bracket assembly (215).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (215):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the low friction tape (230) from the
bracket assembly (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-008-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Lifevest Box Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 21) from the
Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the lifevest box assembly (5-230).
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the lifevest box assembly (5-230)
from the furniture assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 21 IPL for the Lifevest Box Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="020"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-020-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Lifevest Box Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 21):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Drill out two pop rivets (10, 15), four flat
washers (20) and collect the cord lanyard assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cord lanyard assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove two lanyard connectors (21)
and one cord (22) from the cord lanyard assembly (5).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the lifevest door
assembly (25):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the bonded part double-sided
tape (35) and collect the bonded part latch cover (30).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the lifevest door
assembly (40):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (50) and collect
the back latch (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the pull tab assembly
(55), latch lever assembly (60) and lifevest door cover assembly (65).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fastener (70) from the
lifevest door assembly (40).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (80) and collect
the latch shear assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the lifevest door (82)
from the lifevest door assembly (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part support bracket (84)
from the lifevest door assembly (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5801: Remove and disassemble the
lifevest cover assembly (85):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(90) from the lifevest cover assembly (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Post SB25-5801: Disengage the loop fastener (91) from the lifevest
box assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>Remove and collect twelve covers from
the lifevest box assembly.(95, 100).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (110, 115),
six flat washers (120) and collect the lifevest box assembly (105).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the lifevest box assembly (105):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon self-locking nuts (130),
two flat washers (135) and collect the latch bar (125).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the bonded part doubler
(140) from the lifevest box assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="021"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-021-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Seat Recess Claddings Installation (Ref. IPL
Fig. 22):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1F and 1G: Remove and
disassemble the cladding assembly (5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(10) from the cladding assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (15) from the
cladding assembly (5).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1F and 1G: Remove two
hexagon head screws (25), two flat washers (30) and collect the bracket
assembly (20).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (20):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(35) from the bracket assembly (20).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1F and 1G: Remove three
countersunk head screws (45), three countersunk washers (50) and collect
the cladding assembly (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the cladding assembly
(40):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four bonded part magnets (55) from
the cladding assembly (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove and collect
the seat surround cladding assembly (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1E: Remove one countersunk
head screw (65), one finishing countersunk washer (70) and collect
the seat surround cladding assembly (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D and 1E: Disassembly
the seat surround cladding assembly (60):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (75) from the seat
surround cladding assembly (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three or two bonded part magnets (80)
from the seat surround cladding assembly (60).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1E: Remove and disassemble
the cladding assembly (85):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (90) from the cladding
assembly (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (100), two
flat washers (105) and collect the cladding bracket (95).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove three countersunk head screws (115,
120), two countersunk finishing washers (125) and collect the seat
surround cladding assembly (110).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the seat surround cladding assembly
(110):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part headrest cover (130)
from the seat surround cladding assembly (110).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the headrest foam (135) from the seat
surround cladding assembly (110).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the cladding assembly
(140):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(145) from the cladding assembly (140).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (155, 160,
165), three flat washers (170), one countersunk finishing washer (175)
and collect the seat surround cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the seat surround cladding assembly
(150):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the seat surround cover (180) from
the seat surround cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the seat surround foam (185) from
the seat surround cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the seat surround cladding (190) from
the seat surround cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four bonded part magnets (195, 200)
from the seat surround seat surround cladding (190).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two countersunk
head screws (210), four head screws (215), two countersunk finishing
washers (225), four flat washers (230) and collect the seat surround
cladding assembly (205).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F and 1G: Remove
three countersunk head screws (210, 220), three hexagon head screws
(215), two countersunk finishing washers (225), three flat washers
(230), one countersunk head washer (235) and collect the seat surround
cladding assembly (205).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the seat surround cladding assembly
(205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part seat surround cover
(240) from the seat surround cladding assembly (205).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part seat surround foam
(245) from the seat surround cladding assembly (205).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the seat surround cladding assembly
(250) from the seat surround cladding assembly (205).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Diassemble the seat surround cladding assembly
(250):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (255) from the cladding
assembly (250).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1F and 1G: Remove one
or two countersunk head screws (265), one or two countersunk washers
(270) and collect the side cladding assembly (260).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1F and 1G: Disassemble
the side cladding assembly (260):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part side cladding cover
(275) from the side cladding assembly (260).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part side cladding foam
(280) from the side cladding assembly (260).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the cladding assembly (285) from the
side cladding assembly (260).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cladding assembly (285):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(290) from the cladding assembly (285).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part support bracket assembly
(295) from the cladding assembly (285).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(300) from the bracket assembly (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D and 1E: Remove and
disassemble the cladding assembly (305):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(310) from the cladding assembly (305).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one bonded part magnet (311) from
the cladding assembly (305).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D and 1E: Remove two
hexagon head screws (320), four cappings (321, 322) and collect the
bracket assembly (315).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D and 1E: Remove two
countersunk head screws (335), two countersunk washers (340) and collect
the cladding assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cladding assembly (330):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(345) from the cladding assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (350) from
the cladding assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove six bonded part magnets (355) from
the cladding assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D and 1E: Remove and
disassemble the closeout assembly (360):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (365) from
the closeout assembly (360).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D and 1E: Remove two
countersunk head screws (375), two countersunk finishing washers (380)
and collect the bracket assembly (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (370):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(385) from the bracket assembly (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (395), four
flat washers (400) and collect the bracket assembly (390).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bracket assembly
(390):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one earth stud (405) from the bracket
assembly (390).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Figure 30 Parts List for Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (415, 420),
two flat washers (425) and collect the support bracket assembly (410).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the support bracket
assembly (410):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fastener (430) from the support
bracket assembly (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (440, 445),
two flat washers (450) and collect the cladding bracket assembly (435).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the cladding bracket
assembly (435):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fastener (455) from the cladding
bracket assembly (435).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="022"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-022-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Kickstrip and Seals Cladding Installation (Ref.
IPL Fig. 23):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1F: Remove and disassemble
the center closeout aisle kickstrip assembly (5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bonded part bracket
assembly (10).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the bracket assembly (10):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release one quarter turn screw (20), one quarter turn washer (25),
one quarter turn receptacle (30), one ejector spring (35) and collect
the bracket (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part magnet (40) from the
center closeout aisle kickstrip assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part p-seal (45) from the
center closeout aisle kickstrip assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1F: Remove two hexagon
head screws (55), two flat washers (60) and collect the bracket (50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1J and 1L: Remove two
hexagon head screws (70), two flat washers (75) and collect the clip
assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1J and 1L: Disassemble
the clip assembly (65):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (85) and
collect the cladding support bracket (80).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the attachment bracket (90) and console
spring clip bracket (95) from the clip assembly (65).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H and
1K: Remove one hexagon head screw (105), one countersunk head screw
(115), one flat washer (110), one bush (120) and collect the forward
console cladding assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (105), one
flat washer (110) and collect the forward console cladding assembly
(100).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the forward console cladding
assembly (100):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1G, 1H and 1K: Remove
two bonded part magnets (125) from the forward console cladding assembly
(100).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (130) from
the forward console cladding assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1J and 1L: Disengage the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (135) from the forward console cladding assembly (100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Remove and disassemble
the accessing panel assembly (140):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release two quarter turn screws (150), two quarter turn washers (155),
two quarter turn receptacles (160), two ejector springs (165) and
collect the baseframe access cladding (145).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bonded part attachment
bracket (170) from the accessing panel assembly (140).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Remove two hexagon
head screws (180), two flat washers (185) and collect the attachment
bracket (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Remove two hexagon
head screws (195), two flat washers (200) and collect the bracket
(190).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1G, 1H and 1K: Remove
and collect the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove three countersunk
head screws (215), three washers (220) and collect the aisle kickstrip
cladding assembly (210).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1E, 1G, 1H and
1K: Remove and disassemble the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1G, 1H and 1K: Attach
the bonded parts supporting sheets (221, 222, 223).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1G, 1H and 1K: Attach the
bonded part suppoting sheet (224).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bonded part aisle floor seal (236).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1G, 1H and 1K: Remove
double-sided tapes (225) from the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly
(210).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disengage the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (230) from the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly
(210).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(235) from the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove and disassemble the ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly
(240):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release two quarter turn screws (250), two quarter turn retainers
(255) and collect the ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly (245).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded part magnets (260) from
the ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly (245).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5797: Remove and collect the bonded
part doubler (261) from the ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly (240).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove six countersunk head screws (270), six flat washers (275)
and collect two light cover support brackets (265).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove two hexagon head screws (285), two flat washers (290) and
collect two brackets (280).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove and disassemble the aft aisle kickstrip cladding assembly
(295):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bonded parts kickstrip bracket
(316) to the aft aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (295):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release one quarter turn screw (305), one quarter turn retainer (310)
and collect the aft aisle kickstrip cladding (300).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three bonded part magnets (315) from
the cladding aft aisle kickstrip (300).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove one hexagon head screw (325), one flat washer (330) and
collect the light cover support bracket (320).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove one hexagon head screw (340), one flat washer (345) and
collect the light cover support bracket assembly (335).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and 1K: Remove
one countersunk head screw (355), one flat washer (360) and collect
the aft aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (350).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the aft aisle kickstrip
cladding assembly (350):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove the bonded
part seal (365), double-sided tapes (370) and two bonded magnets (375)
from the aft aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (350).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D, 1F, 1H and 1K: Remove two
bonded part supporting sheets (378, 379) from the aft aisle kickstrip
cladding assembly (350).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove and collect
the bonded part floor seal assembly (376) and bonded part kickstrip
bracket (377).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1F: Remove one countersunk
head screw (385), one countersunk finishing washer (390) and collect
the cladding assembly (380).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1F: Disassemble the cladding
assembly (380):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (395) from
the cladding assembly (380).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(400) from the cladding assembly (380).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove two countersunk head screws (410), two flat washers (415)
and collect the aft base frame shroud assembly (405).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the aft base frame shroud assembly
(405):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded part p-seals (420, 425)
from the aft base frame shroud assembly (400).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bonded part bracket
assembly (426) and bonded part footwell bracket (427).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove one countersunk
head screw (435), one countersunk finishing washer (440) and collect
the seat to seat cladding assembly (430).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Disassemble the seat
to seat cladding assembly (430):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tape (445) and self-adhesive
duotec fastener (450) from the seat to seat cladding assembly (430).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded part seat to seat brackets
(451, 452).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H, 1J and 1L:
Remove one or three countersunk head screws (460), one or three washers
(465) and collect the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (455).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the aisle kickstrip cladding
assembly (455):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H, 1J and 1L:
Remove the double-sided tapes (470) from the aisle kickstrip cladding
assembly (455).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1H and 1K: Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(475) from the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (455).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1H and 1K: Remove the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (480) from the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly
(455).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1J and 1L: Remove
and collect eight bonded supporting sheets (481, 482).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bonded aisle floor
seal (483).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove one countersunk head screw (490), one washer (495) and
collect the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Disassemble the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (485):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (500) from
the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (485).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1H and 1K: Remove the double-sided
tapes (505) from the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove six bonded part magnets (510) from
the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (485).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bonded bracket attachment
(511) and bracket assembly (512).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D and 1F: Remove
the bonded supporting sheet (513).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1H and 1K: Remove two countersunk
head screws (520), two countersunk washers (525) and collect the backshell
kickstrip cladding assembly (515).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1H and 1K: Disassemble the backshell
kickstrip cladding assembly (515):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part seal (530) and double-sided
tapes (535) from the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (515).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove two countersunk head screws (545, 550), two flat washers
(555) and collect the aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly (540).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove and disassemble the aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly
(540):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded bonded part magnets (560)
from the aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly (540).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove the bonded part bracket
assembly (565) from the aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly (540).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Remove two countersunk head screws (580) and collect the aft support
footwell shroud (575).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="023"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-023-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the N-Aisle Claddings Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
24):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Remove two
countersunk head screws (10), two countersunk finishing washers (15)
and collect the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the seat-to-seat cladding assembly
(5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (20) from the
seat-to-seat cladding assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Remove one
countersunk head screw (30), one countersunk finishing washers (35)
and collect the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the seat-to-seat cladding assembly
(25):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (40) from the
seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(45) from the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1L,1M, 1P and
1Q: Remove two countersunk head screws (55), two countersunk washers
(60) and collect the under-aisle arm pad cladding (50).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the under-aisle arm pad cladding
(50):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessry, remove the bonded part under
aisle arm decor cladding (65) from the under-aisle arm pad cladding
(50).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the under armrest cladding assembly
(70) from the under-aisle arm pad cladding (50).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the under armrest cladding assembly
(70):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (75) from the
under armrest cladding assembly (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1K and 1N: Remove three countersunk
head screws (85), three countersunk washers (90) and collect the mid
backshell cladding assembly (80).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1K and 1N: Disassemble the mid
backshell cladding assembly (80):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part mid backshell decor
cladding (95) from the backshell cladding assembly (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the under armrest
cladding assembly (100):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (105) from
the under armrest cladding assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (110) from the under
armrest cladding assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1K and 1N: Remove and disassemble
the capping cladding assembly (115) from the n-Aisle Claddings Installation.
</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (120) from
the capping cladding assembly (115).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Remove two countersunk
head screws (130), two countersunk washers (135) and collect the ctr
closeout cladding assembly (125).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the ctr closeout cladding assembly
(125):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(140) from the ctr closeout cladding assembly (125).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three bonded part magnets (145) from
the ctr closeout cladding assembly (125).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Remove four countersunk
head screws (155), four countersunk washers (160) and collect the
ctr closeout cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the ctr closeout cladding assembly
(150):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(165) from the ctr closeout cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded part magnets (170) from
the ctr closeout cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (180)
two countersunk finishing washers (185) and collect the forward console
cladding assembly (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the forward console cladding
assembly (175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the seat surround
cladding (190):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(195) from the seat surround cladding (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (205),
two countersunk finishing washers (210) and collect the console side
cladding (211).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the console side cladding assembly
(200):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (215) from
the console side cladding assembly (200).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1L, 1M, 1P and
1Q: Remove two countersunk head screws (225) and collect the cladding
support bracket (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two counter-sunk head screws (235),
two countersunk finishing washers (240) and collect the fwd console
cladding assembly (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the forward console cladding
assembly (230):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(245) from the forward console cladding assembly (230).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1L, 1M, 1P and
1Q: Remove two console spring clip bracket (250) from the n-Aisle
Claddings Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1L: Remove three countersunk head screws (260), three
countersunk finishing washers (265) and collect the aft tray cladding
assembly (255).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1L: Disassemble the aft tray cladding assembly (255):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the tray table assembly
(270):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the tray table panel
assembly (275):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1K, 1L and 1P: Disengage
the self-adhesive loop fasteners (280) from the tray table panel assembly
(275).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (285) from the tray
table panel assembly (275).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(290) from the tray table panel assembly (275).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1K, 1L, 1N and
1P: Remove two countersunk head screws (300), two countersunk finishing
washers (305) and collect the tray table strip cladding (295).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the tray table strip cladding
(295):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded part magnets (310) from
the tray table strip cladding (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L and 1N: Remove one or two countersunk head screws (320), one
or two countersunk finishing washers (325) and collect the tray table
panel (315).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Remove two countersunk head screws (335, 340),
two or one countersunk head screws (345), three countersunk finishing
washers (350), one flat washer (355) and collect the aft aisle cladding
assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the aft aisle cladding assembly
(330):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (360) from the aft
aisle cladding assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one or three bonded part magnets (365)
from the aft aisle cladding assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Remove two countersunk
head screws (375), two countersunk finishing washers (380) and collect
the cladding assembly (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cladding assembly (370):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double-sided tapes (385) from
the cladding assembly (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Remove one countersunk head screw (395), one countersunk
washer (400) and collect the aft top console cladding assembly (390).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the aft top console cladding
assembly (390):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (405) from the console
cladding assembly (390).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1H, 1J, 1K and
1N: Remove three countersunk head screws (415) and collect the cladding
support bracket (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cladding support bracket
(410):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the duotec fasteners (420) from the
cladding support bracket (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Remove four countersunk head screws (430, 435),
four countersunk finishing washers (440, 445) and collect the aft
seat cladding assembly (425).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the aft seat cladding assembly
(425):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (450) from the aft
seat cladding assembly (425).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the duotec fasteners (455) from the
aft seat cladding assembly (425).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B and 1C: Remove and
disassemble the life vest closeout assembly (460):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (465) from the life
vest closeout assembly (460).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1K, 1L, 1N and
1Q: Remove and disassemble the aft to console left cladding (470):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (475) from the aft
to console left cladding (470).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Remove three countersunk head screws (485, 490,
497), three flat washers (495), one plastic cap ( 496) and collect
the pcu bumper bracket assembly (480).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Remove two countersunk head screws (510) and collect
the pcu bumper bracket assembly (505).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the pcu bumper bracket assembly
(505):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (515) from the bumper
bracket assembly (505).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part edging grommet (520)
from the pcu bumper bracket assembly (505).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (530),
two flat washers (535) and collect the mid console sup bracket (525).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (545,
550) and collect the ottoman left column (540).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (560,
565) and collect the meal panel support bracket (555).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (575,
580) and collect the ottoman right column (570).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="024"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-024-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Underseat Drip Tray (Ref. IPL Fig. 25):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (10), two
flat washers (15) and collect the support bracket (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (25), two
flat washers (30) and collect the drip tray bracket (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E and 1F: Remove
two hexagon head screws (40), two flat washers (45) and collect the
support bracket (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the drip tray sub assembly
(50) from the underseat drip tray assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the drip tray sub assembly (50):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three nylatch plungers (60), three
nylatch grommets (65) and collect the drip shield (55).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four studs (70) and four eyelets (75)
from the drip tray subassembly (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the drip shield installation (80,
80B) from the underseat drip tray assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the drip shield installation
(80, 80B):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5773: Remove the double-sided tapes
(84) from the drip shield installation (80B).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the drip shield installation
(85):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one nylatch plunger (95), one nylatch
grommet (100) and collect the drip shield (90).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fasteners (105) from the
drip shield installation (85).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one nylatch plunger (107), one nylatch
grommet (108) and collect the drip shield (106).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fasteners (109) from the
drip shield installation (80B).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E and 1F: Remove
and collect the drip shield installation (110) from the underseat
drip tray assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the drip shield installation
(110):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one nylatch plunger (120), one nylatch
grommet (125) and collect the drip shield (115).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fastener (130) from the
drip shield installation (110).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove and disassemble the
drip shield installation (135):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(140, 140A) from the drip shield installation (135).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part support bracket (145)
from the drip shield installation (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the drip shield installation
(150):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one nylatch plunger (160), one nylatch
grommet (165) and collect the drip shield (155).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fasteners (170) from the
drip shield installation (150).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the central beam cover
assembly (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the central beam cover assembly
(175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two bonded rail spar assemblies (180)
form the central beam cover assembly (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble two spar assemblies (180):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (185) from the
rail spar assembly (180).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the beam assembly (190)
from central beam cover assembly (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the beam assembly (190):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the fascia plate (195).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disassemble the fascia plate (195).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Drill out the pop rivet (205), two flat washers
(210) and collect the cord lanyard assembly (200) from the fascia
plate (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part center backing plate
(215) and the fascia plate (220) from the fascia plate assembly (195).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(225, 230) from the fascia plate (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Remove the self-adhesive hook and loop fasteners (235) from
the beam assembly (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the beam cover (240) from the beam
assembly (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="025"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-025-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Vertical Caps Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 26):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (10), one
pan head screw (15), two or one countersunk head screws (20), one
flat washer (25), two finishing countersunk washers (30) and collect
the static door capping (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1L and 1N: Remove
four countersunk head screws (40, 45, 50), one flat washer (55), two
finishing countersunk washers (60) and collect the static door capping
(35).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Remove three
countersunk head screws (70, 75), three flat washers (80) and collect
the upper capping (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Remove two
countersunk head screws (90), two flat washers (95) and collect the
dot edge capping (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J, 1K,
1L, 1M and 1N: Remove four countersunk head screws (105, 110), four
flat washers (115) and collect the capping (100).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J, 1K,
1L, 1M and 1N: Remove two countersunk head screws (125), one socket
cap head screw (130), three flat washers (135) and collect the capping
(120).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J, 1K,
1L, 1M and 1N: Remove two countersunk head screws (145, 150), two
flat washers (155, 160) and collect the aisle lower capping (140).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Remove three
hexagon head screws (170), three flat washers (175) and collect the
closeout assembly (165).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Disassemble
the closeout assembly (165):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the bonded part mounting bracket
(176) and bonded part privacy bracket assembly (177).</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (185) from the
privacy screen closeout assembly (180).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the privacy screen closeout
(181) from the privacy screen closeout  assembly (180).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Remove three hexagon
head screws (195), three flat washers (200) and collect the privacy
screen closeout assembly (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the privacy screen closeout assembly
(190):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (205) from the
privacy screen closeout assembly (190).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1K and 1M: Remove four
countersunk head screws (215), four flat washers (220) and collect
the edge capping (210).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1K and 1M: Remove two
countersunk head screws (230), two flat washers (235) and collect
the edge capping (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1, 1E, 1F: Remove and
collect the top cap (240).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1H and 1J: Remove one countersunk
head screw (245), one flat washer (250) and collect the top cap (240).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1E and 1F: Remove two countersunk
head screws (260), two flat washers (265) and collect the top cap
(255).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove and collect
the closeout assembly (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Remove two
hexagon head screws (275), two flat washers (280) and collect the
closeout assembly (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5739: For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1H and
1J: Remove one hexagon head screw (281), two flat washers (283), one
nut (282) and collect the closeout assembly (270).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1H and
1J: Disassemble the closeout assembly (270).</para><revend></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (285) from the closeout assembly (270).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Remove the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (290) from the closeout assembly (270).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the bonded part support bracket
assembly (295) from the closeout assembly (270).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(295):</para><revend></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(300) from the support bracket assembly (295).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para> For assembly 1 and 1A: Remove and
Disassemble the bonded part doubler assembly (301):</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the bonded part double sided
tape (302) from the doubler assembly (301).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two hexagon
head screws (310), two flat washers (315) and collect the support
bracket assembly (305).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(305):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(316) from the support bracket assembly (305).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Remove
two hexagon head screws (325), two flat washers (330) and collect
the top capping bracket assembly (320).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1H and 1J: Disassemble the
top capping bracketassembly (320):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Drill out one pop rivet (340), one flat washer
(345) and collect the cord lanyard assembly (335).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Remove
two hexagon head screws (355, 360), three flat washers (365), one
self-locking nut (370) and collect the top cap (350).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Remove two hexagon head
screws (355), two flat washers (365) and collect the top cap (350).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1L and 1N: Remove six
countersunk head screws (380), six flat washers (385) and collect
the closeout (375).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1L and 1N: Remove three
countersunk head screws (395), three flat washers (400) and collect
the edge capping (390).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Remove one countersunk
head screw (410) and collect the privacy screen closeout assembly
(405).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Disassemble the privacy
screen closeout assembly (405):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (415) from the
privacy screen closeout assembly (405).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the bonded part double-sided
tapes (420) from the privacy screen closeout assembly (405).</para>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Remove six countersunk
head screws (430), six flat washers (435) and collect the bracket
(425).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Remove two hexagon
head screws (445), two flat washers (450) and collect the privacy
screen closeout assembly (440).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="026"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-026-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Composite Integration (Ref. IPL Fig. 27):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the bare shell assembly
(5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove ten hexagon head screws (15, 20),
sixteen washers (25), four nuts (30) and collect the front beam assembly
(10).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the front beam assembly (10):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (40), four
flat washers (45), two nuts (50) and collect the EQ bracket (35).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (60), four
flat washers (65), two nuts (70) and collect the EQ bracket (55).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (80), two
nuts (85), four flat washers (90) and collect the EQ bracket (75).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the EQ front beam (95).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(96) from the rear beam assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove fourteen hexagon head screws (105,
110, 115, 120), twenty two flat washers (125), eight nuts (130) and
collect the rear beam assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(96) to the rear beam assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the rear beam assembly (100):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (140), four
flat washers (145), two nuts (150) and collect the EQ bracket (135).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon head screws (160, 165),
three nuts (170), six flat washers (175) and collect the EQ bracket
(155).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (185), two
nuts (190), four flat washers (195) and collect the EQ bracket (180).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the rear beam (200):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove one tape (201) from the rear beam
(200).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the shell composite
assembly (205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1D, 1F and 1G: Remove
two socket head screws (215), two flat washers (220) and collect the
indexing block (210).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1D, 1F and 1G: Remove
two socket head screws (230), two flat washers (235) and collect the
indexing block (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (245), two
flat washers (250) and collect the bracket (240).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the sidewall panel
assembly (255):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C,1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1K and 1M: Disengage
the self-adhesive loop fasteners (260) from the sidewall panel assembly
(255).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1K and 1M: Disengage
the self-adhesive hook fasteners (265) from the sidewall panel assembly
(255).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1E, 1G and 1H: Disengage
the self-adhesive hook fasteners (270) from the sidewall panel assembly
(255).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the aluminum tape (271) from the sidewall
panel assembly (255).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G and 1H:
Remove the grommet edging (272) from the sidewall panel assembly (255).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L and 1M: Remove ten hexagon head screws (280), ten flat washers
(285) and collect the bracket (275).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G,
1H, 1K, 1L and 1M: Remove four hexagon head screws (295), two socket
head screws (300), six flat washers (305) and collect the EQ aisle
sidewall panel (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ aisle sidewall panel (290):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1K
and 1M: Remove the duotec fasteners (306) from the EQ aisle sidewall
panel (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1H and 1M: Remove the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (307) from the EQ aisle sidewall panel (290).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G,
1H, 1K, 1L and 1M: Remove the aluminum tapes (308) from the EQ aisle
sidewall panel (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L and 1M:Remove the edging grommet (309) from the EQ aisle sidewall
panel (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1H and 1M:
Remove one socket head screw (315), two countersunk head screws (320),
one flat washer (325) and collect the bracket (310).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the doubler-reinforcement
(330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the tv support assembly
(335):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J and 1L: Disengage
the self-adhesive hook fasteners (340) from the tv support assembly
(335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (345) from the tv
support assembly (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the aluminium tapes (350) from the
tv support assembly (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1H,
1J, 1K, 1L and 1M: Remove the grommet (355) from the tv support assembly
(335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1H, 1K and 1M: Remove the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (356) from the tv support assembly
(335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the doublers (360).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (370), one
countersunk head screw (375), three flat washers (380) and collect
the EQ tray table support panel (365).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the EQ tray table support panel
(365):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the aluminum tape (381) and edging
grommet (382) from the EQ tray table support panel (365).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one socket head screw (390), one flat
washer (395) and collect the pcu bracket (385).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk screws (405) and collect
the bracket (400).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the support footrest
panel (410):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the aluminum tape (411) from the support
footrest panel (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the footrest vertical
panel (415):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the aluminum tape (416) and edging
grommet (417) from the footrest vertical panel (415).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the backshell (420):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the aluminum tapes (425) from the
backshell (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J
and 1L: Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (430) from the backshell
(420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the edging grommet (435) from the
backshell (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1E, 1H, 1K and 1M: Disengage the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (440) from the backshell (420).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="030" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-030-009-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Remove the Canopy Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 28) from the
Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access to the canopy installation (5-135,
6-135).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the canopy installation (5-135, 6-135)
from the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 28 IPL for the Canopy Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="027"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-027-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Canopy Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 28):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (10, 15),
four flat washers (20, 25) and collect the support bracket assembly
(5).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the support bracket assembly
(5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G,
1J and 1L: Remove two hexagon head screws (35), two flat washers (40)
and collect the bracket (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the bracket attachment (45).</para>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1, 1D and 1E: Remove
one bracket (50) and one center front seal from the canopy installation(55).
</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1A and 1G: Remove one
doubler from the canopy installation(60).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (70), two
flat washers (75) and collect the light bracket assembly (65).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the light bracket assembly (65):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one block spacer (80) and transfer
tape (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(90) and from the light backet assembly (65).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the bonded part reflector (91)
from the light bracket assembly (65).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the light bracket (92) from
the light bracket assembly (65).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (100)
and collect the aisle capping assemble (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H, 1J,
1K and 1L: Remove five hexagon head screws (110), five flat washers
(120) and collect the grab handle (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the panel trim assembly from
the canopy installation(125).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Remove three countersunk
head screws (135), three flat washers (140) and collect the capping
(130).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Remove three
hexagon head screws (150), six washers (155), three hexagon self-locking
nuts (160) and collect the support bracket (145).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1J and 1L: Remove
one countersunk head screw (170), one countersunk finishing washer
(175) and collect the support bracket (165).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1G, 1J and 1L: Remove two
countersunk head screws (185) and collect the electrical bracket assembly
(180).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (195, 200),
eleven flat washers (205, 210), five hexagon self locking nuts (215)
and collect the sub canopy assembly (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one doubler from the canopy installation(220).
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (230), four
countersunk head screws (235, 240), four hexagon self locking nuts
(250), eight flat washers (245) and collect the aisle capping assembly
(225).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the aisle capping assembly (225):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one hexagon head screw (260), one
flat washer (265) and collect the support bracket (255).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove self-adhesive loop fasteners (270) from the aisle
capping assembly (225).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the bonded part cover from
the canopy installation(275).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon head screws (285), three
flat washers (290) and collect the base aisle capping (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (300) and
collect the top capping epf aux rail (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (310) and
collect the top capping bracket (305).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the top capping bracket (305):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Remove bonded parts double-sided tapes
(315) from the top capping bracket (305).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the capping (320) from the
aisle capping assembly (225).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(325) from the aisle capping assembly (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the cover assembly (330) from
the canopy installation.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the cover assembly (330):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Remove one diffuser (335) from the
cover assembly (330).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one transfer tape (340) from the cover
assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(345) from the cover assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>Remove the cover assembly (346) from
the canopy installation.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Remove and disassemble
the spacer assembly (350):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fastener (360), bonded
part double-sided tape (365)  and collect the spacer (355).</para>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For assembly 1D: Remove the seal (370)
from the canopy installation.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="028"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-028-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Rear Row Closeout Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 29):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the seal (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove two socket
cap head screws (15), two flat washers (20) and collect the attachment
bracket assembly (10).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Disassemble the attachment
bracket assembly (10):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fastener (25) from the
attachment bracket assembly (10).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove three hexagon
head screws (35), three flat washers (40) and collect the base frame
bracket (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove and collect
the base frame bracket (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove three socket
cap head screws (55, 60), two flat washers (65), one washer (70) and
collect the rear row frame assembly (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Disassemble the rear
row frame assembly (50):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook and loop fasteners (75,
80) from the rear row frame assembly (50).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove two socket cap head screws (90), two
flat washers (95) and collect the support bracket (85).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (105,
120), four countersunk finishing washers (110, 125) and collect the
attachment brackets (100, 115).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release and remove two quarter turn fasteners (130), two quarter turn
receptacles (135), two ejector springs (140) and two quarter turn
washers (145).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one socket cap head screw (155), one
flat washer (160) and collect the middle bracket (150).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release and remove two quarter turn screws (165), two quarter turn
receptacles (170), two ejector springs (175) and two quarter turn
washers (180).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one socket cap head screw (190), one
flat washer (195) and collect the support bracket (185).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one socket cap head screw (205), one
flat washer (210) and collect the bracket (200).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove three socket cap head screws (220),
three flat washers (225) and collect the support bracket (215).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the bracket (230).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove two hexagon
head screws (240), two flat washers (245) and collect the closeout
bracket (235).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove six countersunk
head screws (255, 260), six countersunk finishing washers (265) and
collect two support plates (250).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove four countersunk
head screws (275), four countersunk finishing washers (280) and collect
the back bracket assembly (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disassemble the back
bracket assembly (270):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fastener (285) from the
back bracket assembly (270).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove six socket
head screws (295, 300, 300A), nine washers (305, 310), three self-locking
nuts (315) and collect the support assembly (290).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Disassemble the support
assembly (290):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fasteners (320, 325) from
the support bracket (330).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the support bracket (330).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove four socket
head screws (340, 345), two hexagon head screws (350), eight flat
washers (355, 360, 365), two self-locking nuts (370) and collect the
bracket assembly (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disassemble the bracket
assembly (335):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fasteners (375) from the
bracket assembly (335).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove three hexagon
head screws (385), three flat washers (390) and collect the bracket
assembly (380).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Disassemble the bracket
assembly (380):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fasteners (395) and collect
the bracket (400).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove two socket
cap head screws (410), two flat washers (415) and collect the attachment
bracket (405).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove nine socket head screws (425, 430),
four self-locking nuts (435), thirteen flat washers (440, 445) and
collect the top support assembly (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the closeout panel
assembly (450):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive loop fasteners (455, 465) from
the closeout panel assembly (445).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revst><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove the self-adhesive loop
fasteners (460) from the closeout panel assembly (450).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove the double-sided
tape (470) from the closeout panel assembly (450).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the rear closeout
assembly (475):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove the double-sided
tape (480) and and two bonded backshell bracket (482) from the rear
closeout assembly (475).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove the bonded
part magnet (476) and two bonded nutplate bracket (481) from the closeout
panel assembly (450).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the rear closeout
assembly (485):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part floor seal (490),
two magnets (496) from the rear closeout assembly (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Remove the bonded
part nutplate bracket (495) from the rear closeout assembly (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove two socket
cap head screws (505), two flat washers (510) and collect the back
bracket assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disassemble the back
bracket assembly (500):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release two quarter turn fasteners (520), two quarter turn receptacles
(525), two ejector springs (530), two quarter turn washers (535) and
collect the bracket (515).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove and disassemble
the sidewall closeout assembly (540):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove one socket cap head screw (550), one
flat washer (555) and collect the sidewall closeout (545).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bonded part p-seal (560) from
the sidewall closeout (545).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Collect the sidewall closeout (565).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove two socket
cap head screws (575), two flat washers (580) and collect the bracket
assembly (570).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disassemble the bracket
assembly (570):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-029-a01"></refint>) to
release one quarter turn screw (590), one quarter turn receptacle
(595), two ejector springs (600), one quarter turn washer (605) and
collect the bracket (585).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Remove four socket
cap head screws (615), four flat washers (620) and collect the decompression
vent install (610).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Disassemble the decompression
vent install (610):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the p-seal (625) from the decompression
panel (630).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove seven pop rivets (631), fourteen flat
washers (632) and collect the decompression panel (630).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT</para></caution>
<revst><para>Remove the self-adhesive hook fastener (635) from the
decompression panel (630).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="029"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-029-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 30):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Earth/ground stud assembly - remove one hexagon-head
bolt (30), one lock washer (25), two corrosion protective washers
(20) and one plain electrical nut (15) from the structure.</para>
<note><para>Self-locking nut (5) and the pressure washer (10) are
removed and retained during the disassembly of earth stud/ground assembly
in situ.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="040" seq="030"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-040-033-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Disassemble the Suite Identification Kit Assembly (Ref. IPL
Fig. 31):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the suite ID plate
assemblies (5, 30, 55, 80, 105, 130, 155, 180, 205, 230, 255, 280,
305, 330, 355, 380, 405, 430, 455, 480, 505, 530, 555, 580, 605, 630,
655, 680):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disengage and collect the suite ID plates
(10, 35, 60, 85, 110, 135, 160, 185, 210, 235, 260, 285, 310, 335,
360, 385, 410, 435, 460, 485, 510, 535, 560, 585, 610, 635, 660, 685).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If necessary, remove and collect the transfer
tapes (15, 40, 65, 90, 115, 140, 165, 190, 215, 240, 265, 290, 315,
340, 365, 390, 415, 440, 465, 490, 515, 540, 565, 590, 615, 640, 665,
690).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the double sided tapes (25, 50, 75,
100, 125, 150, 175, 200, 225, 250, 275, 300, 325, 350, 375, 400, 425,
450, 475, 500, 525, 550, 575, 600, 625, 650, 675, 700) and collect
the diffusers (20, 45, 70, 95, 120, 145, 170, 195, 220, 245, 270,
295, 320, 345, 370, 395, 420, 445, 470, 495, 520, 545, 570, 595, 620,
645, 670, 695).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-4000" revdate="20260617">
<title>CLEANING</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-100-801-a-01" revdate="20260617">
<title>General</title>
<topic>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED
FROM THE ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>DO THE PROCEDURES IN AN ESD AREA. WEAR MANUFACTURER'S
RECOMMENDED WRIST STRAP WHICH IS CONNECTED TO A SOFT GROUND. MAKE
SURE THAT THE WRIST STRAP TOUCHES THE SKIN. OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED,
OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED
BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This section specifies the procedures necessary
to clean the unit during workshop maintenance.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-100-802-a01" revdate="20260617">
<title>Cleaning</title>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Reason for the Job:</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>To keep the unit clean and serviceable.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
