<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Job Set-up:</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-001-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Plastic Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE
ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE
INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth to remove
collected dust.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with a weak solution of soapy water to remove dirt. If necessary,
use a soft brush to apply the solution on textured surfaces.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Dry the surface with a soft cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-002-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Metal Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE
ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE
INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth to remove
collected dust.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with water to remove dirt.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Dry with a soft cloth.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-003-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Electrical Components Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE
ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE
INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<warning><para>DO THE PROCEDURES IN AN ESD AREA. WEAR MANUFACTURER'S
RECOMMENDED WRIST STRAP WHICH IS CONNECTED TO A SOFT GROUND. MAKE
SURE THAT THE WRIST STRAP TOUCHES THE SKIN. OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<para>Remove dirt with a soft brush or a clean, dry, lint free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-004-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Leather Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth to remove
collected dust.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with a weak solution of soapy water to remove dirt.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Dry the surface with a soft cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-005-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Decorative Laminate Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<warning><para>WHEN CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with water to remove dirt.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Dry with a soft cloth.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with a weak solution of soapy water to remove dirt.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Dry with a soft cloth.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-006-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Painted Surfaces Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<warning><para>WHEN CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<caution><para>AFTER A SURFACE IS painted DO NOT CLEAN FOR A MINIMUM
OF fourteen days. THIS WILL PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with water to remove dirt.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Dry with a soft cloth.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with a weak solution of soapy water to remove dirt.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Dry with a soft cloth.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-007-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Cleaning Adhesive Fastbond 2000:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Overspray can be removed while still wet
with clean soapy water.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<caution><para>OBEY THE MANUFACTURER'S INSTRUCTIONS WHEN YOU USE CLEANER/THINNERS.
TOO MUCH USE CAN CAUSE STAINING.</para></caution>
<para>Adhesive which has dried can be removed with cleaner/thinner
(T160) and a lint free cloth.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-008-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Loose Covers Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>obey THE manufacturers instructions for loose cover
cleaning and limitations on the number of cleaning cycles. if you
do not obey these instructions, damage to the covers can occur.</para>
</caution>
<para>Clean the loose covers as specified by the manufacturer. Refer
to Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-011-a01">table-25-26-62-99a-011-a01
</refint> for manufacturer information.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-009-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Table Assembly Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Fully deploy the table assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use a lint free cloth to remove any dirt
or debris from the table assembly and slide mechanism.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do a check for FOD in the table cassette.
Remove any FOD if necessary, refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-26-62-1000"></refint>.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Fully stow the table assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-010-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Nomex Fabric Surface Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<warning><para>WHEN CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT YOU DO NOT USE THE TALLOW SOAP, STARCH
AND FABRIC SOFTENERS. THE USE OF TALLOW SOAP, STARCH AND FABRIC SOFTENERS
WILL LEAVE A FILM OR COATING ON THE FABRIC. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS
INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT YOU DO NOT USE THE FIBRE SHEDDING CLOTH
OR SPONGE. THE USE OF FIBRE SHEDDING CLOTH OR SPONGE CAN LEAVE LINT
ON THE FABRIC SURFACE. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT YOU DO NOT USE THE CHLORINE BLEACH,
HIGH PH AND TOO MUCH HOT WATER. THE USE OF CHLORINE BLEACH, HIGH PH
AND TOO MUCH HOT WATER WILL WEAKEN THE FABRIC AND ACCELERATE COLOUR
BLEED AND LOSS. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean the nomex fabric surface as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a wet soft cloth or
sponge made moist with water to remove dirt.</para>
<note><para>Use soft low alkalinity, hot water up to 140 &ordm;F (60
&ordm;C) max mixed with soapy water.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that enough water left in the soft
cloth or sponge to wet the nomex surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Carefully, clean the surface.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that you do not wet the nomex surface
with too much water.</para>
<note><para>The use of more water can cause the distort to the fabric
surface and de-laminate from the surface.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the absorbent paper towel to remove unwanted
water from the nomex surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use a new absorbent paper towel, once the
absorbent paper towel has reached its max absorbency.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply light even motion with the absorbent
paper towel, on the nomex surface to remove the unwanted water from
the surface. Do not scrub or rub the surface.</para>
<note><para>The use of scrub or more rub motion on the surface, can
cause paper towels to disintegrate and fibre contamination on the
surface.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Repeat the above steps until the surface
is cleaned fully.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Wash the nomex fabric surface as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Wash the surface with soft low alkalinity
water with temperature up to 122 &ordm;F (50 &ordm;C) max.</para>
<note><para>Do not use soapy water to wash the nomex surface.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a wet soft cloth or
sponge made moist with water to remove dirt.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that enough water left in the soft
cloth or sponge to wet the nomex surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Carefully, clean the surface.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that you do not wet the nomex surface
with too much water.</para>
<note><para>The use of more water can cause the distort to the fabric
surface and de-laminate from the surface.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the absorbent paper towel to remove unwanted
water from the nomex surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use a new absorbent paper towel, once the
absorbent paper towel has reached its max absorbency.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply a light even motion with the absorbent
paper towel, on the nomex surface to remove the unwanted water from
the surface. Do not scrub or rub the surface.</para>
<note><para>The use of scrub or rub motion on the surface, can cause
paper towels to disintegrate and fibre contamination on the surface.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Repeat the above steps until the surface
is cleaned fully.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Replace the water with soft low alkalinity
water with temperature of 86 &ordm;F (30 &ordm;C) and wash it again.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a wet soft cloth or
sponge made moist with water to remove dirt.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that enough water left in the soft
cloth or sponge to wet the nomex surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Carefully, clean the surface.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that you do not wet the nomex surface
with too much water.</para>
<note><para>The use of more water can cause the distort to the fabric
surface and de-laminate from the surface.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the absorbent paper towel to remove unwanted
water from the nomex surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use a new absorbent paper towel, once the
absorbent paper towel has reached its max absorbency.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply a light even motion with the absorbent
paper towel, on the nomex surface to remove the unwanted water from
the surface. Do not scrub or rub the surface.</para>
<note><para>The use of scrub or rub motion on the surface, can cause
paper towels to disintegrate and fibre contamination on the surface.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Dry the nomex fabric surface as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Dry the nomex fabric with the help of absorbent
paper towel.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>USE LOW HEAT AND PREVENT USE OF TOO MUCH HEAT WHEN
YOU DRY THE NOMEX SURFACE. THE USE OF TOO MUCH HEAT CAN CAUSE THE
COLOUR CHANGE AND COLOUR LOSS ON THE SURFACE.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT OVER DRY THE NOMEX SURFACE, IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE UNIT CAN OCCUR.</para></caution>
<para>If necessary, use a hair dryer set to low heat, to dry the nomex
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="100" seq="011"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-100-011-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Isovolta AIRDEC Decorative Laminate Cleaning Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The cleaning procedure is applicable only
for the Isovolta decor laminate products, as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>AIRDEC-F series,</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>AIRDEC-G series,</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>AIRDEC-1E,</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>AIRDEC-X1,</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>AIRDEC-plus.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<caution><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, YOU MUST
USE A SOFT CLOTH WITH LIGHT PRESSURE TO PREVENT OVER POLISH THE STAINED
AREA. THIS WILL HELP TO PREVENT THE GLOSSY APPEARANCE OF THE CLEANING
SURFACE.</para></caution>
<caution><para>IT IS RECOMMENDED TO TEST THE SOLVENTS AND CLEANING
AGENTS BEFORE USE. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A
RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE THE ABRASIVE CLEANING AGENT. IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Cleaning procedure:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth to remove
collected dust.</para>
<note><para>The procedure to remove the stains from Isovolta AIRDEC
decorative laminates depends upon the staining agent.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Light stain:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with clean water to remove dirt and light stain, such as coffee,
tea and red wine etc.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Medium stain:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with a weak solution of soapy water to remove the medium stains,
such as lipstick and ballpoint pen ink etc.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with a soft cloth made
moist with clean water to remove dirt.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Heavy stains:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Clean the surface with solvent type cleaning
agent to remove the heavy stains, such as color marks, brown shoe
polish, adhesive and paint etc.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Clean the decorative laminate surface as
specified by the manufacturer. Refer to Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-26-62-99a-074-a01"></refint> for approved solvents
and cleaning agent information.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Dry the surface with a soft cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-5000" revdate="20260318">
<title>INSPECTION/CHECK</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-200-801-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>General</title>
<topic>
<title>Inspection/Check Procedures:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="99A" seq="063"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" id="table-25-26-62-99a-063-a01"><?Pub Lcl
_tabindent="1">
<title>Inspection/Check Procedures</title>
<tgroup cols="1" align="left" charoff="50" char="">
<?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="4.87in"?>
<colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.47*">
<thead valign="bottom">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center">
<para>INSPECTION/CHECK PROCEDURES</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody valign="top">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Electrical Equipment Visual Inspection</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Seat and Furniture Visual Inspection</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Foreign Object Debris (FOD) Visual Inspection</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Table Assembly Visual Inspection</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Radio Frequency Identification (RFID) Tag Check</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>EPF System Visual Inspection</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-200-802-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Visual Inspection</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To visually examine the unit for damage or
unserviceable parts.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-200-001-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Electrical Equipment Visual Inspection:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE
ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE
INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<warning><para>DO THE PROCEDURES IN AN ESD AREA. WEAR MANUFACTURER'S
RECOMMENDED WRIST STRAP WHICH IS CONNECTED TO A SOFT GROUND. MAKE
SURE THAT THE WRIST STRAP TOUCHES THE SKIN. OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<para>Visually examine electrical cables and harnesses for:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Damage because of trapping, pinching or scuffing.
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Too much strain on cables.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Support at correct intervals.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Permitted tension to prevent damage with
unit structure.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that the harness connector spring
clips and retainer (if applicable) are in position.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>When LRUs or IFE components are replaced,
make sure that an additional protection of sleeves is provided for
the connectors and pigtails of the LRUs and IFE components.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE
ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE
INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<warning><para>DO THE PROCEDURES IN AN ESD AREA. WEAR MANUFACTURER'S
RECOMMENDED WRIST STRAP WHICH IS CONNECTED TO A SOFT GROUND. MAKE
SURE THAT THE WRIST STRAP TOUCHES THE SKIN. OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<para>Visually examine electrical components for:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Damage to insulation, casings or mountings.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Signs of overheating, burning or cracking.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Loose connections.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-200-002-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Seat and Furniture Visual Inspection:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Visually examine dress covers:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Examine dress covers for signs of wear or
damage.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Replace defective dress covers which do not
meet the necessary standard.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Visually examine cushion foams:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Examine cushion foams for signs of wear or
damage.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Make sure that cushion foams give good support.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Cushions are to lose no more than:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>50% of their initial compression.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>25% of their initial height.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Replace defective cushion foams which do
not meet the necessary standard.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-200-003-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Foreign Object Debris (FOD) Visual Inspection:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE
ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE
INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<para>Examine the furniture, seat and furniture mechanism, to make
sure that there is no FOD.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Examine between the seat and the furniture
adjacent to the seat, to make sure that there is no FOD.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If applicable, make sure that all FOD prevention
devices are in position and correctly installed.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-200-004-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Table Assembly Visual Inspection:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deploy the table assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do a visual check of the table assembly for
Foreign Object Debris (FOD) and dirt.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Make sure that the surfaces where the table
moves are carefully examined.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If found, remove FOD and clean the table
assembly, refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-26-62-4000">
pgblk-25-26-62-4000</refint> for cleaning procedures.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Stow the table assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="803"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-200-803-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Radio Frequency Identification (RFID) Tag Check</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To collect indentifcation information from
parts or assemblies with RFID tags installed.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Tools, Fixtures and Equipment:</para>
<note><para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="vendlist-25-26-62"></refint> for
vendor addresses.</para></note>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="25" subjnbr="00" func="99A" seq="013"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" id="table-25-25-00-99a-013-a01"><?Pub Lcl
_tabindent="1">
<title>Tools, Fixtures and Equipment</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="left" charoff="50" char="">
<?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="12.00in"?>
<colspec colname="col2" colwidth="1.18*">
<colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.43*">
<colspec colname="col4" colwidth="1.39*">
<thead valign="bottom">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center">
<para>REFERENCE AND/OR PART NUMBER</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center">
<para>DESCRIPTION AND/OR SPECIFICATION</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center">
<para>SUPPLIER CODE OR NAME AND ADDRESS</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody valign="top">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>MC9090-Z</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Handheld RFID reader</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>V7H229</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Consumables:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use the Handheld RFID reader to collect and
record the RFID data from the part or assembly. Refer to manufacturer
instructions to operate the RFID reader.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="804"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-200-804-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>EPF System Visual Inspection</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To visually examine the EPF system.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>EPF System Visual Inspection:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Do a visual check of the EPF system.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>In the event of a failure of the primary
slide mechanism of the suite door, make sure that you apply a small
amount of additional force to move the suite door back as normal operation.
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If the door operates correctly with the help
of primary slide mechanism the EPF button will be sub-flush.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If the primary slide mechanism has failed
and the EPF system has been activated, the EPF button will pop-out
and stay above the bezel.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>In the event of a failure of the primary
slide mechanism, the main carriage block assembly (16-100) will separate
from the EPF system bracket spigot block assembly (16-165), this will
activate the EPF button (16-320) on outside of the suite door.</para>
<note><para>When the EPF button activated, the door will slide on
a roller to move the door back to TTL position.</para></note>
<note><para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-26-62-8000"></refint> pageblock of this manual, for
EPF system re-set procedure.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="200" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-26-62-200-001-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>EPF SYSTEM VISUAL INSPECTION</title>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-INSP-5001-01-00.cgm" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-200-001-a01-1" revdate="20260318"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-INSP-5001-02-00.cgm" sheetnbr="2" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-200-001-a01-2" revdate="20260318"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-6000" revdate="20260617">
<title>REPAIR</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-300-801-a-01" revdate="20260617">
<title><?Pub Lcl _foottit="REPAIR GENERAL">General</title>
<topic>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>ONLY APPROVED PERSONS WITH THE NECESSARY
SKILLS can complete THE repair PROCEDURES IN THIS MANUAL.</para>
</caution>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Replace the parts that do not meet inspection
standards and are not applicable for repair.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN surtec 650 is USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use a brush or pen applicator to apply a protective layer of
Surtec 650 to all aluminium surfaces that are rough or damaged. For
the correct application of Surtec 650, obey the manufacturer instructions
(VU0PK2). Refer to<refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="vendlist-25-26-62"></refint> for
vendor address.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use standard workshop procedures to make
minor repairs on sheet metal and riveted assemblies.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To stitch seams that have opened on upholstery,
use an applicable needle and nylon thread.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For structural repairs other than listed
contact Safran Seats GB Limited.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Repair Procedures:</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="99A" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" id="table-25-26-62-99a-002-a01"><?Pub Lcl
_tabindent="1">
<title>Repair Procedures</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="left" charoff="50" char="">
<?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="12.00in"?>
<colspec colname="col2" colwidth="1.00*">
<colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.47*">
<thead valign="bottom">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center">
<para>REPAIR NUMBER</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top" align="center">
<para>DESCRIPTION</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody valign="top">
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Repair 1</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Double-sided Tape</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Repair 2</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rowsep="1" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Hook, Loop and Duotec Fastener</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Repair 3</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Inserts</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Repair 4</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Composite Honeycomb Panels</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Repair 5</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Decorative Laminate</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Repair 6</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="0" rotate="0" valign="top">
<para>Paint</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Repair Procedures:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>When an approved repair is made which involves
to add or remove material, the repair number must be put on the component
or part (by painting, etching, engraving, etc.) to show that it has
been modified.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The repair number must be positioned as close
to the manufacturer's part number as possible and can be an appendix
to this number.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the Record of Repair to record all repairs
done to the unit. Refer to table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-26-62-99a-021-a01"></refint>.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<?eval =v1612x(75)?>
<?eval +1?x(75)[?pb?]?>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
