<topic>
<title>Repair 1-1. Repair of joints made with double-sided tape:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-001-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Removal of double-sided tape:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use a craft knife to cut through the double-sided
tape while the parts are disassembled.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Remove remaining double-sided tape with a lint free cloth made
moist with a weak solution of soapy water or with Isopropyl alcohol.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Installation of double-sided tape:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN adhesives ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive (S708) to the areas
to have double-sided tape attached and let the adhesive to dry for
a minimum of 30 minutes.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Cut the double-sided tape to the correct
length.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the backing paper from one side of
the double-sided tape. Attach the tape to the part in the correct
position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the backing paper from the other side
of the double-sided tape and assemble the parts together.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tape and leave to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
