<topic>
<title>Repair 2-1. Sew on hook and loop fastener attached to fabric:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-002-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Cut the thread and remove the old hook and
loop fastener.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use an applicable needle and thread of the
correct colour to sew the new hook and loop fastener onto the fabric.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Repair 2-2. Self-adhesive hook and loop fastener attached to
structure:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-003-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to soak the hook
and loop fastener that is bonded to the structure.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the hook and loop fastener from the
structure.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove remaining adhesive and clean the surface
of the structure with Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN adhesives ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive (S708) to the structure
and let the adhesive to dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If required, cut the self-adhesive hook and
loop fastener to the correct length.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the backing paper and push the hook
and loop fastener on to the structure.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Remove unwanted adhesive with Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free
cloth.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Let the adhesive cure for a minimum of 12
hours.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Repair 2-3. Self-adhesive duotec fastener attached to structure:</title>
