<topic>
<title>Repair 4-1. Composite Honeycomb Panel Repair, Top Skin Damaged
Without Holes (Ref. Fig. 6002):</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-007-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>General:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>you must contact safran seats gb LIMITED to make sure
that the DAMAGE IS in a location which is applicable for this repair.
IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE
UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>This repair is for damage to the top skin of the panel of less
than 76.20 mm (3.00 in) in diameter and 1.00 mm (0.040 in) deep. The
damage must be a minimum of 304.80 mm (12.00 in) away from other areas
of damage. For damage out of permitted areas, contact Safran Seats
GB Limited.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>It is possible that the finished repair will
not be to the initial production quality standard.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-008-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For damaged panels with decorative laminate:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN DAMAGED DECORATIVE laminate IS CUT AWAY, MAKE
SURE THAT THE COMPOSITE PANEL IS NOT DAMAGED.</para></caution>
<caution><para>WHEN THE HEAT GUN IS USED, APPLY HEAT GRADUALLY. TOO
MUCH HEAT WILL DAMAGE THE COMPOSITE HONEYCOMB PANEL.</para></caution>
<para>Cut a rectangle around the area to be repaired. From one corner
apply heat from the heat gun and carefully remove the decorative laminate
from the panel.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For damaged panels with a painted surface:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove paint back to the surface of the composite.
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Clean the area to be repaired with Isopropyl alcohol and a lint
free cloth.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use grade 240 abrasive paper on the area
to be repaired, to give a key for the repair paste.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN adhesives and repair materials ARE USED, OBEY
ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED
BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Mix together two part adhesive (AW2104 opaque base and HY4076
pale yellow hardener).</para>
<note><para>To mix together the adhesive: add 100 parts by weight
of base to 40 parts by weight of hardener and mix together. Make sure
that when mixed the compounds are a constant colour.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Add the same amount of shredded glass cloth
(AMF5-1-7781) to the same amount of prepared adhesive (AW2104/HY4076)
and mix to make a paste.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Fill the damaged area with the paste. Make
sure that the paste fills the dent fully.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Let the paste cure for 12 hours at 23 deg
C (73 deg F).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use grade 150 abrasive paper to get a smooth
finish on the repair.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For repaired panels with decorative laminate:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply decorative laminate to the repaired
panel, refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="task-25-26-62-300-806-a01">task-25-26-62-300-806-a01</refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For repaired panels with a painted surface:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply paint to the repaired panel, refer
to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="task-25-26-62-300-807-a01">task-25-26-62-300-807-a01
</refint>.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26"
subjnbr="62" func="99B" seq="114" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="6000" chg="u" key="graphic-25-26-62-99b-114-a01"
revdate="20260617">
<title>COMPOSITE HONEYCOMB PANEL REPAIR, TOP SKIN DAMAGED WITHOUT
HOLES</title>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6002-01-00.cgm" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-114-a01-1" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Repair 4-2. Composite Honeycomb Panel, Top Skin Delamination
(Ref. Fig. 6003):</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-009-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>General:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>you must contact safran seats gb LIMITED to make sure
THAT the DAMAGE IS in a location which is applicable for this repair.
IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE
UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>This repair is for damage to the top skin of the panel of less
than 76.20 mm (3.00 in) in diameter. The damage must be a minimum
of 304.80 mm (12.00 in) away from other areas of damage. For damage
out of permitted areas, contact Safran Seats GB Limited.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>It is possible that the finished repair will
not be to the initial production quality standard.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-010-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For damaged panels with decorative laminate:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN DAMAGED DECORATIVE laminate IS CUT AWAY, MAKE
SURE that THE COMPOSITE PANEL IS NOT DAMAGED.</para></caution>
<caution><para>WHEN THE HEAT GUN IS USED, APPLY HEAT GRADUALLY. TOO
MUCH HEAT WILL DAMAGE THE COMPOSITE HONEYCOMB PANEL.</para></caution>
<para>Cut a rectangle around the area to be repaired. From one corner
apply heat from the heat gun and carefully remove the decorative laminate
from the panel.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For damaged panels with a painted surface:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Identify the area to be repaired with a felt
tip marker.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Drill a series of 2.50 mm (0.10 in) holes
approximately 25.00 mm (1.00 in) apart, through the panel top skin
only.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN adhesives ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Mix two part adhesive (AW2104/HY4076):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Add 100 parts by weight of AW2104 opaque
base to 40 parts by weight of HY4076 pale yellow hardener. Make sure
that the mixed adhesive is a constant colour.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Put the panel in a vertical position and
fill the top holes with two part adhesive. Make sure that the adhesive
flows from the bottom holes and all the holes are filled.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive and cover the area
with release film.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply a light pressure equally on the repair
area with applicable clamps.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Put the panel in a horizontal position with
the injected top skin down. Let the adhesive cure for 12 hours at
23 deg C (73 deg F).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use grade 150 abrasive paper to get a smooth
finish of the repair.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For repaired panels with decorative laminate:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply decorative laminate to the repaired
panel, refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="task-25-26-62-300-806-a01">task-25-26-62-300-806-a01</refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For repaired panels with a painted surface:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply paint to the repaired panel, refer
to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="task-25-26-62-300-807-a01">task-25-26-62-300-807-a01
</refint>.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26"
subjnbr="62" func="99B" seq="115" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="6000" chg="u" key="graphic-25-26-62-99b-115-a01"
revdate="20260617">
<title>COMPOSITE HONEYCOMB PANEL, TOP SKIN DELAMINATION REPAIR</title>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6003-01-00.cgm" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-115-a01-1" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
