<topic>
<title>Repair 5-1. Laminate Scratches or Cuts:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="011"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-011-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>General:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This repair is for small areas of damaged
decorative laminate contained in a maximum area of 76.20 mm x 76.20
mm (3.00 in x 3.00 in). The damaged decorative laminate must be a
minimum of 304.80 mm (12.00 in) away from other areas of damage. For
damage out of permitted areas, contact Safran Seats GB Limited.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>It is possible that the finished repair will
not be to the initial production quality standard.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="012"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-012-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN Touch up paint and paint repair pens ARE USED,
OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED
BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use a small paint brush or paint repair pen to apply an equivalent
colour paint to the decorative laminate. Obey the manufacturers instructions.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, the repair can be blended in
before the repair paint has dried:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use a pinch roller and push a piece of laminate
material of the same texture on to the repaired area.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Repair 5-2. Laminate With Heat Activated Adhesive:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="013"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-015-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>General:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This repair is for small areas of damaged
decorative laminate contained in a maximum area of 76.20 mm x 76.20
mm (3.00 in x 3.00 in). The damaged decorative laminate must be a
minimum of 304.80 mm (12.00 in) away from other areas of damage. For
damage out of permitted areas, contact Safran Seats GB Limited.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>It is possible that the finished repair will
not be to the initial production quality standard.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Replace decorative laminate on flat and single
curved surfaces only. Special equipment is necessary for decorative
laminate replacement on compound curved surfaces.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="014"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-115-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Cut a repair patch of decorative laminate
with heat activated adhesive.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Put the repair patch on the damaged area,
apply masking tape to hold in position if necessary.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN DAMAGED DECORATIVE LAMINATE IS CUT AWAY, MAKE
SURE THAT THE COMPOSITE PANEL IS NOT DAMAGED.</para></caution>
<para>Cut a rectangle through the repair patch and through the damaged
laminate. Be careful not to cause damage to the composite panel.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Collect the repair patch and remove the inner
cut rectangle to be used for the repair.</para>
<note><para>The cut repair patch rectangle will be the same dimensions
as the laminate cut out from the panel.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN THE HEAT GUN IS USED, APPLY HEAT GRADUALLY. TOO
MUCH HEAT WILL DAMAGE THE COMPOSITE HONEYCOMB PANEL.</para></caution>
<para>Remove the rectangle of damaged decorative laminate from the
panel. If necessary, carefully apply heat with a heat gun from one
corner of the damaged laminate.</para>
<note><para>If there is structural damage to the composite panel,
contact Safran Seats GB Limited.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Remove remaining adhesive and clean the surface of the panel
with iso-propyl alcohol and a lint free cloth.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THEMANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use a paint brush to apply contact adhesive (Fastbond 2000)
to the panel area to be repaired. Do not apply contact adhesive to
the repair patch.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Wait for the contact adhesive contact adhesive
to dry and become translucent (approximately 30 minutes).</para>
<note><para>When the contact adhesive has dried, the repair patch
must be bonded in less than 4 hours.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If attached, remove protective backing paper
or liner from the repair patch.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Align the repair patch and put in position
on the panel.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN THE HEAT GUN IS USED, APPLY HEAT GRADUALLY. TOO
MUCH HEAT WILL DAMAGE THE COMPOSITE HONEYCOMB PANEL.</para></caution>
<para>Use a heat gun and pinch roller to gradually apply heat and
pressure to the repair patch.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Continue gradually with heat and pressure
for approximately two minutes until the adhesive is activated and
the repair patch bonded.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, bond the overlapping edges
of the trimmed panels with adhesive S708.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the repair patch
and leave to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Clean the repaired area with iso-propyl alcohol and a lint free
cloth.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, the repair area edges can be
finished with an applicable touch up paint, refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="task-25-26-62-300-807-a01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300"
seq="001" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-26-62-300-001-a01" revdate="20260617">
<title>DECORATIVE LAMINATE REPAIR, LAMINATE WITH HEAT ACTIVATED ADHESIVE</title>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6004-01-00.cgm" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-300-001-a01-1" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6004-02-00.cgm" sheetnbr="2" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-300-001-a01-2" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6004-03-00.cgm" sheetnbr="3" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-300-001-a01-3" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6004-04-00.cgm" sheetnbr="4" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-300-001-a01-4" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="807"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-300-807-a01" revdate="20260617">
<title><?Pub Lcl _foottit="REPAIR 6">Repair 6. Painted Surfaces</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To repair damaged paint.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Repair 6-1. Small Areas of Damaged Paint.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Repair 6. Tools, Fixtures and Equipment:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Repair 6. Consumables:</para>
