</topic>
<topic>
<title>Repair 6-1. Small Areas of Damaged Paint (Ref. Fig. 6004):</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="015"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-013-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>General:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This repair is for small areas of damaged
paint contained in a maximum area of 76.20 mm x 76.20 mm (3.00 in
x 3.00 in). The damaged paint must be a minimum of 304.80 mm (12.00
in) away from other areas of damage. For damage out of permitted areas,
contact Safran Seats GB Limited.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>It is possible that the finished repair will
not be to the initial production quality standard.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="300" seq="016"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-300-014-a01" revdate="20260617"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN paints, primers and fillers are used, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<caution><para>dO NOT CLEAN THE REPAIRED AREA FOR 48 HOURS.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove paint back to the surface of the material.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Prepare the surface, obey the paint manufacturers
instructions.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply a layer of primer, refer to table <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-045-a01">table-25-26-62-99a-045-a01
</refint>. Obey the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Prepare the surface, obey the paint manufacturers
instructions.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If applicable, apply a layer of base coat
paint, refer to table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-26-62-99a-045-a01">table-25-26-62-99a-045-a01</refint>.
Obey the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Prepare the surface, obey the paint manufacturers
instructions.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply a layer of top coat paint, refer to
table <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-045-a01">table-25-26-62-99a-045-a01
</refint>. Obey the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Finish the surface, obey the paint manufacturers
instructions.</para></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26"
subjnbr="62" func="99B" seq="110" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="6000" chg="u" key="graphic-25-26-62-99b-110-a01"
revdate="20260617">
<title>PAINT LOCATIONS</title>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6005-01-00.cgm" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-110-a01-1" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6005-02-00.cgm" sheetnbr="2" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-110-a01-2" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6005-03-00.cgm" sheetnbr="3" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-110-a01-3" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-REP-6005-04-00.cgm" sheetnbr="4" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-99b-110-a01-4" revdate="20260617"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="7000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-7000" revdate="20261016">
<title>ASSEMBLY</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="400" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-400-801-a01" revdate="20260617">
<title>General</title>
<topic>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM
THE ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY approved PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE
INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>DO THE PROCEDURES IN AN ESD AREA. WEAR MANUFACTURER'S
RECOMMENDED WRIST STRAP WHICH IS CONNECTED TO A SOFT GROUND. MAKE
SURE THAT THE WRIST STRAP TOUCHES THE SKIN. OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS
ARE TO BE WORN DURING ASSEMBLY. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION
THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>DO NOT push or pull the unit ACROSS FLOOR
SURFACES. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE
TO THE UNIT OR to THE floor SURFACES.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING ASSEMBLY, IF
YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE
UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT THERE IS A GAP BETWEEN THE
ACTUATOR AND THE SUITE STRUCTURE. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION
THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT THERE IS A GAP BETWEEN THE
ACTUATOR MOVING PARTS, THE ELECTRICAL HARNESSES AND THE SUITE STRUCTURE.
IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE
UNIT.</para></caution>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Before assembly, make sure that all necessary
maintenance procedures have been completed.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attaching parts with wear or damage must
be replaced before assembly.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If hook and loop fasteners or double-sided
tape must be replaced, refer to the <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-26-62-6000"></refint> pageblock.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>When Loctite thread locking compound is used,
apply Loctite activator unless assembly procedure instructions are
different. Refer to table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-26-62-99a-003-a01"></refint>.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>A full list of fasteners with specified torque
values is given in the <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-26-62-8000"></refint> pageblock.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>When fasteners are hand tightened make sure that you
do not tighten too much. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>When torque values are not specified, the parts are to be &ldquo;hand
tightened&rdquo;:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>You must make sure that each of the mating
surfaces are fully together and cannot turn and are not loose.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>You must think about the material type, for
example soft trim or plastic parts.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For adjustment procedures, refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-26-62-1000"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For LRU installation procedures refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-26-62-13000"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The numbers in brackets, for example (125),
refer to an item number in the IPL. The figure of the IPL is given
at the start of each section.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Where the numbers in brackets have a number
before the item, for example (10-125), this refers to an item number
in a different figure in the IPL. For this example, &ldquo;10&rdquo;
refers to the IPL figure and &ldquo;125&rdquo; to the item in that
figure.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For LRU connectors that have been removed,
do a visual inspection for pushed back, corroded, unseated or misaligned
pins/sockets before you connect the connector. This is to make sure
that the bonding system has been reconnected through correct mating
of the pin /sockets.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If you replace any label or placard that
has information fields to be completed, use a solvent resistant marker
pen to copy all relevant information to the new label or placard.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>When LRUs or IFE components are replaced,
make sure that an additional protection of sleeves is provided for
the connectors and pigtails of the LRUs and IFE components.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>During assembly, the actuator must be properly
adjusted with the suite structure to make sure of the full privacy
screen movement.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Make sure that the override cable is installed
into the override mechanism and adjust the override cable correctly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="400" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="r"
key="task-25-26-62-400-802-a01" revdate="20261016">
<chgdesc>CHANGED ASSEMBLY PROCEDURE</chgdesc>
<title>Assemble the Unit</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To assemble the unit after maintenance procedures.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
