<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="037"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-440-037-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Suite Identification Kit Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig.
31):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the suite ID plate assemblies
(5, 30, 55, 80, 105, 130, 155, 180, 205, 230, 255, 280, 305, 330,
355, 380, 405, 430, 455, 480, 505, 530, 555, 580, 605, 630, 655, 680):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the diffusers (20, 45, 70, 95, 120,
145, 170, 195, 220, 245, 270, 295, 320, 345, 370, 395, 420, 445, 470,
495, 520, 545, 570, 595, 620, 645, 670, 695) with the double sided
tapes (25, 50, 75, 100, 125, 150, 175, 200, 225, 250, 275, 300, 325,
350, 375, 400, 425, 450, 475, 500, 525, 550, 575, 600, 625, 650, 675,
700).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT DOUBLE SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN THE
CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<revend><para>Attach the double sided tapes (25, 50, 75, 100, 125,
150, 175, 200, 225, 250, 275, 300, 325, 350, 375, 400, 425, 450, 475,
500, 525, 550, 575, 600, 625, 650, 675, 700) to the diffusers (20,
45, 70, 95, 120, 145, 170, 195, 220, 245, 270, 295, 320, 345, 370,
395, 420, 445, 470, 495, 520, 545, 570, 595, 620, 645, 670, 695) as
follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
double sided tapes (25, 50, 75, 100, 125, 150, 175, 200, 225, 250,
275, 300, 325, 350, 375, 400, 425, 450, 475, 500, 525, 550, 575, 600,
625, 650, 675, 700) and to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the double sided tapes (25,
50, 75, 100, 125, 150, 175, 200, 225, 250, 275, 300, 325, 350, 375,
400, 425, 450, 475, 500, 525, 550, 575, 600, 625, 650, 675, 700) in
position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the double sided
tapes (25, 50, 75, 100, 125, 150, 175, 200, 225, 250, 275, 300, 325,
350, 375, 400, 425, 450, 475, 500, 525, 550, 575, 600, 625, 650, 675,
700).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the transfer tapes (15,
40, 65, 90, 115, 140, 165, 190, 215, 240, 265, 290, 315, 340, 365,
390, 415, 440, 465, 490, 515, 540, 565, 590, 615, 640, 665, 690).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the suite ID plates (10, 35, 60, 85,
110, 135, 160, 185, 210, 235, 260, 285, 310, 335, 360, 385, 410, 435,
460, 485, 510, 535, 560, 585, 610, 635, 660, 685).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-001-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 30):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Earth/ground stud assembly - Install one
hexagon-head bolt (30) and one lock washer (25) on structure. Install
two corrosion protective washers (20) and one plain electrical nut
(15) on bolt.</para>
<note><para>Self-locking nut (5) and pressure washer (10) are attached
during assembly of earth ground/stud assembly in situ.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-037-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Rear Row Closeout Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 29):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble the decompression
vent install (610):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fastener
(635) to the decompression panel (630) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive hook fastener (635) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the the self-adhesive hook fastener
(635) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fastener (635).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the decompression panel (630) with
seven pop rivets (631) and fourteen flat washers (632).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the p-seal (625) to the decompression
panel (630).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the decompression
vent install (610) with four socket cap head screws (615) and four
flat washers (620).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble the bracket
assembly (570):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-028-a01"></refint>) to
attach the bracket (585) with one quarter turn screw (590), one quarter
turn receptacle (595), two ejector springs (600) and one quarter turn
washer (605).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the bracket
assembly (570) with two socket cap head screws (575) and two flat
washers (580).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble and attach
the sidewall closeout assembly (540):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the sidewall closeout (565).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 401 (with Primer 770) to the bonded
part p-seal (560). Attach the p-seal (560) to the sidewall closeout
(565).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 16 deg C (60 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the sidewall closeout (545) with one
socket cap head screw (550) and one flat washer (555).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble the back
bracket assembly (500):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-028-a01"></refint>) to
install two quarter turn fasteners (520), two quarter turn receptacles
(525), two ejector springs (530), two quarter turn washers (535) and
attach the bracket (515).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the back bracket assembly (500) with
two socket cap head screws (505) and two flat washers (510).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the rear closeout assembly
(485):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the magnet (496) to the rear closeout
(485).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded parts nutplate bracket (495), magnet (496)
to the rear closeout (485) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the bonded parts to the rear closeout
(485) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded parts floor seal (490) to the rear closeout
(485) with adhesive Loctite 406 with primer 770.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the bonded parts magnet bracket
(497) to the rear closeout (485) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the rear closeout assembly
(475):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and the bonded surface of the rear closeout assembly (475).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the bonded
part magnets (476) to the rear closeout assembly (475) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT DOUBLE SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN THE
CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the double-sided tape (480) to
the rear closeout assembly (475) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
double sided tape (480) and to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the double sided tape (480) in
position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the double sided
tape (480).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the bonded parts nutplate bracket
(481) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the bonded parts nutplate bracket
(481), backshell bracket (482) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the closeout panel assembly
(450):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT DOUBLE SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN THE
CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the double sided tape (470) to
the closeout panel assembly (450) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
double sided tape (470) and to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the double sided tape (470) in
position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the double sided
tape (470).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the bonded parts back plate (471)
with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(455, 465) to the closeout panel assembly (450) as follows:</para>
