<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
double-sided tape (365) and to the bonded surface(350).</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the double-sided tape (365) in
position on to the bonded surface (350).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tape (365).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the cover assembly (330):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(345) to the cover assembly (330) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (345) and to the bonded surface(330).</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(345) in position on to the bonded surface(330).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para> Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (345).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the transfer tape (340) to the cover
assembly (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one diffuser (335) to the cover assembly
(330).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cover assembly (330) to the canopy
installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the aisle capping assembly (225):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(325) to the aisle capping assembly (225) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (325) and to the bonded surface(225).</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(325) in position on to the bonded surface(225).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para> Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (325).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the capping (320) to the aisle capping
assembly (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the top capping bracket (305):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN THE
CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach two double-sided tapes (315) to the top capping bracket
assembly (305) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
double-sided tapes (315) and to the bonded surface(305).</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the double-sided tapes (315)
in position on to the bonded surface(305).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (315).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the top capping bracket equipped (305)
with six hexagon head screws (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the top capping epf aux rail (295)
with four hexagon head screws (300).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the base aisle capping (280) with
three hexagon head screws (285) and three flat washers (290).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the cover (275) with the adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (270)
to the aisle capping assembly (225) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (270) and to the bonded surface(225).</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(270) in position on to the bonded surface(225).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (270).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (255) with one
hexagon head screw (260) and one flat washer (265).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the aisle capping assembly (225) with
four hexagon head screws (230), four countersunk head screws (235,
240), eight flat washers (245) and four hexagon self lock nuts (250).
Torque the hexagon screws (230) to 24.0 Nm (17.70 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one doubler (220) to the canopy installation.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the sub canopy assembly (190) with
six hexagon head screws (195, 200), eleven flat washers (205, 210)
and five hexagon self lock nuts (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1G, 1J and 1L: Attach the
electrical bracket assembly (180) with two countersunk head screws
(185).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1J and 1L: Attach
the support bracket (165) with one countersunk head screw (170) and
one countersunk finishing washer (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Attach the support
bracket (145) with three hexagon head screws (150), six flat washers
(155) and three hexagon self-locking nuts (160).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Attach the capping
(130) with three hexagon head screws (135) and three flat washers
(140).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the panel trim assembly (125) to the
canopy installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H, 1J,
1K and 1L: Attach the grab handle (105) with five hexagon head screws
(110) and five flat washers (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the aisle capping assembly (95) with
two countersunk head screws (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the light bracket assembly (65):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
 AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE  MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revend><revst><para> Attach the bonded part reflector (91) to the
light bracket assembly (65)  with the adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the light bracket (92) to the light
bracket assembly (65).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(90) to the light backet assembly (65) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fastener (90) and to the bonded surface(65).</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(90) in position on to the bonded syrface(65).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (90).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the transfer tape (85) and one block
spacer (80).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the light bracket assembly (65) with
two hexagon head screws (70) and two flat washers (75).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1G: Attach one doubler
(60) to the canopy installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1, 1D and 1E: Attach
one bracket (50) and one center front seal to the canopy installation(55).
</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the support bracket assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the bracket attachment (45).</para>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E,
1F, 1G, 1J and 1L: Attach the bracket (30) with two hexagon head screws
(35) and two flat washers (40).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket assembly (5) with
four hexagon head screws (10, 15) and four flat washers (20, 25).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-440-001-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Canopy Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 28) to the Furniture
Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the canopy installation (5-135, 6-135)
to the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 28 IPL for the Canopy Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-003-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Composite Integration (Ref. IPL Fig. 27):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bare shell assembly
(5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the shell composite assembly
(205).</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the backshell (420):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1H, 1K and 1M: Engage the
self-adhesive hook fasteners (440) to the backshell (420) as follows:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (440) and backshell (420).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (440)
in position on to the backshell (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (440).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the edging grommet (435) to the backshell
(420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J
and 1L: Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (430) to the backshell
(420) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (430) and the backshell (420).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (430)
in position on to the backshell (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (430).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the aluminum tapes (425) to the backshell
(420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the footrest vertical
panel (415):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the aluminum tape (416) and edging
grommet (417) to the footrest vertical panel (415).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the support footrest
panel (410):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the aluminum tape (411) to the support
footrest panel (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the aluminum tape (381) and edging
grommet (382) to the EQ tray table support panel (365).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the EQ tray table support panel
(365):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket (400) with two countersunk
screws (405). Torque the countersunk screws (405) to 2.3 Nm (1.6 lbf.ft).
</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the pcu bracket (385) with one socket
head screw (390) and one flat washer (395). Torque the socket head
screw (390) to 2.3 Nm (1.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the tray table support panel (365)
with two socket head screws (370), one countersunk head screw (375)
and three flat washers (380). Torque the socket head screw (370) to
2.3 Nm (1.6 lbf.ft) and the countersunk head screw (375) to 5.0 Nm
(3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the tv support assembly (335):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the doublers (360) to the tv support
assembly (335):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1H, 1K and 1M: Attach the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (356) to the tv support assembly (335)
as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (356) and tv support assembly (335).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (356)
in position on to the tv support assembly (335).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (356).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1H,
1J, 1K, 1L and 1M: Attach the edging grommet (355) to the tv support
assembly (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the aluminium tapes (350) to the tv
support assembly (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (345)
to the tv support assembly (335) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (345) and tv support assembly (335).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (345)
in position on to the tv support assembly (335).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (345).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J
and  1L: Engage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (340) to the tv support
assembly (335) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (340) and tv support assembly (335).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (340)
in position on to the tv support assembly (335).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (340).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the doubler-reinforcement (330).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1H and 1M:
Attach the bracket (310) with one socket head screw (315), two countersunk
head screws (320) and one flat washer (325). Torque the socket head
screw (315) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft) and the countersunk head screw
(320) to 2.3 Nm (1.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the EQ aisle sidewall panel (290):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L and 1M: Attach the edging grommet (309) to the EQ aisle sidewall
panel (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the aluminum tapes (308) to the EQ
aisle sidewall panel (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1H and 1M: Engage
the self-adhesive hook fasteners (307) to the EQ aisle sidewall panel
(290) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (307) and EQ aisle sidewall panel (290).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (307)
in position on to the EQ aisle sidewall panel (290).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (307).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1K
and 1M: Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (306) to the EQ
aisle sidewall panel (290) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (306) and EQ aisle sidewall panel (290).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (306)
in position on to the EQ aisle sidewall panel (290).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (306).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G,
1H, 1K, 1L and 1M: Attach the EQ aisle sidewall panel (290) with four
hexagon head screws (295), two socket head screws (300) and six flat
washers (305). Torque the hexagon head screws (295) to 5.0 Nm (3.6
lbf.ft) and the socket head screws (300) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L and 1M: Attach the bracket (275) with ten hexagon head screws
(280) and ten flat washers (285). Torque the hexagon head screws (280)
to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the sidewall panel assembly
(255):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly1, 1A, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G and 1H:
Attach the grommet edging (272) to the sidewall panel assembly (255).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G,
1J, 1K, 1L and 1M: Attach the aluminum tape (271) to the sidewall
panel assembly (255).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1E, 1G
and 1H: Engage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (270) to the sidewall
panel assembly (255) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (270) and sidewall panel assembly (255).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (270)
in position on to the sidewall panel assembly (255).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (270).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1K
and 1M: Engage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (265) to the sidewall
panel assembly (255) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (265) and sidewall panel assembly (255).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (265)
in position on to the sidewall panel assembly (255).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (265).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G,
1H and 1L: Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (260) to the sidewall
panel assembly (255) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (260) and sidewall panel assembly (255).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (260)
in position on to the sidewall panel assembly (255).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (260).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket (240) with two hexagon
head screws (245) and two flat washers (250). Torque the hexagon head
screws (245) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1D, 1F and 1G: Attach
the indexing block (225) with two socket head screws (230) and two
flat washers (235). Torque the socket head screws (230) to 5.0 Nm
(3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1D, 1F and 1G: Attach
the indexing block (210) with two socket head screws (215) and two
flat washers (220). Torque the socket head screws (215) to 5.0 Nm
(3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the rear beam assembly (100):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ rear beam (200) to the rear
beam assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one tape (201) to the rear beam (200).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket EQ (180) with two hexagon
head screws (185), two nuts (190) and four flat washers (195). Torque
the hexagon head screws (185) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ bracket (155) with three hexagon
head screws (160, 165), three nuts (170) and six flat washers (175).
Torque the hexagon head screws (160, 165) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ bracket (135) with two hexagon
head screws (140), four flat washers (145) and two nuts (150). Torque
the hexagon head screws (140) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the rear beam assembly (100) with
fourteen hexagon head screws (105, 110, 115, 120), twenty two flat
washers (125) and eight nuts (130). Torque the hexagon head screws
(105, 110, 115, 120) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the front beam assembly (10):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ front beam (95) to the front
beam assembly (10).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ bracket (75) with two hexagon
head screws (80), two nuts (85) and four flat washers (90). Torque
the hexagon head screws (80) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ bracket (55) with two hexagon
head screws (60), four flat washers (65) and two nuts (70). Torque
the hexagon head screws (60) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ bracket (35) with two hexagon
head screws (40), four flat washers (45) and two nuts (50). Torque
the hexagon head screws (40) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the front beam assembly (10) with
ten hexagon head screws (15, 20), sixteen washers (25) and four nuts
(30). Torque the hexagon head screws (15, 20) to 5.0 Nm (3.6 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-004-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Vertical Caps Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 26):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Attach the privacy
screen closeout assembly (440) with two hexagon head screws (445)
and two flat washers (450).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Attach the bracket
(425) with six countersunk head screws (430) and six flat washers
(435).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Assemble the privacy
screen closeout assembly (405):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (420) to the privacy screen closeout
assembly (405) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
double-sided tapes (420) and to the bonded surface (405).</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the double-sided tapes (420)
in position on to the bonded surface (405).</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (420).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(415) to the privacy screen closeout assembly (405) as follows:</para>
<revend></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (415) and to the bonded surface (405).</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(415) in position on to the bonded surface (405).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (415).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Attach the privacy
screen closeout assembly (405) with one countersunk head screw (410).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1L and 1N: Attach the
edge capping (390) with three countersunk head screws (395) and three
flat washers (400).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1L and 1N: Attach the
closeout (375) with six countersunk head screws (380) and six flat
washers (385).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Attach the top cap (350)
with two hexagon head screws (355) and two flat washers (365).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Attach
the top cap (350) with two hexagon head screws (355, 360), three flat
washers (365) and one self-locking nut (370).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1H and 1J: Assemble the
top capping bracket assembly (320):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cord lanyard assembly (335) with
one pop rivet (340) and one flat washer (345).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Attach
the top capping bracket assembly (320) with two hexagon head screws
(325) and two flat washers (330).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the support bracket assembly (305):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(316) to the support bracket assembly (305) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (316) and to the bounded surface (305).</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(316) in position on to the bounded surface (305).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (316).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the support
bracket assembly (305) with two hexagon head screws (310) and two
flat washers (315).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5739:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Attach one
hexagon head screw (281), two flat washers (283) and one nut (282)
to the closeout assembly (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1H and
1J: Assemble the closeout assembly (270):</para><revend></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst>
<warning><para> WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
 AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE  MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY</para></warning>
<revend><revst><para>For assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the bonded part
doubler assembly (301) with adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para> Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the support bracket assembly (295):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the double sided tape (302) to the
doubler assembly (301) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double
sided tape (302) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double sided tape (302) in position
on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the double sided
tape (302).</para><revend>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(300) to the support bracket assembly (295) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (300) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(300) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (300).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the bonded part support bracket
assembly (295) to the closeout assembly (270) with adhesive Scotch-Weld
DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Attach the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (290) to the closeout assembly (270)
as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (290) and to the bonded surface(270).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(290) in position on to the bonded sruface (270).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (290).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Engage the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (285) to the closeout assembly (270) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (285) and to the bonded surface (270).</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(285) in position on to the bounded surface (270).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (285).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5739: For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1H and
1J: Attach one hexagon head screw (281), two flat washers (283) and
one nut (282) to the closeout assembly (270).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1H and 1J: Attach the
closeout assembly (270) with two hexagon head screws (275) and two
flat washers (280).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the
closeout assembly (270) to vertical caps installation.</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1, 1E and 1F: Attach
the top cap (255) with two countersunk head screws (260) and two flat
washers (265).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1H and 1J: Attach the top
cap (240) with one countersunk head screw (245) and one flat washer
(250).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1E and 1F: : Attach the top
cap (240) in position to the vertical caps installation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1K and 1M: Attach the
edge capping (225) with two countersunk head screws (230) and two
flat washers (235).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1K and 1M: Attach the
edge capping (210) with four countersunk head screws (215) and four
flat washers (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Assemble the privacy
screen closeout assembly (190):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (205)
to the privacy screen closeout assembly (190) with adhesive Alpha
S708.</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (205) and privacy screen closeout assembly (190).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (205)
in position on to the privacy screen closeout assembly (190).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (205).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Attach the privacy
screen closeout assembly (190) with three hexagon head screws (195)
and three flat washers (200).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Assemble the
closeout assembly (165):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
 AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE  MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY</para></warning>
<revend><para>Assemble and attach the privacy screen closeout assembly
(180):</para>
<note><para> Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners (185)
to the privacy screen closeout assembly (180) as follows:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (185) and to the bonded surface (180).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (185)
in position on to the bonded surface(180).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (185).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Attach the
closeout assembly (165) with three hexagon head screws (170) and three
flat washers (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J, 1K,
1L, 1M and 1N: Attach the aisle lower capping (140) with two countersunk
head screws (145, 150) and two flat washers (155, 160).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J, 1K,
1L, 1M and 1N: Attach the capping (120) with two countersunk head
screws (125), one socket cap head screw (130) and three flat washers
(135).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1J, 1K,
1L, 1M and 1N: Attach the capping (100) with four countersunk head
screws (105, 110) and four flat washers (115).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Attach the
dot edge capping (85) with two countersunk head screws (90) and two
flat washers (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Attach the
upper capping (65) with three countersunk head screws (70, 75) and
three flat washers (80).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1L and 1N: Attach
the static door capping (35) with four countersunk head screws (40,
45, 50), one flat washer (55) and two finishing countersunk washers
(60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the static door capping (5) with one
countersunk head screw (10), one pan head screw (15), two or one countersunk
head screws (20), one flat washer (25) and two finishing countersunk
washers (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-005-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Underseat Drip Tray Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 25):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the central beam cover assembly
(175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the beam assembly (190):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the beam cover (240) to the beam assembly
(190).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook and
loop fasteners (235) to the beam assembly (190) as follows:</para>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
hook and loop fasteners (235) and to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the hook and loop fasteners (235)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the hook and loop
fasteners (235).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(225, 230) to the beam assembly (190) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (225, 230) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(225, 230) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (225, 230).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the fascia plate assembly (195):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the fascia plate (220).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part center backing plate (215) to the fascia
plate (220) with 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the cord lanyard assembly (200) with
one pop rivet (205) and two flat washers (210).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the beam assembly (190) to central
beam cover assembly (175).	</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble two rail spar assemblies (180):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(185) to the rail spar assembly (180) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (185) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(185) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (185).</para><revend>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach two bonded part rail spar assemblies (180) to the central
beam cover assembly (175) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the central beam cover assembly (175)
to the underseat drip tray assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Assemble and attach the
drip shield installation (135):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the drip shield installation
(150):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fasteners
(170) to the drip shield installation (150) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive hook fasteners (170) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners
(170) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (170).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the drip shield (155) with one nylatch
plunger (160) and one nylatch grommet (165).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part support bracket (145) and drip shield
installation (150) to the drip shield installation (135) with adhesive
3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(140, 140A) to the drip shield installation (135) as follows:</para>
<revend></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (140, 140A) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(140, 140A) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (140, 140A).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E and 1F: Assemble
the drip shield installation (110):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fastener
(130) to the drip shield installation (110) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive hook fastener (130) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fastener
(130) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fastener (130).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the drip shield (115) with one nylatch
plunger (120) and one nylatch grommet (125).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E and 1F: Attach
the drip shield installation (110) to the underseat drip tray assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the drip shield installation (80,
80B):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fasteners
(109) to the drip shield installation (80B) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive hook fasteners (109) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners
(109) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (109).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the drip shield (106) with one nylatch
plunger (107) and one nylatch grommet (108).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the drip shield installation
(85):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the drip shield (90) with one nylatch
plunger (95) and one nylatch grommet (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fasteners
(105) to the drip shield installation (85) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive hook fasteners (105) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners
(105) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (105).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Post SB25-5773: Attach the double-sided tapes (84) to the drip
shield installation (80B) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
double-sided tapes (84) and to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the double-sided tapes (84) in
position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para> Apply pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (84).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the drip shield installation (80,
80B) to the underseat drip tray assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the drip tray sub assembly (50):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach four stud (70) and four eyelet (75)
to the drip tray sub assembly (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the drip shield (55) with three nylatch
plungers (60) and three nylatch grommets (65).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the drip tray sub assembly (50) to
the underseat drip tray assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E and 1F: Attach
the support bracket (35) with two hexagon head screws (40) and two
flat washers (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the drip tray bracket (20) with two
hexagon head screws (25) and two flat washers (30).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (5) with two hexagon
head screws (10) and two flat washers (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-006-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the N-Aisle Claddings Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
24):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the ottoman right column (570) with
four countersunk head screws (575, 580).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the meal panel support bracket (555)
with four countersunk head screws (560, 565).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the ottoman left column (540) with
four countersunk head screws (545, 550).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the mid console sup bracket (525)
with two countersunk head screws (530) and two flat washers (535).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the pcu bumper bracket assembly
(505):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the loctite 406 to the edging grommets (520). Attach the
bonded part edging grommet (520) to the pcu bumper bracket assembly
(505).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg
F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fasteners (515)
to the pcu bumper bracket assembly (505) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (515) and pcu bumper bracket assembly (505).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (515)
in position on to the pcu bumper bracket assembly (505).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (515).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Attach the pcu bumper bracket assembly (505) with
two countersunk head screws (510).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Attach the pcu bumper bracket assembly (480) with
three countersunk head screws (485, 490), three flat washers (495,
497) and one plastic cap (496).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1K, 1L, 1N and
1Q: Assemble and attach the aft to console left cladding (470):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (475)
to the aft to console left cladding (470) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (475) and aft to console left cladding (470).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (475)
in position on to the aft to console left cladding (470).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (475).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B and 1C: Assemble and
attach the life vest closeout assembly (460):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (465)
to the life vest closeout assembly (460) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (465) and life vest closeout assembly (460).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (465)
in position on to the life vest closeout assembly (460).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (465).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the aft seat cladding assembly (425):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(455) to the aft seat cladding assembly (425) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (455) and aft seat cladding assembly (425).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (455)
in position on to the aft seat cladding assembly (425).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (455).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (450)
to the aft seat cladding assembly (425) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (450) and aft seat cladding assembly (425).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (450)
in position on to the aft seat cladding assembly (425).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (450).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Attach the aft seat cladding assembly (425) with
four countersunk head screws (430, 435) and four countersunk finishing
washers (440, 445).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the cladding support bracket (410):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
