four countersunk washers (160).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Attach the ctr closeout
cladding assembly (125) with two countersunk head screws (130) and
two countersunk washers (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the ctr closeout cladding assembly
(125):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(140) to the ctr closeout cladding assembly (125) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (140) and ctr closeout cladding assembly (125).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (140)
in position on to the ctr closeout cladding assembly (125).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (140).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1G: Attach the ctr closeout
cladding assembly (125) with two countersunk head screws (130) and
two countersunk washers (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1K and 1N: Assemble and Attach
the capping cladding assembly (115) to the N-Aisle Claddings Installation:
</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (120) to the capping cladding
assembly (115) as follows: </para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tapes (120) and the capping cladding assembly (115).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tapes (120) in position
on to the capping cladding assembly (115).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (120).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1K and 1N: Assemble the mid
backshell cladding assembly (80):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the under armrest cladding
assembly (100):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (110)
to the under armrest cladding assembly (100) as follows:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (110) and the under armrest cladding assembly (100).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (110)
in position on to the under armrest cladding assembly (100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (110).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (105) to the under armrest cladding
assembly (100) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tapes (105) and the under armrest cladding assembly (100).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tapes (105) in position
on to the under armrest cladding assembly (100).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (105).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part mid backshell decor cladding (95) to
the backshell cladding assembly (80) with adhesive Alpha S708.</para>
<note><para>Leave 30 minutes to dry at 16 deg C to 27 deg C (60.8
deg F to 80.6 deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the mid backshell cladding assembly
(80) with three countersunk head screws (85) and three countersunk
washers (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the under-aisle arm pad cladding
(50):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the under armrest cladding
assembly (70):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (75) to the under armrest cladding
assembly (70) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tapes (75) and the under armrest cladding assembly (70).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tapes (75) in position
on to the under armrest cladding assembly (70).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (75).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the under armrest cladding assembly
(70) to the under-aisle arm pad cladding (50).</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>If removed, attach the under aisle arm decor cladding (65) with
Scotch-Weld 2000 B/A BLUE.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 48 hours at 24 deg C (75.2 deg F)
or room temperature.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1D, 1G, 1L, 1M,
1P and 1Q: Attach the under-aisle arm pad cladding (50) with two countersunk
head screws (55) and two countersunk washers (60).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the seat-to-seat cladding assembly
(25):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(45) to the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (45) and seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25)</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (45)
in position on to the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (45).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (40) to the seat-to-seat cladding
assembly (25) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tapes (40) and the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tapes (40) in position
on to the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (40).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Attach the
seat-to-seat cladding assembly (25) with one countersunk head screw
(30) and one countersunk finishing washer (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the seat-to-seat cladding assembly
(5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (20) to the seat-to-seat cladding
assembly (5) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tapes (20) and the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (5).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tapes (20) in position
on to the seat-to-seat cladding assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (20).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: Attach the
seat-to-seat cladding assembly (5) with two countersunk head screws
(10) and two countersunk finishing washers (15).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-007-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Kickstrip and Seals Cladding Installation (Ref.
IPL Fig. 23):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Attach the aft support footwell shroud (575) with two countersunk
head screws (580).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Attach and assemble the aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly (540):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>If removed, attach the bonded part bracket assembly (565) to
the aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly (540) with Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.
</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and the bonded surface of the aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly
(540).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two bonded part magnets (560) to the
aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly (540) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and 1K: Apply the Loctite
222 to the threads of the countersunk head screws (545, 550). Attach
the aft seat kickstrip cladding assembly (540) with two countersunk
head screws (545, 550) and two flat washers (555).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1H and 1K: Assemble the backshell
kickstrip cladding assembly (515):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tape (535) to the backshell kickstrip
cladding assembly (515) as follow:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double
sided tape (535) and the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (515).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double sided tape (535) in position
on to the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (515).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double sided
tape (535).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the seal (530) to the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly
(515) with adhesive Alpha S708.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 30 minutes to dry at 16 deg C to
27 deg C (60.8 deg F to 80.6 deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1H and 1K: Attach the backshell
kickstrip cladding assembly (515) with two countersunk head screws
(520) and two countersunk washer (525).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Assemble the backshell kickstrip cladding assembly (485):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bracket attachment (511) and bracket assembly (512)
with adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D and 1F: Attach the supporting
