AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and the aft aisle kickstrip cladding (300).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach three magnets (315) to the aft aisle
kickstrip cladding (300) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-028-a01"></refint>) to
install one quarter turn screw (305), one quarter turn retainer (310)
to the aft aisle kickstrip cladding (300).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Attach two brackets (280) with two hexagon head screws (285) and
two flat washers (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Attach two light cover support brackets (265) with six countersunk
head screws (270) and six flat washers (275).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H and
1K: Assemble the ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly (240):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Post SB25-5797: Attach the bonded part doubler (261) to the
ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly (240) with the adhesive scotch-weld
DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and to the bonded surface of the ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly
(245).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two bonded part magnets (260) to the
ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly (245) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-028-a01"></refint>) to
install two quarter turn screws (250), two quarter turn receptacles
(255) to the ottoman kickstrip cladding assembly (245).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H
and 1K: Assemble the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1G, 1H and 1K: Attach the bonded parts
supporting sheets (221, 222, 223) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1E, 1G, 1H and 1K: Attach the bonded parts supporting
sheet (224) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the aisle floor seal (236) with adhesive Loctite 406
with primer 770.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Engage the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (235) to the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210)
as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (235) and aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (235)
in position on to the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (235).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Engage the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (230) to the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210)
as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (230) and aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (230)
in position on to the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (230).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (225) to the aisle kickstrip cladding
assembly (210) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tapes (225) and the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tapes (225) in position
on to the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (225).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the aisle
kickstrip cladding assembly (210) with three countersunk head screws
(215) and three washers (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1G, 1H and 1K: Attach
the aisle kickstrip cladding assembly (210).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Attach the bracket
(190) with two hexagon head screws (195) and two flat washers (200).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Attach the attachment
bracket (175) with two hexagon head screws (180) and two flat washers
(185).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E and 1G: Assemble the accessing
panel assembly (140):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part attachment bracket (170) to the accessing
panel assembly (140) with scotch-weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-028-a01"></refint>) to
install two quarter turn screw (150), two quarter turn receptacles
(160), two quarter turn washers (155), two ejector springs (165) to
the baseframe access cladding (145).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the forward console cladding assembly
(100):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1J and 1L: Engage the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (135) to the forward console cladding
assembly (100) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (135) and forward console cladding assembly (100).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (135)
in position on to the forward console cladding assembly (100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (135).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (130) to the forward console cladding
assembly (100) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tapes (130) and the forward console cladding assembly (100).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tapes (130) in position
on to the forward console cladding assembly (100).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (130).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and to the bonded surface of the forward console cladding assembly
(100).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1G, 1H and 1L: Attach
two bonded part magnets (125) to the forward console cladding assembly
(100) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H and
1K: Install one hexagon head screw (105), one countersunk head screw
(115), one flat washer (110), one bush (120) to the forward console
cladding assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the forward console cladding assembly
(100) with one hexagon head screw (105) and one flat washer (110).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1J and 1L: Assemble
the clip assembly (65):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the attachment bracket (90) and console
spring clip bracket (95) to the clip assembly (65).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cladding support bracket (80)
with two countersunk head screws (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1J and 1L: Attach the
clip assembly (65) with two hexagon head screws (70), and two flat
washers (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1F: Attach the bracket
(50) with two hexagon head screws (55) and two flat washers (60).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1F: Assemble the ctr
closeout aisle kickstrip assembly (5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive loctite 406 with primer 770 to the p-seal
(45) and attach the bonded part p-seal (45) to the ctr closeout aisle
kickstrip assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (10):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and to the bonded surface of the bracket assembly (10).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bonded part magnet (40) to the
bracket assembly (10) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-028-a01"></refint>) to
install one quarter turn screw (20), quarter turn washer (25), one
quarter turn receptacle (30), one ejector spring (35) to the bracket
(15).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bracket assembly (10) to the ctr closeout aisle kickstrip
assembly (5) with 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-008-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Seat Recess Cladding Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
22):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the cladding bracket
assembly (435):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (455)
to the cladding bracket assembly (435) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (455) and cladding bracket assembly (435).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (455)
in position on to the cladding bracket assembly (435).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (455).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 222 (with activator 7649) to the
threads of the hexagon head screw (445). Attach the cladding bracket
assembly (435) with two hexagon head screws (440, 445) and two flat
washers (450).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the support bracket assembly
(410):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook fastener (430)
to the support bracket assembly (410) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fastener (430) and the support bracket assembly (410).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fastener (430)
in position on to the support bracket assembly (410).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the support bracket
assembly (410).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
