</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach three magnets (195) to the seat surround
cladding (190) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER.</para>
</warning>
<para>Attach one magnet (200) to the seat surround cladding (190)
with adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the seat surround cladding (190) to
the seat surround cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the seat surround foam (185) to the
seat surround cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the seat surround cover (180) to the
seat surround cladding assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the seat surround cladding assembly
(150) with four hexagon head screws (155, 160, 165), three flat washers
(170) and one countersunk finishing washer (175).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the seat surround cladding assembly
(110):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the cladding assembly
(140):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(145) to the cladding assembly (140) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (145) and cladding assembly (140).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (145)
in position on to the cladding assembly (140).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (145).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the headrest foam (135) to the seat
surround cladding assembly (110).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER.</para>
</warning>
<para>Attach the headrest cover (130) to the seat surround cladding
assembly (110) with adhesive Scotch Weld 2000 B/A Blue.</para>
<note><para>Leave 48 hours to dry at 24 deg C (72 deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the seat surround cladding assembly
(110) with three countersunk head screws (115, 120) and two countersunk
finishing washers (125).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER.</para>
</warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 222 (with activator 7649) to the
threads of the hexagon head screws (100). Attach the cladding bracket
(95) with two hexagon head screws (100) and two flat washers (105).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1E: Assemble and attach
the cladding assembly (85):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (90)
to the cladding assembly (85) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (90) and cladding assembly (85).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (90)
in position on to the cladding assembly (85).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (90).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D and 1E: Assemble
and attach the seat surround cladding assembly (60):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and to the bonded surface of the seat surround cladding assembly (60).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach three or two bonded part magnets (80)
to the seat surround cladding assembly (60) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (75)
to the seat surround cladding assembly (60) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (75) and seat surround cladding assembly (60).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (75)
in position on to the seat surround cladding assembly (60).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (75).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1D and 1E: Attach the seat surround
cladding assembly (60) with one countersunk head screw (65) and one
finishing countersunk washer (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the seat surround
cladding assembly (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the cladding assembly
(40):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and to the bonded surface of the cladding assembly (40).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach four bonded part magnets (55) to the
cladding assembly (40) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1F and 1G: Attach the
cladding assembly (40) with three countersunk head screws (45) and
three countersunk washers (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (20):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(35) to the bracket assembly (20) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para> Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (35) and bracket assembly (20).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (35)
in position on to the bracket assembly (20).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (35).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1F and 1G: Attach the
bracket assembly (20) with two hexagon head screws (25) and two flat
washers (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1F and 1G: Assemble and
attach the cladding assembly (5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fasteners (15)
to the cladding assembly (5) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (15) and cladding assembly (5).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (15)
in position on to the seat surround cladding assembly (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (15).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(10) to the cladding assembly (5) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (10) and  cladding assembly (5).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (10)
in position on to the  cladding assembly (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (10).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-009-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Lifevest Box Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 21):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the lifevest box assembly (105):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>If removed, attach the doubler (140) to the lifevest box assembly
(105) with Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the latch bar (125) with two hexagon
self-locking nuts (130) and two flat washers (135).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the lifevest box assembly (105) with
six hexagon head screws (110, 115) and six flat washers (120).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>Attach twelve covers (95, 100) on
the lifevest box assembly.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>Post SB25-5801: Attach the self-adhesive
loop fastener (91) to the lifevest box assembly (105) as follows:</para>
<revend></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fastener (91) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fastener
(91) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fastener (91).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5801: Assemble and attach the lifevest
cover assembly (85):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(90) to the lifevest cover assembly (85) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (90) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(90) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (90).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the lifevest door assembly
(25):</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the lifevest door assembly
(40):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part support bracket (84) to the lifevest
door (82) with adhesive 3M Scotch-Weld DP8825NS and attach to the
lifevest door assembly (40).</para><revend>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the latch shear assembly (75) with
two hexagon head screws (80). Torque the hexagon head screws (80)
to 2.0 Nm (1.4 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fastener (70)
to the lifevest door assembly (40) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive hook fastener (70) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fastener
(70) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fastener (70).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the pull tab assembly (55), latch
cover assembly (60) and lifevest door cover assembly (65).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the back latch (45) with two pan head
screws (50). Torque the pan head screws (50) to 2.0 Nm (1.4 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tape (35) to the latch cover (30) as
follow:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tape (35) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tape (35) in position
on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the double sided
tape (35).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the cord lanyard assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach two lanyard connectors (21)
and one cord (22) to the cord lanyard assembly (5).</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cord lanyard assembly (5) with
two pop rivets (10, 15) and four flat washers (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="036"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-036-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Lifevest Box Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 21) to the
Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the lifevest box assembly (5-230)
to the furniture assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 21 IPL for the Lifevest Box Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-010-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the FWD Fascia Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 20):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (215):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the low friction tape (230) to the
bracket assembly (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (215) with two
hexagon head screws (220) and two flat washers (225).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (195):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the low friction tape (210) to the
bracket assembly (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach three bracket assemblies (195) with
six hexagon head screws (200) and six flat washers (205).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the capping (190) to the fascia Installation.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach three brackets (175) with six hexagon
head screws (180) and six flat washers (185).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach three brackets (160) with six hexagon
head screws (165) and six flat washers (170).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the trim assembly (145):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the panel assembly (150)
to the trim assembly (145):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(155) to the panel assembly (150) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (155) and to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(155) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (155).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the trim assembly (130):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the panel assembly (135)
to the trim assembly (130):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(140) to the panel assembly (135) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (140) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning></warning>
<para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (140) in position on
to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (140).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the fascia panel (125) to the
 Fascia Installation.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the literature pocket assembly (85):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (115):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fasteners (120)
to the bracket assembly (115) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive hook fasteners (120) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners
(120) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (120).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (115) to the
literature pocket assembly (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two literature pockets (100) with
four countersunk head screws (105) and four flat washers (110).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the literature pocket assembly (85)
with four hexagon head screws (90) and four flat washers (95).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the trim panel assembly (55):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the trim (82) to the trim panel assembly
(55).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the panel assembly (75):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the trim panel (81) to the panel assembly
(75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners (80)
to the panel assembly (75) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (80) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(80) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (80).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the panel assembly (75) to the trim
panel assembly (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the logo (65) to the trim panel assembly
(55) with two circlip (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the trim panel assembly (55) with
two countersunk head screws (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the locking bracket (40) with two
hexagon head screws (45) and two flat washers (50).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the monitor bracket (35) to the bracket
assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive loctite 406 to the edging grommets (30) and
attach the bonded part edging grommets (30) to the bracket assembly
(5).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach four spacers (15) with four countersunk
head screws (20) and four flat washers (25).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (5) with one
countersunk head screw (10).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="011"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-011-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Outboard Bridge Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 19):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1H,
1J, 1K, 1L and 1M: Assemble the support bracket assembly (120):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (145) to the support
bracket assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the foam bridge support dampener (135)
with one countersunk head screw (140). Torque the countersunk head
screw (140) to 2.8 Nm (2.0 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1H,
1J, 1K, 1L and 1M: Attach the support bracket assembly (120) with
two countersunk head screws (125) and two flat washers (130). Torque
the countersunk head screws (125) to 2.8 Nm (2.0 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the bridge assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the electrical kit (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the end cap (116) to the electrical kit (35) with the
adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the bridge assembly (95):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1L, 1M and
1N: Attach the cable clamp (110) with one hexagon head screw (115).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1E, 1F, 1J, 1G, 1L,
1M and 1N: Attach the cable tie mount (100) with one countersunk head
screw (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1D, 1E, 1H, 1F, 1G, 1K,
1L 1M and 1N: If removed, attach the roundit (91) to the electrical
kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: If removed, install
the roundit (90) to the electrical kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1J, 1L,
1M and 1N: If removed, install the roundit (85) to the electrical
kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>If removed, install the roundit (80) to the
electrical kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C and 1J: Connect
and install the harness assembly (75) to the electrical kit (35) at
connectors P2, P6B and P6.</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1G, 1H and 1N: Attach the
harness assembly (65) with four pan head screws (70).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1M and 1N: Connect the harness assembly (65) to the electrical
kit (35) at connectors P1, P1A, P2, P2A, J1C and P1C.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Connect and install the harness assembly
(60) to the electrical kit (35) at connectors P1A, P2A, P4A and P10.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1G, 1L, 1M and 1N: Connect
and install the harness assembly (55) to the electrical kit (35) at
connectors D23P, P201, P101 and P100A.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Connect and install the harness assembly
(50) to the electrical kit (35) at connectors D14P, D16P and D301P.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F and 1G: Install the fixing
base (45) to the electrical kit (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install twenty-nine or twenty-eight or thirty
or thirty-one tie cables (40) to the electrical kit (35).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the electrical kit (35) to the bridge
assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cover (20) to the bridge assembly
(5) with five or two pan head screws (25) and five or two flat washers
(30).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bridge assembly (5) with two countersunk
head screws (10) and two flat washers (15). Torque two countersunk
head screws (10) to 2.8 Nm (2.0 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="012"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-012-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Folding Armrest Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 18):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the folding armrest assembly (45):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the armrest base structure assembly
(60):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the hinge (80) with two pins (85).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the armrest base structure (75) to
the armrest base structure assembly (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the armrest structure cap (65) with
two countersunk head screws (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one armrest base structure assembly
(60) to the folding armrest assembly (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Attach two bonded part folding armrest foam (55) to the
folding armrest assembly (45) with Scotch-Weld 2000 B/A BLUE.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 48 hours at 24 deg C (75.2 deg F)
or room temperature.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cover assembly (50) to the folding
armrest assembly (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the folding armrest assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the transfer tapes (40) and the folding
armrest assembly (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the RH and LH armrest mounting structures
(25, 30) to the armrest bottom cladding (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the folding armrest assembly (5) with
four hexagon head screws (10, 15) and four flat washers (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-440-003-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Folding Armrest Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 18)
to the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the folding armrest installation (5-165,
6-165) to the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 18 IPL for the Folding Armrest Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="013"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-013-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Upper Console Stowage Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
17):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the structure stowage assembly (65):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the panel assembly (420):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(430) and self-adhesive hook fasteners (425) to the panel assembly
(420) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (430), self-adhesive hook fasteners (425) and to
the panel assembly (420).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (430)
and self-adhesive hook fasteners (425) to the panel assembly (420)
in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (430) and self-adhesive hook fasteners (425).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the drip tray tube (415) to the structure
stowage assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the drip tray assembly
(395):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the transfer tape (411) and drip tray
(412).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (410) and to the drip tray assembly (395).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push four self-adhesive hook fasteners (410)
to the drip tray assembly (395) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (410).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the circlip (405) to the drip tray
assembly (395).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the drip tray bezel (400) to the drip
tray assembly (395).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the trim panel assembly
(380):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (390) and to the panel assembly (385).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (390)
to the panel assembly (385) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (390).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the trim panel assembly
(365):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (375) and to the panel assembly (370).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (375)
to the panel assembly (370) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (375).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the spring plunger (360) to the structure
stowage assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the panel assembly (345):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (355) and to the panel assembly (345).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (355)
to the panel assembly (345) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (355).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the panel assembly (345) with nine
pan head screws (350).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the spacer assembly (335):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT DOUBLE SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN THE
CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tape (340) to the spacer assembly (335)
as follow:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tape (340) and the spacer assembly (335).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tape (340) in position
on to the spacer assembly (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tape (340).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the hall effect assembly
(320):</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (300):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two nylatch grommets (330) and two
nylatch plungers (325) to the hall effect assembly (320).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook fastener (315)
to the bracket assembly (300) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fastener (315) and to the bracket assembly (300).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fastener (315)
to the bracket assembly (300) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fastener (315).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (300) with two
countersunk head screws (305) and two flat washers (310).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the microphone bracket
assembly (280):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(295) to the microphone bracket assembly (280) as follows:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (295) and to the microphone bracket assembly (280).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (295)
to the microphone bracket assembly (280) in position.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (295).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two nylatch grommets (290) and two
nylatch plungers (285) to the microphone bracket assembly (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (265):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(275) to the bracket assembly (265) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (275) and to the bracket assembly (265).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (275)
to the bracket assembly (265) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (275).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (265) with one
countersunk head screw (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the trim panel assembly (230):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the upper stowage panel
assembly (255):</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (260) and to the upper stowage panel assembly (255).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (260)
to the upper stowage panel assembly (255) in position.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
 loop fasteners (260).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bezel microphone (245) and bezel microphone retainer
(250) to the trim panel assembly (230) with adhesive Loctite 243.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 1 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the trim panel assembly (230) with
two pan head screws (235) and two flat washers (240).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the latch striker assembly
(220):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bumper (225) to the latch striker
assembly (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the striker plate (210) with two countersunk
head screws (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the retainer striker (200) with two
countersunk head screws (205).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the stowage door assembly (90):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the trimmed door assembly (195) to
the stowage door assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive DP8825NS to the magnet (190). Attach the
bonded part magnet (190) to the stowage door assembly (90).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS,
HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL
HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive DP8825NS to the panel assembly (185). Attach
the bonded part panel assembly (185) to the stowage door assembly
(90).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bezel bracket (175) with two pan
head screws (180).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the latch assembly (120):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the latch frame (170) to the latch
assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the latch handle (165) to the latch
assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two springs (140, 160) to the latch
assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two latch hooks (125, 145) with two
latch shafts (130, 150) and two circlips (135, 155).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the latch assembly (120) to the stowage
door assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the latch cover (110) with two countersunk
head screws (115).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two hinges (100) with four countersunk
head screws (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the stowage door assembly (90) with
four countersunk head screws (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the structure stowage assembly (65)
with ten hexagon head screws (70, 75, 80) and ten flat washers (85).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket (50) with two hexagon
head screws (55) and two flat washers (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the trim panel assembly
(35):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the panel assembly (40):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (45) and to the panel assembly (40).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (45)
to the panel assembly (40) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (45).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the light panel assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the light panel (30) to the light
panel assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT DOUBLE SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN THE
CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the light diffuser (20) with double-sided tapes (25)
as follow:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tape (25) and the light diffuser (20).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tape (25) in position
on to the light diffuser (20).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tape (25).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the light panel assembly (5) with
one countersunk head screw (10) and one countersunk finishing washer
(15).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-440-004-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Upper Console Stowage Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
17) to the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the upper console stowage installation
(5-145, 6-145) to the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig.
6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 17 IPL for the Upper Console Stowage Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="014"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-014-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Sliding Door Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 16):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bonded door panel
assembly (325):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the equipped internal door (505) to
the bonded door panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach two bonded part decorative door panels (495, 500) to
the bonded door panel assembly (325) with adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F)..</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the latch bezel assembly (485) with
two countersunk head screws (490).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one latch hook (480) to the bonded
door panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one spring (475) to the bonded door
panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one link (470) to the bonded door
panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the latch plate (460) with two countersunk
head screws (465).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bezel assembly (450) with four
countersunk head screws (455).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the latch hook assembly
(435):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the latch hook (440) with one ball
plunger (445).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the link (430) to the bonded door
panel assembly (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the latch cover plate (420) with three
countersunk head screws (425).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part edge capping (415) to the bonded door
panel assembly (325) with adhesive 3M&trade; 7246-2 B/A FST.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 1 is 7 days at 23 &plusmn; 2
&deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only during
the first 24 hours.</para></note>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 2 is 24 hours at 23 &plusmn;
 2 &deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only
during the first 6 hours. Then cure for 60 to 70 minutes at 80 &plusmn;
5 &deg;C (176 &plusmn; 9 &deg;F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the edge capping assembly
(400):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the edge capping (410) with one pin
(405).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part edge capping assembly (400) with adhesive
3M&trade; 7246-2 B/A FST.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 1 is 7 days at 23 &plusmn; 2
&deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only during
the first 24 hours.</para></note>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 2 is 24 hours at 23 &plusmn;
2 &deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only during
the first 6 hours. Then cure for 60 to 70 minutes at 80 &plusmn; 5
&deg;C (176 &plusmn; 9 &deg;F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the handle (390) with two countersunk
head screws (395).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the edge capping assembly
(375):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the edge capping (385) with two pins
(380).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part edge capping assembly (375) with adhesive
3M&trade; 7246-2 B/A FST.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 1 is 7 days at 23 &plusmn; 2
&deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only during
the first 24 hours.</para></note>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 2 is 24 hours at 23 &plusmn;
 2 &deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only
during the first 6 hours. Then cure for 60 to 70 minutes at 80 &plusmn;
5 &deg;C (176 &plusmn; 9 &deg;F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the edge capping assembly
(360):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the edge capping (370) with two pins
(365).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part capping assembly (360) with the adhesive
3M&trade; 7246-2 B/A FST.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 1 is 7 days at 23 &plusmn; 2
&deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only during
the first 24 hours.</para></note>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 2 is 24 hours at 23 &plusmn;
 2 &deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only
during the first 6 hours. Then cure for 60 to 70 minutes at 80 &plusmn;
5 &deg;C (176 &plusmn; 9 &deg;F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the top edge capping (345) with two
pan head screws (350) and two flat washers (355).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the capping assembly
(330):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the edge capping (340) with one pin
(335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bonded part capping assembly (330) with the adhesive
3M&trade; 7246-2 B/A FST.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 1 is 7 days at 23 &plusmn; 2
&deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only during
the first 24 hours.</para></note>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time cycle 2 is 24 hours at 23 &plusmn;
 2 &deg;C (73.4 &plusmn; 3.6 &deg;F). Apply 100 kPa pressure only
during the first 6 hours. Then cure for 60 to 70 minutes at 80 &plusmn;
5 &deg;C (176 &plusmn; 9 &deg;F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the button assembly (295):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one button (320) to the button assembly
(295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one spring (315) to the button assembly
(295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one spacer (310) to the button assembly
(295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 222 (with activator 7649) to threads
of one rod (305). Attach the rod (305) to the button assembly (295).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the button assembly (295) with one
set screw (300).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 222 (with activator 7649) to threads
of one collar (290). Attach the collar (290) to the rail assembly
(90).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach nine plates (275, 280, 285).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the door guide assembly (230):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the roller support (270) to the door
guide assembly (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach four springs (265) to the door guide
assembly (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two pins (250), two flat washers (255)
and two rollers (260) to the door guide assembly (230).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the door guide (240) with two countersunk
head screws (245).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the door guide assembly (230) with
three countersunk head screws (235).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the striker plate (215) with two countersunk
head screws (220) and two flat washers (225).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the closeout assembly (200) with seven
countersunk head screws (205, 210).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the spigot block assembly (165):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the spigot block (195) to the spigot
block assembly (165).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two cam followers (185) with four
nuts (190). Torque the nuts (190) to (0.3 Nm &plusmn; 10% (0.2 lbf.ft
 &plusmn; 10%).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the spigot block assembly (165) with
four countersunk head screws (170, 175) and two set screws (180).
Torque the countersunk screws (170, 175) to 21.5 Nm (15.8 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the rail assembly (90):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the rail (160) to the top rail assembly
(90).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the carriage block assembly (100):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one bracket (155) to the carriage
block assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the spring (150) to the carriage block
assembly (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the unlocking lever (140) with one
slotted spring pin (145).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the platine (130) with two countersunk
head screws (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the support pin (120) with one set
screw (125).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the support pin (110) with one set
screw (115).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the carriage block assembly (100)
with eight countersunk head screws (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the top rail assembly (90) with eleven
socket head screws (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket support assembly (70):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(85) to the bracket support assembly (70) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (85) and bracket support assembly (70).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (85)
in position on to the bracket support assembly (70).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (85).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket assembly (70)
with two hexagon head screws (75) and two flat washers (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the top stopper assembly (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the door stop assembly (65) to the
top stopper assembly (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the magnet (55) with two countersunk
head screws (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive loctite 480 to the seal (50). Attach the
seal (50) to the top stopper assembly (35).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 30 minutes to 24 hours at 22
deg C (72 deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the stopper assembly (35) with two
countersunk head screws (40) and two flat washers (45).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the top roller assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the roller bracket (30) to the top
roller assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the roller (20) with one pin (25).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the top roller assembly (5) with one
hexagon head screw (10) and one flat washer (15).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-440-005-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Sliding Door Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 16) to
the Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the sliding door installation (5-140,
6-140) to the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 16 IPL for the Sliding Door Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="015"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-015-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Dot Door Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 15):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Attach the clip (415) with two socket head
screws (420) and two flat washers (425).</title></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support pin (405) with two countersunk
head screws (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the dot panel assembly
(195):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the dot panel (400) with tapered dowel
(395) to the dot panel assembly (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the dot edge capping (380) with two
socket head screws (385) and two flat washers (390).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the aft standard EQ cap (355) with
four socket head screws (360, 365, 370) and four flat washers (375).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the dot bottom EQ inner
cladding (345):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the dot upper inner cladding (351)
to the dot bottom EQ inner cladding (345).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners (350)
to the dot bottom EQ inner cladding (345) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (350) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (350)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (350).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the dot lower EQ inner
cladding (335):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the dot upper inner cladding (341)
to the dot inner EQ inner cladding (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fastener (340)
to the dot lower EQ inner cladding (335) as follows: </para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fastener (340) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fastener (340)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fastener (340).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the dot mid EQ inner
cladding (325):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the dot upper inner cladding (331)
to the dot mid EQ inner cladding (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners (330)
to the dot mid EQ inner cladding (325) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (330) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (330)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (330).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the dot top EQ inner
cladding (310):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the dot upper inner cladding (321)
to the dot top EQ inner cladding (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tapes (320) to the dot top EQ inner
cladding assembly (310) as follow:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tapes (320) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tapes (320) in position
on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the double-sided
tapes (320).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fastener (315)
to the dot top EQ inner cladding (310) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fastener (315) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fastener (315)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fastener (315).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two clips (295) with four socket head
screws (300) and four flat washers (305).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two mounting brackets (280) with four
socket head screws (285) and four flat washers (290).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bumper cover (275) to the dot
panel assembly (195).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive DP8825NS to the lateral bumper support (270)
and attach the lateral bumper support (270) to the dot panel assembly
(195).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the dot bumper assembly (255) with
two countersunk head screws (260) and two flat washers (265).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the dot latch assembly
(220):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket (250) to the dot latch
assembly (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two latches (240) with four pop rivets
(245).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(235) to the dot latch assembly (220) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (235) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (235)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (235).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the dot latch assembly (220) with
two socket head screws (225) and one flat washer (230).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two wedge block (210) with two socket
head screws (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two wedge blocks (210) with four socket
head screws (205) to the dot panel assembly (195).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support pin (180) with two socket
head screws (185) and two flat washers (190).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5781: Attach the dot secure clamp
(176) with one socket head screw (177), one flat washer (178).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5781: Attach the dot secure clamp
(176) with one socket head screw (177A), one flat washer (178).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bracket assembly
(140):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket (175) to the bracket assembly
(140).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two receptacles (165) with eight pan
head screws (170).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5781: Attach the bracket assembly
(140) with one socket head screw (150A) and one flat washer (160).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5781: Attach the bracket assembly
(140) with one socket head screw (150B) and one flat washer (160).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (140) with one
pan head screw (145), one countersunk head screw (150) and two flat
washers (155, 160).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the latch cover assembly (105):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the latch cover (135) to the latch
cover assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cord lanyard assembly (120) with
the pop rivet (125) and the washer (130).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS to the bonded part bracket
(115) and attach the bracket (115) to the latch cover assembly (105).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(110) to the latch cover assembly (105):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para> Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (110) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (110)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (110).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<revend></prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the toggle switch assembly (75):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the toggle switch outer case (100)
to the toggle switch assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the latch toggle (85) with hinge pin
(90) and the ball plunger (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the toggle switch assembly (75) with
one socket head screw (80).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one clip (60) with four socket head
screws (65) and four washers (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the support bracket assembly (30):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS to the bonded part attachment
spacer (56). Attach the bonded part attachment spacer (56) to the
support bracket assembly (30).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73 deg
F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bumper electrical
assembly (45):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Connect the TTL indicator (55) at connector
D43P to the support bracket assembly (30) and connect the harness.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Connect the IUL (50) to the support bumper
assembly (30) at connector P8 and connect the harness.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket assembly (30)
with six countersunk head screws (35) and six flat washers (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the bumper assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS to the lateral bumper
support (20). Attach the bumper cover (25) and lateral bumper support
(20) to the bumper assembly (5).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73 deg
F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bumper assembly (5) with two countersunk
head screws (10) and two flat washers (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-032-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Dot Door Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 15) to the
Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the dot door installation (5-240,
6-235) to the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 15 IPL for the Dot Door Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="016"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-016-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Closeout Panel Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 14):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the fixed
privacy panel (350) to the closeout panel installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the forward
panel (345) to the closeout panel installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the elite panel
(340) to the closeout panel installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the closeout panel assembly (220):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Attach the closeout
panel (335) to the closeout panel assembly (220).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Assemble the spigot
(300):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the block (330), pin console alignment
(325), bushing (320) to the spigot assembly (300).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fastener (315)
to the spigot assembly (300) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fastener (315) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fastener (315)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fastener (315).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Attach the spigot
assembly (300) with two hexagon head screws (305) and two flat washers
(310).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Assemble the spigot
assembly (265):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the block (295), the pin console alignment
(290), the bushing (285) to the spigot assembly (265).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fastener (280)
to the spigot assembly (265) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fastener (280) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fastener (280)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fastener (280).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1D: Attach the spigot
assembly (265) with two hexagon head screws (270) and two flat washers
(275).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the seat surround
cladding (262) to the closeout panel assembly (220).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the closeout
panel (261) to the closeout panel assembly (220).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<revend>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and to the bonded surface of the closeout panel assembly (220).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C and 1E: Attach the
bonded part four or three magnets (260) to the closeout panel assembly
(220) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the closeout
panel assembly (220) with five countersunk head screws (235, 240)
and five flat washers (255).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B and 1D: Attach the
closeout panel assembly (220) with one countersunk head screws (225),
two socket head screws (230), one finishing countersunk washer (245)
and two flat washers (250).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Assemble the lower
middle cladding assembly (205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Attach the bracket (215) to the lower middle cladding assembly
(205) with the adhesive Scotch-Weld DP8825NS.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the magnets
and to the bonded surface of the lower middle cladding assembly (205)</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two magnets (210) to the lower middle
cladding assembly (205) in position.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 0.5 hours at 60.8 deg F to 80.6
deg F (16 deg C to 27 deg C).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the bracket
(190) with two hexagon head screws (195) and two flat washers (200).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Assemble the spigot
assembly (155):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the block (185), the pin console alignment
(180) and the bushing (175) to the spigot assembly (155).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fastener (170)
to the spigot assembly (155) as follows:</para></prcitem><revend>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fastener (170) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fastener (170)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fastener (170).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the spigot
assembly (155) with two hexagon head screws (160) and two flat washers
(165).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Assemble the spigot
assembly (120):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the block (150), the pin console alignment
(145) and the bushing (140) to the spigot assembly (120).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fastener (135)
to the spigot assembly (120) as follows:</para></prcitem><revend>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fastener (135) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fastener (135)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fastener (135).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the spigot
(120) with two hexagon head screws (125) and two flat washers (130).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the attachment
bracket (105) with eight countersunk head screws (110) and eight finishing
countersunk washers (115).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the attachment
bracket (85) with twelve countersunk head screws (90, 95) and twelve
finishing countersunk washers (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1E: Attach the attachment
bracket (60) with six countersunk head screws (65, 70) and six finishing
countersunk washers (75, 80).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Attach the attachment bracket
(45) with eight countersunk head screws (50) and eight finishing countersunk
washers (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C and 1E: Attach the
angled bracket (15) with six countersunk head screws (20, 25, 30),
two hexagon nuts (35), and two flat washers (40).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the lower edge
capping privacy (5) with eight countersunk head screws (10).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="029"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-029-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Privacy Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13A):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B: Attach the privacy screen
EQ panel (240) with three hexagon head screws (245) and three flat
washers (250). Torque three hexagon head screws (245) to 9.0 Nm (6.6
lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Assemble the privacy screen
assembly (5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the privacy screen assembly (235)
to the privacy screen assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the interface bracket (215) with three
countersunk head screws (220), three flat washers (225) and three
self-locking nuts (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the end capping retainer (195) with
one countersunk head screw (200), one flat washer (205) and one self-locking
nut (210).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two cable mounting brackets (185)
with four countersunk head screws (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the top capping assembly (135):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the top capping (180) to the top capping
assembly (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two fixing hook cappings (165) with
four countersunk head screws (170).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the cap attachment bracket (150) with
two countersunk head screws (155) and two flat washers (160).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the top capping assembly (135) with
one countersunk head screw (140) and one flat washer (145).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the stopper bracket (120) with two
countersunk head screws (125) and two flat washers (130).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the electrical bracket (105) with
two countersunk head screws (110) and two flat washers (115).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the cat-track assembly (75):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the chain mounting bracket (100) to
the cat-track assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach thirty-two chains (95) to the cat-track
assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the chain mounting bracket (90) to
the cat-track assembly (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cat-track assembly (75) with two
pan head screws (80) and two self-locking nuts (85).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket (60) with two pan head
screws (65) and two self-locking nuts (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the privacy electrical
installation (30):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the LRU interface cable (55) to the
privacy electrical installation (30) at connector P1.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the protection cable (50) to the privacy
electrical installation (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (45) to the
privacy electrical installation (30) at connectors P1 and J4.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the cable tie (40).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install ten tie wraps (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Attach the privacy screen
assembly (5) with five hexagon screws (10, 15) and five washers (20,
25). Torque three hexagon head screws (10) to 9.0 Nm (6.6 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend></prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="017"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-017-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Privacy Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Assemble the locking bracket
assembly (820):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the manual override (855) to the
locking bracket assembly (820).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the spring (850) to the locking bracket
assembly (820).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the adjustable slider (845) to the
locking bracket assembly (820).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the locking pin (840) to the locking
bracket assembly (820).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the locking pin (825) with one hexagon
self-locking nut (830) and one washer (835).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Assemble the upper privacy
panel (765):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the upper privacy panel (815) to
the upper privacy panel (765).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners (810)
to the upper privacy panel (765) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (810) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (810)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (810).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install four stop blocks (800) with four
countersunk head screws (805).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5750:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the upper privacy
panel (765) with nine hexagon head screws (770, 775, 775A), twelve
flat washers (780, 785) and nine hexagon self-locking nuts (790, 795).
Torque the hexagon head screws (775, 775A) to 6.0 Nm (4.4 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5750:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the upper privacy
panel (765) and two closeout brackets (761, 762) with nine hexagon
head screws (770, 775, 775B), twelve flat washers (780, 785) and nine
hexagon self-locking nuts (790, 795). Torque the hexagon head screws
(775) to 6.0 Nm (4.4 lbf.ft) and the hexagon screws (775B) to 24.0
Nm (17.70 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Assemble the middle privacy
panel (730):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the middle privacy panel (760) to
the middle privacy panel (730).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(755) to the middle privacy panel (730) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (755) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (755)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (755).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install two stop blocks (745) with two countersunk
head screws (750).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the middle privacy
panel (730) with ten countersunk head screws (735) and ten flat washers
(740). Torque the countersunk head screws (735) to 0.7 Nm (0.5 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Assemble the middle privacy
panel (695):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the middle privacy panel (725) to
the middle privacy panel (695).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(720) to the middle privacy panel (695) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (720) and the middle privacy panel (695).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners (720)
in position on to the middle privacy panel (695).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (720).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two stop blocks (710) with two countersunk
head screws (715).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the middle privacy
panel (695) with ten countersunk head screws (700) and ten flat washers
(705). Torque the countersunk head screws (700) to 0.7 Nm (0.5 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Assemble the lower privacy
panel (660):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install lower privacy panel (690) to the
lower privacy panel (660).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(685) to the lower privacy panel (660).</para><revend></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (685) and the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(685) in position on to the seat to seat cladding assembly (430).</para>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (685).</para>
<note></note>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the armrest support (675) with seven
countersunk head screws (680).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1: Install the lower
privacy panel (660) with eight countersunk head screws (665) and eight
flat washers (670). Torque the countersunk head screws (665) to 1.4
Nm (1.0 lbf.ft).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Assemble the lower privacy
panel (625):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the lower privacy panel (655) to
the lower privacy panel (625).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(650) to the lower privacy panel (625) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive loop fasteners (650) and the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fasteners
(650) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fasteners (650).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install seven countersunk head screws (645)
to attach the armrest support (640).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the lower privacy panel (625) with
eight countersunk head screws (630) and eight flat washers (635).
Torque the countersunk head screws (630) to 1.4 Nm (1.0 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>For Assembly 1B: Install the bobbin
pin (620) to the privacy screen assembly.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the belt assembly (500):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the t-piece (615)
to the belt assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Install the drive
belt assembly (610) to the belt assembly (500).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the bobbin pin (605)
to the belt assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B: Attach the stopper (590)
with two cap head screws (595) and two flat washers (600). Torque
the cap head screws (595) to 6.0 Nm (4.4 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B: Attach the stopper (575)
with two hexagon head screws (580) and two flat washers (585). Torque
the hexagon head screws (580) to 6.0 Nm (4.4 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Attach the attachment bracket
(560) with two hexagon head screws (565) and two flat washers (570).
Torque the hexagon head screws (565) to 6.0 Nm (4.4 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Attach the rail support
bracket (545) with three hexagon head screws (550) and three flat
washers (555). Torque the hexagon head screws (550) to 6.0 Nm (4.4
lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Install the rail support
bracket (530) two hexagon head screws (535) and two flat washers (540).
Torque the hexagon head screws (535) to 6.0 Nm (4.4 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Install the rail support
bracket (515) with three hexagon head screws (520) and three flat
washers (525). Torque the hexagon head screws (520) to 6.0 Nm (4.4
lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the belt assembly (500) with ten
or seven hexagon head screws (505) and ten or seven flat washers (510).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Install the bracket (485)
with two hexagon head screws (490) and two flat washers (495).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Assemble the rail assembly
(360):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the closing cover (480) to the rail
assembly (360).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the rail support bracket (475) to
the rail assembly (360).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the rail assembly (460) with ten
countersunk head screws (465) and ten hexagon self-locking nuts (470).
Torque the self locking nuts (470) to 2.8 Nm (2.1 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the attachment bracket (445) with
one countersunk head screw (450) and one self-locking nut (455). Torque
the self locking nuts (455) to 2.8 Nm (2.1 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the attachment support (430) with
one countersunk head screw (435) and one hexagon self-locking nut
(440).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install one belt (425) to the rail assembly
(360).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Pre SB25-5742:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the attachment support (415) with
two countersunk head screws (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5742, Pre SB25-5769:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the attachment support (415A) with
two countersunk head screws (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5769:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the joggle panel (415B) with two countersunk
head screws (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the torsion strip (400) with one
pop rivet (405) and two flat washers (410).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the pin (390) with two countersunk
head screws (395).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the stopper (375) with two countersunk
head screws (380) and two hexagon self-locking nuts (385). Torque
the self locking nuts (385) to 2.8 Nm (2.1 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the rail assembly
(360) with eight countersunk head screws (365) and eight countersunk
finishing washers (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the disconnect bracket
(345) with two hexagon head screws (350) and two flat washers (355).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Assemble the solenoid assembly
(265):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the privacy electrical installation
(295):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the harness assembly (330) with one
cap head screw (335) and one flat washer (340).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the spacer (325) to the privacy electrical
installation (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the spacing sleeve (320) to the privacy
electrical installation (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the shaft (310) to the privacy electrical
installation (295) with the slotted spring pin (315).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the spring (305) to the privacy electrical
installation (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install two tie wraps (300) to the privacy
electrical installation (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the solenoid bracket (280) with four
cap head screws (285) and four flat washers (290).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Install the solenoid assembly
(265) with two hexagon head screws (270) and two flat washers (275).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Install the stopper bracket
(250) with two hexagon head screws (255) and two flat washers (260).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Assemble the bracket assembly
(235):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Attach the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (245) to the bracket  assembly (235) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (245) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (245)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (245).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Engage the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (245) to the bracket assembly (235).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Install the bracket assembly
(235) with two countersunk head screws (240).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Assemble the actuator assembly
(105):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the privacy actuator assembly (190):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>HOLD THE ACTUATOR DURING INSTALLATION. IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT.</para>
</caution>
<revst><para>Install the actuator (230) to the the privacy actuator
assembly (190).</para><revend></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 222 (with activator 7649) to the
threads of cap head screws (225). Install the gearbox (220) with two
cap head screws (225). Torque the cap head screws (225) to 2.7 Nm
(2.0 lbf.ft).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the drive pulley (210) with one flat
head screw (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the actuator bracket (195) with two
hexagon head bolts (200) and two self lock nuts (205). Torque the
hexagon head bolts (200) to 11.3 Nm (8.3 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the privacy actuator assembly (190)
to the actuator assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the bracket (185) to the actuator
assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the stopper bracket (170) with one
countersunk head screw (175) and one flat washer (180).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the bracket assembly (165).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the belt bracket (150) with four countersunk
head screws (155) and four flat washers (160).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the bracket (145) to the actuator
assembly (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply the adhesive thread locking compound Loctite 243
(242) to the threads of pan head screws (140). Install the manual
override cable (135) with two pan head screws (140).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Install the actuator assembly
(105) with three countersunk head screws (110, 115), three hexagon
head screws (120), three flat washers (125) and one self-locking washer
(130). Torque the hexagon head screws (120) to 6.0 Nm (4.4 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Install the bracket (90)
with two hexagon head screws (95) and two flat washers (100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Install the belt (85).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Assemble and attach
the actuator assembly (50):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply the thread locking compound Loctite 243 (242) to
the threads of countersunk head screws (70). Install the actuator
(65) with one countersunk head screw (70), two flat washers (75) and
one self-locking nut (80).Torque the countersunk head screws (70)
to 21.5 Nm (15.8 lbf.ft).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply the thread locking compound Loctite 243 (242) to
the threads of hexagon head screws (60). Install the actuator bracket
(55) with two hexagon head screws (60). Torque the hexagon head screws
(60) to 4.0 Nm (2.9 lbf.ft).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Attach the actuator assembly
(50) with two hexagon head screws (51) and two flat washers (52).
Torque the hexagon head screws (51) to 4.0 Nm (2.9 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Assemble the manual
override assembly (20):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the bracket (45).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the manual override cable (35) with
two pan head screws (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1B: Install the manual
override assembly (20) with one hexagon head screw (25) and one flat
washer (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Install the cable tie (10)
with one countersunk head screw (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install four or one tie wraps (5).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-031-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Privacy Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13) to the
Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the privacy screen assembly (5-115,
6-115) to the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 13 IPL for the Privacy Screen Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="038"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-038-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Cocktail Table Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 12):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (430) with two
hexagon head screws (435) and two flat washers (440). Torque the hexagon
head screws (435) to 4.0 Nm (2.9 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the cocktail table equipped (90):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one light diffuser (420) and one cocktail
table rim assembly (425) to the cocktail table equipped (90).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one light diffuser (405) with three
pan head screws (410) and three flat washers (415).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the cocktail table trim assembly
(270):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the trim assembly (400) to the cocktail
table trim assembly (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the trim assembly (355):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive loctite 406 to the bonded part edging grommets
(395). Attach the edging grommet (395) to the feature strip assembly
(385) and earth stud (390).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg
F).</para></note>
<note><para>Refer to Figure 30 Parts List for Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (370) with two
hexagonal head screws (375) and two flat washers (380).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the trim assembly (355) with two countersunk
head screws (360) and two flat washers (365).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the capping assembly (340) with one
pan head screw (345) and one flat washer (350).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the capping assembly (325) with three
pan head screws (330) and three flat washers (335).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the capping assembly (310) with two
pan head screws (315) and two flat washers (320).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (295) with two
countersunk head screws (300) and two flat washers (305).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cocktail table trim assembly (270)
with two countersunk head screws (275) four hexagon head screws (280,
285) and four flat washers (290, 292).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the capping assembly (260) with two
countersunk head screws (265).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (245) with two
hexagon head screws (250) and two flat washers (255).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the button assembly (230) with one
pan head screw (235) and one flat washer (240).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (195):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive loctite 406 to the bonded part edging grommet
(225) and attach the edging grommet (225) to the bracket assembly
(195).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg
F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (210) with one countersunk
head screw (215) and one flat washer (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (195) with two
hexagon head screws (200) and two flat washers (205).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one bracket assembly (185) and one
threaded rod (190) to the cocktail table equipped (90).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cover (170) with four hexagon
head screws (175) and four flat washers (180).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (155) with two
hexagon head screws (160) and two flat washers (165).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Assemble the flap
closeout assembly (120):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the closeout assembly (150):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the closeout flap (153) to the closeout
assembly (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply adhesive DP8825NS to two bonded part hinge blocks (151,
152). Attach two hinge blocks (151, 152) to the closeout assembly
(150).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the closeout assembly (150) to the
flap closeout assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two springs (140, 145) to the flap
closeout assembly (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the block hinge (130) with two pins
(135).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the flap closeout
assembly (120) with two countersunk head screws (125).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two cocktail table brackets (105)
with four hexagon head screws (110) and four flat washers (115).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cocktail table equipped (90) with
eight hexagon head screws (95) and eight flat washers (100). Torque
the hexagon head screws (95) to 4.0 Nm (2.9 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the armrest assembly (70):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (75) with three
hexagon head screws (80) and three flat washers (85).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the armrest assembly (40):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>If removed, attach the bonded part trim leather (65) with 3M
Scotch Weld 2000 B/A BLUE.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 48 hours at 24 deg C (75.2 deg F)
or room temperature.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>If removed, attach the bonded part armrest foam (60) to the
armrest assembly (70) with adhesive Alpha S708.</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 30 minutes at 16 deg C to 27 deg
C (60.8 deg F to 80.6 deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the placard indicator
backrest (58) to the armrest assembly (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the armrest assembly (40) with three
hexagon head screws (45, 50) and three flat washers (55). Torque the
hexagon head screws (45) to 2.3 Nm (1.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the footwell panel assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (20) to the trim
panel assembly (35) with three hexagon self-locking nuts (25) and
three flat washers (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the footwell panel assembly (5) with
two pan head screws (10) and two flat washers (15). Torque the pan
head screws (10) to 2.3 Nm (1.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-440-008-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Cocktail Table Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 12) to the
Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cocktail table assembly (5-150,
6-150) to the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 12 IPL for the Cocktail Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="019"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-019-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Meal Table Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 11):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the meal table assembly (5):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the leaf table assembly
(455):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3><revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive DP8825NS to the stopper (515). Attach the
bonded part stopper (515) to the leaf table assembly (455).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the leaf table (510) to the leaf table
assembly (455).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 2701 (with activator 7649) to the
threads of countersunk head screw (505). Attach the bearing (500)
with eight countersunk head screws (505). Torque the eight countersunk
head screws (505) with 0.6 Nm (0.4 lbf.ft).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 30 minutes at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the tray table cover (485) with twelve
pan head screws (490) and twelve flat washers (495).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the V-Groove track (480).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the end guide cam follower (470) with
two countersunk head screws (475).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the guide cam follower (460) with
eight countersunk head screws (465).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the film (445) and transfer tapes
(450) to the meal table assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the arm leaf mounting assembly (405):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the arm leaf (440).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive DP8825NS to the support leafs (435). Attach
two support leafs (435).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the pad friction (430) and two compression
springs (425).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the pad retainer (415) with two countersunk
head screws (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 2701 (with activator 7649) to the
threads of socket head screw (410). Attach the arm leaf mounting assembly
(405) with eight socket head screws (410). Torque the eight socket
head screws (410) with 0.6 Nm (0.4 lbf.ft).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 30 minutes at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the middle arm assembly (290):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach six stop pads (401, 402).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the middle arm (400) and spring plunger
(395).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY IS REMOVED, MAKE SURE THAT
THE SLIDES DO NOT DISCONNECT FROM THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY RAIL. IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE SLIDES AND RAIL WILL OCCUR.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the rail (385) with nine socket head screws (390). Torque
the eighteen socket head screws (390) with 0.3 Nm (0.2 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>WHEN THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY IS REMOVED, MAKE SURE THAT
THE SLIDES DO NOT DISCONNECT FROM THE SLIDE ASSEMBLY RAIL. IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE SLIDES AND RAIL WILL OCCUR.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach two rails (375) with eighteen socket head screws (380).
Torque the eighteen socket head screws (380) with 0.3 Nm (0.2 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach six carriages (365, 370).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bolt (360) and spring (355) to
the middle arm assembly (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the stop pad (351).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the front arm latch assembly (320):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the front arm latch (335) with two
cam followers (340), two flat washers (345) and bolt (350).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the front arm latch assembly (320)
with one special head screw (325) and one flat washer (330).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the plate cover (310) with three countersunk
head screws (315).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the middle arm assembly (290) with
ten socket head screws (295), one hexagonal nut (300) and one washer
(305). Torque the ten socket head screws (295) with 0.6 Nm (0.4 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive DP8825NS to the arm leaf support pad (285).
Attach the bonded part arm leaf support pad (285) to the arm leaf
support (275).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the arm leaf support (275) with two
countersunk head screws (280).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the meal table handle (265) with four
countersunk head screws (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the arm lower assembly (145):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the lower arm (260) to the arm lower
assembly (145).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive DP8825NS to two bonded covers (250) and one
bonded friction pad (255). Attach two covers (250) and one bonded
friction pad (255) and five stop pads (256) to the lower arm (260).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive full cure time is 24 hours at 23 deg C (73.4
deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the block latch (240) with two countersunk
head screws (245).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two rails (230) with twenty-two socket
head screws (235). Torque the socket head screws (235) to 0.3 Nm (0.2
lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach four carriages (220, 225).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two friction pads (215) and two springs
(210).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two pad retainers (200) with four
countersunk head screws (205).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install one spring (190) and one bolt (195)
to the arm latch assembly (155).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble the arm latch assembly (155):</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the arm latch (170) with two cam followers
(175), two flat washers (180) and one bolt (185).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the arm latch assembly (155) with
one special head screw (160) and one flat washer (165).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 2701 (with activator 7649) to the
threads of socket head screw (150). Attach the arm lower assembly
(145) with twenty socket head screws (150). Torque the socket head
screws (150) with 0.6 Nm (0.4 lbf.ft).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 30 minutes at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the base plate assembly (80):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the block cam follower (130) and the
base plate (140) and the stop pad (136) with five countersunk head
screws (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two guide cam followers (110) and
two pad frictions (125) with four countersunk head screws (115) and
four compression springs (120).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two rear supports (100) with four
countersunk head screws (105).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket (90) with two countersunk
head screws (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 2701 (with activator 7649) to the
threads of socket head screw (85). Attach the base plate assembly
(80) with twenty socket head screws (85). Torque the twenty socket
head screws (85) with 0.6 Nm (0.4 lbf.ft).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 30 minutes at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the block latch assembly (30):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><revst><prcitem><para>Attach the block latch (75) with the
spring (70), the bearing (66) and the plunger (65).</para></prcitem>
<revend></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the touch latch (55) with two countersunk
head screws (60).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the retaining plate (45) with one
countersunk head screw (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the block latch assembly (30) to the
meal table assembly (5) with three hexagonal head screws (35) and
three flat washers (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE MEAL TABLE IS IN THE FULLY DEPLOYED
POSITION BEFORE INSTALLATION INTO THE FURNITURE ASSEMBLY. IF YOU DO
NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<revend><para>Attach the meal table assembly (5) with seven countersunk
head screws (10, 15), three socket head screws (20) and three washers
(25).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="440" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-440-009-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Attach the Meal Table Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 11) to the
Furniture Assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE MEAL TABLE IS IN THE FULLY DEPLOYED
POSITION BEFORE INSTALLATION INTO THE FURNITURE ASSEMBLY. IF YOU DO
NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<revend><para>Attach the meal table installation (5-155, 6-155) to
the furniture assemblies (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and Fig. 6).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 11 IPL for the Meal Table Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="020"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-020-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the STD Row Electrical Brackets Installation (Ref.
IPL Fig. 10A):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(490):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bracket assembly
(505):</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the support bracket (530).</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two cable clamps (535) with four covers
(545, 550) and two hexagon head screws (540).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach four cable clamps (515) to the support
bracket (530) with four hexagon head screws (520) and four flat washers
(525).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (510)
to the support bracket (530).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Figure 30 Parts List for Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C: Attach the bracket assembly
(490) with three hexagon head screws (495) and three flat washers
(500).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1J and 1P: Assemble the disconnect
bracket assembly (470):</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (485)
to the bracket assembly (470).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bracket assembly (470) with four
hexagon head screws (475) and four flat washers (480).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(445):</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (460)
to the disconnect bracket assembly (445).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Figure 30 Parts List for the Earth/Ground Stud
Assembly details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1G, 1H, 1J, 1M, 1N and 1P: Attach
the disconnect bracket assembly (445) with two hexagon head screws
(450) and two flat washers (455).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect TPCU bracket (430)
with two hexagon head screws (435) and two flat washers (440).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Assemble the sub
bracket assembly (410):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (425)
to the sub bracket assembly (410).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Attach the sub
bracket assembly (410) with two hexagon head screws (415) and two
flat washers (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the ISPS bracket assembly (385):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the ISPS bracket (405).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (400)
to the ISPS bracket (405).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the ISPS bracket assembly (385) with
four hexagon head screws (390) and four flat washers (395).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1K
and 1L: Assemble the harness support bracket assembly (345):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the harness support bracket (380).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (375)
to the harness support bracket assembly (380).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two cable clamps (360) to the harness
support bracket (380) with two hexagon head screws (365) and two flat
washers (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the harness support bracket assembly
(345) with one hexagon head screw (350) and one flat washer (355).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Attach one cable
clamp (330) with one hexagon head screw (335) and one flat washer
(340).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Assemble the support
bracket assembly (295):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (325) to the support
bracket assembly (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (310) to the support
bracket (325) with one hexagon head screw (315) and one flat washer
(320).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket assembly (295)
with one hexagon head screw (300) and one flat washer (305).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the switch bracket assembly (270):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the switch bracket (290) to the switch
bracket assembly (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the switch bracket assembly (270)
with two hexagon head screws (275) and two flat washers (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the electrical bracket assembly
(245):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the structure electrical bracket
(265).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (260)
to the electrical bracket (265).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the electrical bracket assembly (245)
with two or one hexagon head screws (250) and two or one flat washers
(255).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1M and 1N:
Install the support bracket (240).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1M and 1N:
Assemble the harness support bracket assembly (175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the support bracket assembly
(210).</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the support bracket (235).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (220) to the support
bracket (235) with three hexagon head screws (225) and three flat
washers (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (215)
to the support bracket (235).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(195):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (205)
to the disconnect bracket assembly (195).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket assembly (195)
with six or four pop rivets (200).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1M, and 1N:
Attach the harness support bracket assembly (175) with five hexagon
head screws (180, 185) and five flat washers (190).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the electrical bracket assembly
(150):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the electrical structure bracket (170).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (165)
to the electrical structure bracket (170).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the electrical bracket assembly (150)
with two hexagon head screws (155) and two flat washers (160).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the support plate equipped
assembly (110):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the panasonic next plate (135) with
four plunger nylatch (140) and four grommet nylatch (145).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach four quarter turn fasteners (125)
with eight pop rivets (130).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (115)
to the Panasonic next plate (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install two support brackets (105).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the next HPS box assembly (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the HPS box assembly
(90):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the HPS bracket (100).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (95)
to the HPS bracket (100).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the HPS box assembly
(55):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach four quarter turn fasteners (80) with
eight pop rivets (85).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the HPS bracket (65) with two plunger
nylatch (70), two grommet nylatch (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (60)
to the HPS bracket (65).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the next HPS box assembly (35) with
six hexagon head screws (40, 45) and six flat washers (50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (30).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (25) to the
disconnect bracket assembly (5).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (20)
to the disconnect bracket (25).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket assembly (5)
with two hexagon head screws (10) and two flat washers (15).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="030"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-030-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the STD Row Electrical Brackets Installation (Ref.
IPL Fig. 10):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(505):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (640).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach three or two earth/ground stud assembly
(630) to the disconnect bracket (640).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Attach the support
bracket (615) to the disconnect bracket (640) with two hexagon head
screws (620) and two flat washers (625).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Attach the cable clamp (600) to the disconnect
bracket (640) with one hexagon head screw (605), one flat washer (610).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1K and 1L: Attach two
clamps (580) to the disconnect bracket (640) with one hexagon head
screw (585), one flat washer (590) and one spacer (595).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Attach twelve or three clamps (560) to the
disconnect bracket (640) with four or one hexagon head screws (565),
one or four flat washers (570) and one or four spacers (575).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1M, 1N and 1P: Attach six or two clamps (545) to the disconnect bracket
(640) with three or one hexagon head screws (550) and three or one
flat washers (555).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1M, 1N and 1P: Attach eight or four clamps (525) to the disconnect
bracket (640) with two hexagon head screws (530, 531), two or one
flat washers (535) and two or one spacers (540).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket assembly (505)
with two hexagon head screws (510), two flat washers (515) and two
spacer (520).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (490) with one hexagon
head screw (495) and one flat washer (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1K and 1L: Assemble
and attach the bracket assembly (455):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (485).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (480)
to the disconnect bracket assembly (455).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable mount tie (470) to the disconnect
bracket (485) with one countersunk head screw (475).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1K and 1L: Attach the
disconnect bracket assembly (455) with two hexagon head screws (460)
and two flat washers (465).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Assemble the disconnect
bracket assembly (410):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (450).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (445)
to the disconnect bracket (450).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (425) to the disconnect
bracket (450) with one hexagon head screw (430) and one flat washer
(435).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Attach the disconnect
bracket assembly (410) with two hexagon head screws (415) and two
flat washers (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Assemble the support
bracket assembly (375):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (405).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (390) to the support
bracket (405) with one hexagon head screw (395) and one flat washer
(400).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Attach the support
bracket assembly (375) with two hexagon head screws (380) and two
flat washers (385).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the support bracket assembly
(275):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach and assemble the disconnect bracket
assembly (355).</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (370).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(360) to the disconnect bracket (370). as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the duotec
fasteners (360) and the disconnect bracket (370).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the duotec fasteners (360) in position
on to thedisconnect bracket (370).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the duotec fasteners
(360).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(305):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (350).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two quarter turn receptables (340)
with four pop rivets (345) to the disconnect bracket (350).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (330)
to the disconnect bracket (350).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach four cable clamp (340) to the disconnect
bracket (350) with four hexagon head screws (320) and four flat washers
(325).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket assembly (305)
with ten pop rivets (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the connector support (290) with one
hexagon head screw (295) and one flat washer (300).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket assembly (275)
with four hexagon head screws (280) and four flat washers (285).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (260) with one hexagon
head screw (265) and one flat washer (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the support box plate
assembly (230).</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-028-a01"></refint>) to
attach the support box plate (245) with two quarter turn studs (250)
and two quarter turn retainers (255).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (235)
to the box support plate (245).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the disconnect bracket
assembly (165):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (225).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook fasteners (220)
to the disconnect bracket (225) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (220) and the disconnect bracket (225).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fasteners (220)
in position on to the disconnect bracket (225).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fasteners (220).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (215)
to the disconnect bracket (225).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (195) to the disconnect
bracket (225) with one hexagon head screw (200) and one flat washer
(205).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (180) to the disconnect
bracket (225) with one hexagon head screw (185) and one flat washer
(190).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket assembly 165)
with two hexagon head screws (170) and two flat washers (175).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (150) with two
hexagon head screws (155) and two flat washers (160).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Attach the support bracket
(135) with two hexagon head screws (140) and two flat washers (145).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (120) with two
hexagon head screws (125) and two flat washers (130).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the reading light bracket assembly
(90):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the reading light bracket (115) to
the reading light bracket assembly (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(105) to the reading light bracket (115) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (105) and the  reading light bracket (115).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (105)
in position on to the  reading light bracket (115).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (105).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1E, 1F, 1K and 1L: Attach the
reading light bracket assembly (90) with two hexagon head screws (95)
and two flat washers (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A: Attach the support bracket
assembly (75) with two hexagon head screws (80) and two flat washers
(85).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1D: Assemble the reading
light sup bracket assembly (35):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the reading light bracket (70).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tape (60) to the reading light bracket
(70) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the double-sided
tape (60) and the reading light bracket (70).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tape (60) in position
on to the reading light bracket (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the double-sided
tape (60).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(55) to the reading light bracket (70) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (55) and the reading light bracket (70).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (55)
in position on to the reading light bracket (70).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (55).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach reading light sup bracket assembly
(35) with two hexagon head screws (40), two self-locking nuts (45)
and four flat washers (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1M, 1N
and 1P: Attach the reading light bracket assembly (15) with one hexagon
head screw (20) and one flat washer (25).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1M, 1N
and 1P: Attach the cable tie (5) with one countersunk head screw (10).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="021"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-021-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the EFR Electrical Brackets Installation (Ref. IPL
Fig. 9):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the TPCU disconnect bracket (955)
with two hexagon head screws (960) and two flat washers (965).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the bracket
(950) to the electrical bracket installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble the disconnect
bracket (925):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (945).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two earth/ground stud assembly (940)
to the disconnect bracket (945).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the disconnect
bracket (925) with two hexagon head screws (930) and two flat washers
(935).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Assemble the harness
support bracket assembly (885):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the harness support bracket (920).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two earth/ground stud assembly (915)
to the harness support bracket (920).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two cable clamp (900) to the harness
support bracket (920) with two hexagon head screws (910) and two flat
washers (905).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the harness
support bracket assembly (885) with two hexagon head screws (890)
and two flat washers (895).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the ISPS bracket assembly (860):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the ISPS bracket (880).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (875)
to the ISPS bracket (880).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the ISPS bracket assembly (860) with
four hexagon head screws (865) and four flat washers (870).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the switch bracket assembly (835):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the switch bracket (855) to the switch
bracket assembly (835).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply the thread locking compound Loctite
222 (with activator 7649) to the threads of the hexagon head screws
(840). Attach the switch bracket assembly (835) with two hexagon head
screws (840) and two flat washers (845).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the electrical bracket assembly
(810):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the structure electrical bracket
(830).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two earth/ground stud assembly (825)
to the structure electrical bracket (830).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply the thread locking compound Loctite
222 (with activator 7649) to the threads of the hexagon head screws
(815). Attach the electrical bracket assembly (810) with two or one
hexagon head screws (815) and two or one flat washers (820).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the support
bracket (805). to the electrical bracket installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the harness support bracket
assembly (740):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble and attach
the support bracket assembly (775):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the support bracket (800).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (795)
to the support bracket (800).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach three cable clamps (780) with three
hexagon head screws (785) and three flat washers (790).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(760):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (770)
to the disconnect bracket assembly (760).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket assembly (760)
with four pop rivets (765).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the harness
support bracket assembly (740) with five hexagon head screws (745,
750) and five flat washers (755).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the electrical bracket
assembly (715):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the structure electrical bracket
(735).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (730)
to the structure electrical bracket (735).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply the thread locking compound Loctite
222 (with activator 7649) to the threads of the hexagon head screws
(720). Attach the electrical bracket assembly (715) with two hexagon
head screws (720) and two flat washers (725).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the support plate equipped
assembly (675):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the Panasonic next plate (700) with
four nylatchplunger (705) and four nylatch grommet (710).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach four quarter turn receptacle fasteners
(690) with eight pop rivets (695).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (680)
to the Panasonic next plate (700).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (670) to the electrical
bracket installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the next HPS box assembly (600):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the HPS bracket assembly
(655):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the HPS bracket (665).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (660)
to the HPS bracket (665).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the HPS box assembly
(620):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach four quarter turn fasteners (645)
with eight pop rivets (650).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the HPS bracket (630) with two nylatch
plunger (635) and two nylatch grommet (640).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (625)
to the HPS bracket (630).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply the thread locking compound Loctite
222 (with activator 7649) to the threads of the hexagon head screws
(610). Attach the next HPS box assembly (600) with six hexagon head
screws (605, 610) and six flat washers (615).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket assembly (595)
to the electrical bracket installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(570):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (590).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (585)
to the disconnect bracket (590).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket assembly (570)
with two hexagon head screws (575) and two flat washers (580).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(430):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (565).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the support
bracket (550) to the disconnect bracket (565) with two hexagon head
screws (555) and two flat washers (560).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach three earth/ground stud assemblies
(540) to the disconnect bracket (565).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1D: Attach the cable
clamp (525) to the disconnect bracket (565) with one hexagon head
screw (530) and one flat washer (535).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1C and 1D: Attach four cable
clamps (505) to the disconnect bracket (565) with one hexagon head
screw (510), one flat washer (515) and one spacer (520).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach four cable
clamps (485) to the disconnect bracket (565) with one hexagon head
screw (490), one flat washer (495) and one spacer (500).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach six or three cable clamps (465) to
the disconnect bracket (565) with two or one hexagon head screws (470),
two or one flat washers (475) and two or one spacers (480).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach four or two cable clamps (450) to
the disconnect bracket (565) with two or one hexagon head screws (455)
and two or one flat washers (460).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket assembly (430)
with two hexagon head screws (435), two flat washers (440) and two
nylon spacers (445).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (415) with one hexagon
head screw (420) and one flat washer (425).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket assembly
(370):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (410).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (405)
to the disconnect bracket (410).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (385) to the disconnect
bracket (410) with one hexagon head screw (390) and one flat washer
(395).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the disconnect
bracket assembly (370) with two hexagon head screws (375) and two
flat washers (380).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Assemble the support
bracket assembly (335):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the support bracket (365).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (350) to the support
bracket (365) with one hexagon head screw (355) and one flat washer
(360).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the support
bracket assembly (335) with two hexagon head screws (340) and two
flat washers (345).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the support bracket assembly (235):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the disconnect bracket
assembly (315):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (330).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(320) to the disconnect bracket (330) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (320) and the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><revst><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(320) in position on to the bonded surface.</para><revend></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (320).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the disconnect bracket
assembly (265):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (310).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach two quarter turn receptacle (300)
to the disconnect bracket (310) with four pop rivets (305).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (290)
to the disconnect bracket (310).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach four cable clamps (275) to the disconnect
bracket (310) with four hexagon head screws (280) and four flat washers
(285).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket assembly (265)
with ten pop rivets (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the connector support (250) with one
hexagon head screw (255) and one flat washer (260).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket assembly (235)
with four hexagon head screws (240) and four flat washers (245).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the support box plate
assembly (205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the DZUS tamper resistant stud key (<refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-26-62-99a-028-a01"></refint>) to
attach the box support plate (220) with two quarter turn screws (225)
and two quarter turn retainers (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach one earth/ground stud assembly (210)
to the support box plate (220).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (190) with one hexagon
head screw (195) and one flat washer (200).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the disconnect bracket (125):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the disconnect bracket (185).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive hook fastener
(180) to the disconnect bracket (125) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive hook fastener (180) and the bonded surface.</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fastener (180)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fastener (180).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the earth/ground stud (175) to the
disconnect bracket (185).</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 30 IPL for the Earth/Ground Stud Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (155) to the disconnect
bracket (185) with one hexagon head screw (160) and one flat washer
(165).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cable clamp (140) to the disconnect
bracket (185) with one hexagon head screw (145) and one flat washer
(150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the disconnect bracket (125) with
two hexagon head screws (130) and two flat washers (135).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (110) with two
hexagon head screws (115) and two flat washers (120).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the support bracket (95) with two
hexagon head screws (100) and two flat washers (105).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the reading light bracket assembly
(70):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the reading light bracket (90) to
the reading light bracket assembly (70).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(86) to the reading light bracket assembly (70) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (86) and tothe bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (86)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (86).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<revend></prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the reading
light bracket assembly (70) with one hexagon head screw (75), one
flat washer (80) and one spacer (81).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the cable
tie (60) with one countersunk head screw (65) and one spacer (66).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>For Assembly 1: Apply the thread locking compound Loctite 222
(with activator 7649) to the hexagon head screws (50) . Attach the
support bracket (45) with two hexagon head screws (50) and two flat
washers (55).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Assemble the reading
light sup bracket assembly (5):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the reading light bracket detail
(40).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT THE DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN
THE CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS
A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Attach the double-sided tape (30) to the reading light bracket
detail (40) as follow:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
double-sided tape (30) and to the bonded surface.</para><revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the double-sided tape (30) in position
on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the double-sided
tape (30).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><revst><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(25) to the reading light bracket detail (40) as follows:</para><revend>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive duotec fasteners (25) to the bonded surface.</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (25)
in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (25).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the reading
light sup bracket assembly (5) with two hexagon head screws (10),
two self-locking nuts (15) and four flat washers (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="022"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-022-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Suite STD Row Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL
Fig. 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1G and 1L: Install two cable
clamps (685) with two hexagon head screws (690) and two flat washers
(695).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1G and 1L: Install the
cable clamps (655) with spacers (680) with the hexagon head screws
(660, 665) and the flat washers (670).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the cable clamps (640) with two hexagon
head screws (645) and two flat washers (650).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the tie base (630) with one countersunk
head screw (635).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the clamps (615) with one hexagon
head screws (620) and one flat washers (625).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the clamps (605) and spacers (610)
with one hexagon head screw (590) and one flat washer (595).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the seat box (585) with six dust
caps (576, 577, 580).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1M, 1N
and 1P: Connect the IFE harness (570) at connectors P4A and J10 with
four countersunk head screws (575).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1D, 1J and 1N: Connect the
IFE harness (560) at connectors P2, P1, J1A, J2A and P1G with eight
countersunk head screws (565).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the ISPS (555) with two protective
covers (550).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (545) at connectors
P3, P2 and P20.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach two clamps (535) and one spacer (540)
with one hexagon head screw (525) and one flat washer (530).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the next premium expansion unit (520)
with two dust caps (510) and one fight cap (515).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assemblies (475, 480,
485, 490, 495, 500, 505) at connectors S01, D10J, P2, J1, P800, D10P,
P10, P1S, P1, P8, P200, P204, J13, P2, P1, P21, D24J, P101, P201 and
P100A.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the cover assemblies
(445, 460).</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the covers (446, 461) to the cover
assemblies (445, 460).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(450, 465) to the cover assemblies (445, 460) as follows:</para>
</prcitem><revend>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (450, 465) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (450,
465) in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (450, 465).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the tie bases (435) with the countersunk
head screws (440).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: Install the tie bases (430).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N and 1P: Connect the bonding assemblies (425) at connectors
GD03A and GD18.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect bonding assemblies (420) at connectors
GD03A, GD03B, GS-1, GD11A, GD02 and GD18.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect one or two bonding assembly (405)
at connectors GD02, GD03A, GD03B and GD13 with one or two nuts (410)
and one or two flat washers (415).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the bondingassemblies (400) at connectors
GD02 and GD17.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Connect the bonding assemblies (395) at connectors
GD04 and GD03B.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1L, 1M,
1N and 1P: Connect the bonding assembly (380) at connectors GD10,
GD03, GD05 and GD17 with two nuts (385) and two flat washers (390).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the bonding assemblies (365) at connectors
GD04, GD05, GD11A, GD14A, GD03A, GD08, GD14B, GD03C, GD10, GD11B,
GD14, GD03C, E1 and ECCB GND with one or two or six or five nuts (370)
and one or two or six or five washers (375).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the bonding assemblies (350) at connectors
J1, GD05, GD02 and GD03C with three nuts (355) and three washers (360).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the bonding assembly (345) at connectors
GD1B, GD06 and P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the bonding assembly (330) at connectors
GD03B, GD07A, GD06, GD03C, GD08, GD7A, GD01B, GD05, GD16, GD07B, GD09,
GD01A, GD03A, GD13, GD19 and GD15 with the nuts (335) and flat washers
(340).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (320) at connectors
P7-1, P14, P7, P3 and J10 with two countersunk screws (325).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Connect the harness assembly (305) at connectors
D14J and D15P with two countersunk head screws (310) and two flat
washers (315).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the bonding assembly (290) at connector
GD06 with one nut (295) and one washer (300).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the controller box (285).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M and 1N: Connect the IFE harness (275) at connectors J10 and
P10 with four countersunk head screws (280).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M and 1N: Attach the peripheral bar (270).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M and 1N: Install the monitor (260) with four socket head screws
(265).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (250) at connectors
P4B and J10 with four countersunk head screws (255).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the cable protections (245) to Suite
STD Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (240) at connectors
P13, P1 and P10.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (235) at connectors
P1 and P2 and attach the conduct (230).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the smart audio adapter (210), the
remote jack (215), the outlet pin (220) and the next triple pin audio
RJM (225) at connectors J1, J2, P1, P7 and P14.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach seven cable clamps (195, 200) with
one or two spacers (205) with five hexagon head screws (175, 180,
185) and five flat washers (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the fixing base (170).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the euphony harness (165) at connectors
P1A5, P4 and P1A2.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the euphony microphone (155) at connector
P1A6 with two countersunk head screws (160).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (140) at connectors
J6, D16J and J4 with two countersunk head screws (145) and two flat
washers (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1J, 1L, 1M, 1N and 1P: Connect the harness assembly (125) at connectors
D15J, J9, J11, J8, J10 and P3 with two countersunk head screws (130)
and two flat washers (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1H, 1J, 1M and 1N:
Connect the harness assembly (120) at connectors J12 and P11.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the cable protections (110, 115)
to Suite STD Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install four RGBW lights (80, 85, 90, 95)
and two mood lights (100, 105) at connector P1.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (65) at connectors
J5, J3, D23, P204, P1, J17, J15, J18, D03P, D039, P100, P2, P3, P4,
J1, J2 and J100A with two countersunk head screws (70) and two flat
washers (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1L, 1M and 1N: Install the cable protection (60) to Suite STD Electrical
Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the cable protection (55) to Suite
STD Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the main PCU (40) at connector J1
with two socket head screws (45) and two flat washers (50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1B: Connect the cable
LRU interface (35) at connector P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the hall effect sensor (20) with
one socket head screw (25) and one hexagon nut (30) at connector P1.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the reading light (10) at connector
P30 with three socket head screws (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the tie wraps (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="023"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-023-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Suite EFR Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
7):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach two cable
clamps (855) with one hexagon head screw (860) and one flat washer
(865).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one or two cable clamps (840) with
one or two hexagon head screws (845) and one or two flat washers (850).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one cable clamp (815) and three cable
clamps (835) with one hexagon head screw (820), one flat washer (825)
and one spacer (830).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A and 1C: Attach two or
three cable clamps (795) and one spacer (810) with two or three hexagon
head screws (800) and two or three flat washers (805).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach two cable clamp (775) and one spacer
(790) with two hexagon head screws (780) and two flat washers (785).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach four cable clamps (760) with four
hexagon head screws (765) and four flat washers (770).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one cable clamp (740) and one spacer
(755) with one hexagon head screw (745) and one flat washer (750).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one cable clamp (720) and one spacer
(735) with one hexagon head screw (725) and one flat washer (730).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach two cable clamps (700) and two cable
clamps (715) with two hexagon head screws (705) and two flat washers
(710).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one cable clamp (665) and one spacer
(695) with one hexagon head screw (685) and one flat washer (690).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one cable clamp (665) with one hexagon
head screw (670) and one flat washer (675).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the seat box (585) with two dust
caps (580).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Connect the IFE harness
(576) with four countersunk head screws (577) at connectors P4A and
J10.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Connect the IFE harness
(570) at connectors P6B and J6B with four countersunk head screws
(575).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Connect the IFE harness
(560) at connectors P2, P1, J1A, J2A and P1G with eight countersunk
head screws (565).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the ISPS (555) with two protective
covers (550).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (545) at connectors
P3, P2 and P20.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the next premium expansion unit (520)
with two dust caps (510) and one flight cap (515).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Connect the harness assembly
(500B) with two countersunk head screws (501) and two flat washers
(502) at connectors J15, P200, P204 and J1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the conduct
(491) and connect the harness assembly (495) at connectors P10, P1S,
P1 and P8.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assemblies (480, 485,
490, 505) at connectors S01, D10J, P2, J1, P800, D10P, P10, P1S, P1,
P8, P2, P1 and P21.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the cover assemblies
(450, 465):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2><revst>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the covers (456, 471) to the cover
assemblies (450, 465).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(455, 470) to the cover assemblies (450, 465):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (455, 470) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (455,
470) in position on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (455, 470).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<revend></prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach two or three tie bases (440) with
two or three countersunk head screws (445).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect two bonding assemblies (430, 435)
at connectors GD03A, GS-1, GD03A, GD18, GD10, GD13, GD03 and GD11B.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach one to two bonding assemblies (415)
with two nuts (420) and two or three flat washers (425) at connectors
GD02, GD03A, GD03B and GD18.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect three bonding assemblies (405, 410)
at connectors GD04, GD03, GD02 and GD17.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach two or one bonding assemblies (390)
with two nuts (395) and two flat washers (400) at connectors GD10,
GD03, GD10 and GD03B.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bonding assemblies (375) with
the nuts (380) and flat washers (385) at connectors GD04, GD05, GD10,
GD11A, GD14A, GD03A, GD08, GD14B and GD03C.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach three bonding assemblies (360) with
two nuts (365) and two flat washers (370) at connectors GD05, GD02
and J1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the bonding assemblies (355) at connectors
GD01B, GD06 and P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<revend>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bonding assembly (345) at connectors
GD03B, GD07A, GD15, GD03C, GD08, GD07A, GD01B, GD01A, GD03A, GD13,
GD19, GD05, GD16, GD09 and GD15 with twelve or ten nuts (345) and
twelve or ten flat washers (350).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (330) with two countersunk
head screws (335) at connectors P7-1, P14, P7, P3 and J10.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (315) with two
countersunk head screws (320) and two flat washers (325) at connectors
D14J and D15P.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the bonding assembly (300) with one
nut (305) and one washer (310) at connector GD06.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the lighting controller box (295).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (285) at connectors
J10 and P10 with four countersunk head screws (290).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the peripheral bar (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the monitor (270) with four socket
head screws (275).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (260) at connectors
P4B and J10 with four countersunk head screws (265).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the cable protection (255) to the
Suite EFR Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (250) at connectors
P13, P1 and P10.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the conduct (240) and connect the
IFE harness assembly (245) at connectors P1 and P12.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the smart audio adapter (220), the
remote jack (225), the outlet unit (230) and the next triple pin audio
RJM (235) at connectors J1, J2, J1, P7, P14 and P1.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IFE harness (175) at connectors
P5B and P11.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the next premium cradle (170) at
connector J2.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the next premium handset (165).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach three fixing bases (160).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the euphony harness (155) at connectors
P1A5, P4 and P1A2.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the euphony microphone (145) at connector
P1A6 with two countersunk head screws (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (130) with two
countersunk head screws (135) and two flat washers (140) at connectors
J6, D16J and J4.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (115) with two
countersunk head screws (120) and two flat washers (125) at connectors
D15J, J8, J9, J10, J11, J12 and P3.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Connect the harness
assembly (110) at connectors J12 and P11.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the cable protections (100, 105)
to Suite EFR Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install four RGBW lights (70, 75, 80, 85)
and two mood lights (90, 95) at each connector P1.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deleted.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (60) at connectors
J5, J3, P100, P2, P3, P4, D03P and P1 to the EFR Electrical Installation
Suite.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B and 1C: Attach the cable
protection (55) to the EFR Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cable protection (50) to the EFR
Electrical Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install and connect the main PCU (35) at
connector J1 with two socket head screws (40) and two flat washers
(45).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Connect the cable LRU interface
(31) at connector P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install and connect the hall effect sensor
(20) at connector P1 with one socket head screw (25) and one hexagon
nut (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install and connect the reading light (10)
at connector P30 with three socket head screws (15).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the tie wraps (5).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="024"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-024-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the STD Row Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the composite integration (535) to
the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 27 IPL for the Composite Integration details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the transition track fitting (525)
and e-nut fitting bolt (530).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and install the foot fitting kit
installation (370):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the EQ foot fitting assembly (500):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (520) to the
EQ foot fitting assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tape (520) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tape (520) in position
on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (520).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the EQ foot fitting assembly (500)
with two hexagon head screws (505), two nuts (510) and four flat washers
(515). Torque the hexagon head screws (505) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the EQ foot fitting assembly (470):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (495) to the
EQ foot fitting assembly (470).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tape (495) and to the bonded surface.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tape (495) in position
on to the bonded surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (495).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend></prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the EQ foot fitting assembly (470)
with two hexagon head screws (475), two nuts (480), four flat washers
(485) and two bearing bushes (490). Torque the hexagon head screws
(475) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the spacer (445):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (465) to the
spacer (445) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<revst><para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the
self-adhesive tape (465) and to the cushion assembly (350).</para>
<revend>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<revst>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tape (465) in position
on to the cushion assembly (350).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<revend>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (465).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install two screws (460) to the foot fitting
kit installation (370). Torque the screws (460) to 11.3 Nm (8.3 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install each of two spacers (445) with one
hexagon head screw (450) and one bearing bush (455). Torque the hexagon
head screws (450) to 21.5 Nm (15.8 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the EQ foot fitting assembly (415):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (440) to the
foot fitting assembly (415) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tape (440) and foot fitting assembly (415).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para> Push the self-adhesive tape (440) in position
on to the foot fitting assembly (415).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (440).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the EQ foot fitting assembly (415)
with two hexagon head screws (420), two nuts (425), four flat washers
(430) and two bearing bushes (435). Torque the hexagon head screws
(420) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install thefront foot fittings (395) with
two hexagon head screws (400), two nuts (405) and four flat washers
(410). Torque the hexagon head screws (400) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install two screws (390) to the foot fitting
kit installation (370). Torque the screws (390) to 11.3 Nm (8.3 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install each of two foot fitting spacer (375)
with one hexagon head screw (380) and spreader (385). Torque the hexagon
head screws (380) to 21.5 Nm (15.85 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1N, 1P and 1Q: Assemble and install the closeout pad installation
(325):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the cushion assembly
(350):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fastener (365)
to the cushion assembly (350) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
loop fastener (365) and cushion assembly (350).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive loop fastener (365)
in position on to the cushion assembly (350).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
loop fastener (365).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(360) and install the support (355) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (360) and self-adhesive duotec fasteners (360).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (360)
in position on to the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (360).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (360).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the bracket assembly (330):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(345) and install the bracket (340) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (345) and the bracket (340).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (345)
in position on to the bracket (340).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (345).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the bracket assembly (330) with two
or five countersunk head screws (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5745:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1G, 1H, 1J, 1N, 1P and 1Q: Assemble
and attach the cover assembly (322) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(323) and attach the cover bracket (324) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (323) and cover bracket (324).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fasteners (323)
in position on to the cover bracket (324).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fasteners (323).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5745:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1G, 1H, 1J, 1N, 1P and 1Q: Engage
the self-adhesive duotec fastener (321) to the STD row furniture assembly
as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para> Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (321) and STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (321)
in position on to the STD row furniture assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (321).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1F, 1M and 1T: Attach the
rear row closeout assembly (320) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 29 IPL for the Rear Row Closeout Assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the kickstrip and seals cladding installation
(315) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 23 IPL for the Kickstrip and Seals Cladding
Installation details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Assemble and attach the bump
strip installation (240):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1N, 1P and
1Q: Attach three clips (300) with six hexagon head screws (305) and
six flat washers (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1K, 1L, 1M, 1R, 1S
and 1T: Attach the clip (300) with two hexagon head screws (305) and
two flat washers (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1F, 1G, 1H, 1J 1N, 1P and
1Q: Install the bumper (275) with four hexagon head screws (285) with
four flat washers (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1K, 1L, 1M, 1R, 1S
and 1T: Install the bumper (275) with four hexagon head screws (280,
285) with four flat washers (290, 295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the IUL-DND-TTL bracket assembly
(250):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bumper electrical
assembly (260).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and install the IUL (265) and TTL
indicator (270).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the IUL-DND-TTL bracket assembly
(245) with three hexagon head screws (250) and three flat washers
(255).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A and 1E: Attach the dot door
installation (235) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 15 IPL for the Dot Door Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the N-aisle cladding installation
(230) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 24 IPL for the N-aisle Cladding Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bed infill installation
(175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Assemble the support bracket assembly
(205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(220) and install the support bracket (225) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (220) and support bracket (225).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (220)
in position on to the support bracket (225).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (220).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Attach the support bracket assembly
(205) with five hexagon head screws (210) and five flat washers (215).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the cushion assembly (180):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener
(195) and install the cushion (200) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (195) and cushion (200).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive duotec fastener (195)
in position on to the cushion (200).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (195).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1A, 1B, 1E and 1F: Attach the
cushion assembly (180) with two hexagon head screws (185) and two
flat washers (190).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Attach the cushion assembly (180).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the under seat drip tray assembly
(170) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 25 IPL for the Under Seat Drip Tray assembly
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1C, 1D, 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L,
1M, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Attach the folding armrest installation
(165) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 18 IPL for the Folding Armrest Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R and 1S: Attach the FWD fascia installation
(160) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 20 IPL for the FWD Fascia Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R and 1S: Attach the meal table assembly (155)
to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 11 IPL for the Meal Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cocktail table assembly (150)
to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 12 IPL for the Cocktail Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the upper console stowage installation
(145) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 17 IPL for the Upper Console Stowage Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the sliding door installation (140)
to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 16 IPL for the Sliding Door Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the canopy installation (135) to the
STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 28 IPL for the Canopy Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the seat recess claddings installation
(130) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 22 IPL for Seat Recess Claddings Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1G, 1H, 1J, 1K, 1L, 1M, 1N,
1P, 1Q, 1R, 1S and 1T: Attach the outboard bridge installation (125)
to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 19 IPL for the Outboard Bridge Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E and 1F:
Attach the closeout panel installation (120) to the STD row furniture
assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 14 IPL for the Closeout Panel Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A and 1B: Attach the privacy
screen installation (115) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 13 IPL for the Privacy Screen Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the vertical caps installation (110)
to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 26 IPL for the Vertical Caps Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the electrical brackets installation
(105) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 10 IPL for the Electrical Brackets Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H, 1J,
1K, 1L, 1N, 1P, 1Q, 1R and 1S: Assemble and attach the ottoman cushion
installation (10):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the ottoman cushion cover
assembly (100):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the ottoman cover (102) and the ottoman
foam (104) to the ottoman cushion cover assembly (100).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the ottoman support assembly
(65):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the transfer tapes (98) to the hinge
panel (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install two magnets (90) and hinge panel
(95).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Alpha S708 to the surface of cladding (75).
Attach the bonded part cladding (75) with six countersunk head screws
(80, 85).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 30 minutes at 16 deg C to 27 deg
C (60.8 deg F to 80.6 deg F).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook fastener (70)
to the ottoman support assembly (65) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fastener (70) and ottoman support assembly (65).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fastener (70)
in position on to the ottoman support assembly (65).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fastener (70).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the ottoman hinge assembly (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the hinge plates (45, 60) with the
hinge pin (50) and retaining ring (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install two ottoman hinge assemblies (35)
with eight countersunk head screws (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 222 (with activator 7649) to threads
of countersunk head screws (20, 30). Install two support brackets
(15, 25) with four countersunk head screws (20, 30).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the STD row electrical installation
(5) to the STD row furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 8 IPL for the STD row Electrical Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="025"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-025-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the EFR Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the composite integration (540) to
the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer Fig 27 IPL for the Composite Integration details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the transition track fitting (530)
and e-nut fitting bolt (535).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the foot fitting kit
installation (315):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble the EQ foot
fitting assembly (500):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (525) to the
EQ foot fitting assembly (500) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tape (525) and EQ foot fitting assembly (500).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tape (525) in position
on to the EQ foot fitting assembly (500).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (525).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ foot fitting assembly (500)
with two hexagon head screws (505), two nuts (510), four flat washers
(515) and two bearing bushes (520). Torque the hexagon head screws
(505) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Assemble the EQ foot
fitting assembly (470):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (495) to the
EQ foot fitting assembly (470) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tape (495) and EQ foot fitting assembly (470).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tape (495) in position
on to the EQ foot fitting assembly (470).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (495).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ foot fitting assembly (470)
with two hexagon head screws (475), two nuts (480), four flat washers
(485) and two bearing bushes (490). Torque the hexagon head screws
(475) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the EQ foot fitting assembly (445):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (465) to the
EQ foot fitting assembly (445) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tape (465) and EQ foot fitting assembly (445).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tape (465) in position
on to the EQ foot fitting assembly (445).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (465).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the EQ foot fitting assembly (445)
with two hexagon head screws (450), two nuts (455) and four flat washers
(460). Torque the hexagon head screws (450) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two screws (440) to the foot fitting
kit installation (315). Torque the screws (440) to 11.3 Nm (8.3 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the equipped spacer assemblies (420):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tapes (435) to the
equipped spacer assemblies (420) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tapes (435) and equipped spacer assemblies (420).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tapes (435) in position
on to the equipped spacer assemblies (420).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tapes (435).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two equipped spacer assemblies (420)
with two hexagon head screws (425) and two bushes (430). Torque the
hexagon head screws (425) to 21.5 Nm (15.8 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the EQ foot fitting assembly (390):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (415) to the
EQ foot fitting assembly (390) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tape (415) and EQ foot fitting assembly (390).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tape (415) in position
on to the EQ foot fitting assembly (390).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (415).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the EQ foot
fitting assembly (390) with two hexagon head screws (395), two nuts
(400), four flat washers (405) and two bearing bushes (410). Torque
the hexagon head screws (395) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the EQ foot fitting assembly (360):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the self-adhesive tape (385) to the
EQ foot fitting assembly (360) as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
tape (385) and EQ foot fitting assembly (360).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive tape (385) in position
on to the EQ foot fitting assembly (360).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
tape (385).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the EQ foot
fitting assembly (360) with two hexagon head screws (365), two nuts
(370), four flat washers (375) and two bearing bushes (380). Torque
the hexagon head screws (365) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the rear RH foot fittings (340) with
two hexagon head screws (345) and two nuts (350) and two flat washers
(355). Torque the hexagon head screws (345) to 6.8 Nm (5.0 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two screws (335) to the foot fitting
kit installation (315). Torque the screws (335) to 11.3 Nm (8.3 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two foot fitting spacers (320) with
two hexagon head screws (325) and two spreaders (330). Torque the
hexagon head screws (325) to 21.5 Nm (15.8 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the kickstrip and seals cladding installation
(310) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer Fig 23 IPL for the Kickstrip and Seals Cladding
Installation details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble and attach
the bump strip installation (245):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the clip (295) with two hexagon head
screws (300) and two flat washers (305).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the bumper (280) with two hexagon
head screws (285) and two flat washers (290).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the IUL-DND-TTL bracket assembly
(250):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bumper electrical
assembly (265).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the IUL (270) and TTL indicator (275).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the IUL-DND-TTL bracket assembly (250)
with five hexagon head screws (255) and five flat washers (260).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the dot door
installation (240) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 15 IPL for the Dot Door Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the N-aisle claddings installation
(235) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 24 IPL for the N-aisle Claddings Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the lifevest box assembly (230) to
the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 21 IPL for Lifevest Box Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the bed infill installation
(175):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble the support
bracket assembly (205):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (220) and to the support bracket (225).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the duotec fastener (220) to the support
bracket (225) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (220).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the support
bracket assembly (205) with three hexagon head screws (210) and three
flat washers (215).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Assemble the cushion
assembly (180):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (195) and to the cushion (200).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the duotec fastener (195) to the cushion
(200) in position.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
duotec fastener (195).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach the cushion assembly (180) with two
hexagon head screws (185) and two flat washers (190).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the underseat drip tray assembly (170)
to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 25 IPL for Underseat Drip Tray Assembly details.
</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the folding
armrest installation (165) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 18 IPL for the Folding Armrest Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the FWD fascia installation (160)
to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 20 IPL for the FWD Fascia Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the meal table assembly (155) to the
EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 11 IPL for the Meal Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the cocktail table assembly (150)
to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 12 IPL for the Cocktail Table Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the upper console stowage installation
(145) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 17 IPL for the Upper Console Stowage Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the sliding door installation (140)
to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 16 IPL for the Sliding Door Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the canopy installation (135) to the
EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 28 IPL for the Canopy Installation details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the seat recess claddings installation
(130) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 22 IPL for Seat Recess Claddings Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B and 1C: Attach the outboard
bridge installation (125) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 19 IPL for the Outboard Bridge Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1 and 1A: Attach the closeout
panel installation (120) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 14 IPL for the Closeout Panel Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: Attach the privacy screen
assembly (115) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 13 IPL for the Privacy Screen Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the vertical caps installation (110)
to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 26 IPL for the Vertical Caps Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the electrical brackets installation
(105) to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 9 IPL for the Electrical Brackets Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the ottoman cushion installation
(10):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and attach the ottoman cushion cover
assembly (100):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the ottoman cover (102) and the ottoman
foam (104) to the ottoman cushion cover assembly (100).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the ottoman support assembly (65):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the transfer tapes (98) to the hinge
panel (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install two magnets (90) and hinge panel
(95).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the bonded part cladding (75) with
six countersunk head screws (80, 85).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook fastener (70)
to the ottoman support assembly (65) as follows:</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN SOLVENTS AND CLEANING AGENTS ARE USED, OBEY ALL
PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY
THE MANUFACTURER. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Use Isopropyl alcohol and a lint free cloth to clean the bonded
surface.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a thin continuous coat of adhesive S708 to the self-adhesive
hook fastener (70) and ottoman support assembly (65).</para>
<note><para>Let the adhesive dry for a minimum of 30 minutes.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Push the self-adhesive hook fastener (70)
in position on to the ottoman support assembly (65).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted adhesive with lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Apply a pressure equally on the self-adhesive
hook fastener (70).</para>
<note><para>Leave the adhesive to cure for a minimum of 12 hours.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the ottoman hinge assembly (35):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Attach the hinge plates (45, 60) with the
hinge pin (50) and retaining ring (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Attach two ottoman hinge assembly (35) with
eight countersunk head screws (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN ADHESIVES ARE USED, OBEY ALL PROCEDURE INSTRUCTIONS
AND HEALTH AND SAFETY WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. THIS
WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para></warning>
<para>Apply the adhesive Loctite 222 (with activator 7649) to threads
of countersunk head screws (20, 30). Install two support brackets
(15, 20) with four countersunk head screws (20, 30).</para>
<note><para>Adhesive cure time is 3 hours at 22 deg C (72 deg F).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install the EFR electrical installation (5)
to the EFR furniture assembly.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 7 IPL for the EFR Electrical Installation
details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
