confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-026-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the Placard Kit Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 4):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Post SB25-5792: For assembly 1, 1A, 1B and
1D, If removed, attach the self-adhesive do not occupy placard (70)
to the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: If removed, attach self-adhesive literature only
placard (65) to the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1G, 1H,
1K, 1L, 1N and 1P: If removed, attach the self-adhesive fasten seat
belt placard (60) to the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1B, 1C, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H,
1J, 1K, 1L, 1M, 1N, 1P and 1Q: If removed, attach the self-adhesive
furniture indicator placard (55) to the placard kit assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive door
open placard (50) to the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive door
slide placard (45) to the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1E and 1H: If removed,
attach the self-adhesive dot panel placard (40) to the placard kit
assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive seat
indicator placard (35) to the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1A, 1B and 1C: If removed,
attach the self-adhesive fasten seat belt placard (30) to the placard
kit assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive max
stowage placard (25) to the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive door
close and latch placard (20) to the placard kit assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive cubby
seal indicator placard (15) to the placard kit assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1: If removed, attach the self-adhesive
central divider placard (10) to the placard kit assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For Assembly 1, 1D, 1E, 1F, 1G, 1H and 1J:
If removed, attach the self-adhesive central divider placard (5) to
the placard kit assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="027"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-027-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the STD Row Suite GA (Ref. IPL Fig. 3):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the loose items kit (45) to the inboard
and outboard STD row suite GA.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the data plates kit assembly (20):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach self-adhesive two serial
no and mods labels (40) to the data plates kit assembly (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive furniture
label (35) to the data plates kit assembly (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive continuation
label (30) to the data plates kit assembly (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive medium
RFID high memory label (25) to the data plates kit assembly (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the data plates kit assembly
(20) to the inboard and outboard STD row suite GA.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the placard kit assembly (15) to the
inboard and outboard STD row suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 4 IPL for the Placard Kit Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the inboard and outboard STD row furniture
assembly (10) to the inboard and outboard STD row suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 6 IPL for the Inboard and Outboard STD Row
Furniture Assembly details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the ETSO assembly (5) to the inboard
and outboard STD row suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to CMM 25-26-61 for the ETSO Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="430" seq="028"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-430-028-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Assemble the EFR Suite GA (Ref. IPL Fig. 2):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the loose items kit (45) to the inboard
and outboard EFR suite GA.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the data plates kit assembly (20):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach two self-adhesive serial
no and mods lables (40) to the data plates kit assembly (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive furniture
label (35) to the data plates kit assembly (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive continuation
label (30) to the data plates kit assembly (20).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>If removed, attach the self-adhesive medium
RFID high memory label (25) to the data plates kit assembly (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the data plates kit assembly (20)
to the inboard and outboard EFR suite GA.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the placard kit assembly (15) to the
inboard and outboard EFR suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 4 IPL for the Placard Kit Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the inboard and outboard EFR furniture
assembly (10) to the inboard and outboard EFR suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to Fig 5 IPL for the Inboard and Outboard EFR Furniture
Assembly details.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the ETSO assembly (5) to the inboard
and outboard EFR suite GA.</para>
<note><para>Refer to CMM 25-26-61 for the ETSO Assembly details.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="8000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-8000" revdate="20260617">
<title>FITS AND CLEARANCES</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="820" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-820-801-a01" revdate="20260617">
<title>Torque Settings</title>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>When fasteners are hand tightened make sure that you
do not tighten too much. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>When torque values are not specified, the parts are to be &ldquo;hand
tightened&rdquo;:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>You must make sure that each of the mating
surfaces are fully together and cannot turn and are not loose.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>You must think about the material type, for
example soft trim or plastic parts.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Fasteners with specified torque values:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="99A" seq="015"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8000" id="table-25-26-62-99a-015-a01"><?Pub Lcl
_tabindent="1">
