<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="11000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-11000" revdate="20260318">
<title>SPECIAL PROCEDURES</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="860" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="11000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-860-801-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Full Height Dropping Privacy Screen Locking Feature Procedure:</title>
<topic>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Reason for the Job:</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>To make sure that the full-height dropping
privacy screen returns to the TTL position correctly in the event
of electrical function failure.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Job set-up information:</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Job set-up:</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Procedure:</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY OR DEATH.</para></warning>
<para>Make sure that all the related electrical power is disconnected
from the privacy screen.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Two persons are necessary to manually operate
the privacy screen. One person to operate the manual override lever
and one person to deploy and stow the privacy screen with two hands
on the privacy screen for support.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Operate the mechanical override lever manually
for the privacy screen to return the privacy screen to TTL position
and make sure that the privacy screen is locked.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Full Height Dropping Privacy Screen Locking
Feature:</para>
<note><para>Applicable to front row centre suites only:</para></note>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Locking procedure (Ref Fig 11001):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Make sure that the privacy screen is at the
fully deployed position.</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Disengage the ball studs to lift the two
top caps (26-240, 26-240A) from the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Locking steps as shown in Ref Fig 11001,
Sheet 2:</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Move the adjustable slider aft, out of the
slot on the locking pin (STEP 1).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Turn the locking pin clockwise to lock the
privacy screen in position (STEP 2).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Move the adjustable slider forward in to
the slot on the locking pin (STEP 3).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Full Height Dropping Privacy Screen is now
locked at full height (STEP 4).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Engage the ball studs to attach the two top
caps (26-240, 26-240A) to the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Unlocking procedure (Ref Fig 11001):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Disengage the ball studs to lift the two
top caps (26-240, 26-240A) from the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Make sure that the Full Height Dropping Privacy
Screen is locked at full height.</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Unlocking steps as shown in Ref Fig 11001,
Sheet 3:</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Move the adjustable slider aft, out of the
slot on the locking pin (STEP 1).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Turn the locking pin anti-clockwise to lock
the privacy screen in position (STEP 2).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Move the adjustable slider forward in to
the slot on the locking pin (STEP 3).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Full Height Dropping Privacy Screen is now
unlocked (STEP 4).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Engage the ball studs to attach the two top
caps (26-240, 26-240A) to the top of the privacy screen.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Connect the related electrical power supply
to the privacy screen.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26"
subjnbr="62" func="820" seq="001" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="11000" chg="u" key="graphic-25-26-62-821-001-a01"
revdate="20260318">
<title>FULL-HEIGHT DROPPING PRIVACY SCREEN BELT FAILURE</title>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SPEC-11001-01-00.cgm" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-821-001-a01-1" revdate="20260318"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SPEC-11001-02-00.cgm" sheetnbr="2" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-821-001-a01-2" revdate="20260318"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SPEC-11001-03-00.cgm" sheetnbr="3" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-821-001-a01-3" revdate="20260318"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="ent252662-SPEC-11001-04-00.cgm" sheetnbr="4" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-26-62-821-001-a01-4" revdate="20260318"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-12000" revdate="20260617">
<title>REMOVAL</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-010-801-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>General</title>
<topic>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM
THE ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY THE approved PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS
ARE TO BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION
THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF
YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE
UNIT.</para></caution>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do not disassemble the unit more than is
necessary to complete the maintenance task.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Before removal record the position of components
and attaching parts to be removed. This will help during installation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Examine all removed components and attaching
parts for wear or damage. Replace parts as necessary.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For adjustment procedures and the identification
of damage or function failure refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-26-62-1000">pgblk-25-26-62-1000</refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do not remove pre-installed Earth Stud assemblies
unless damaged.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The numbers in brackets, for example (125),
refer to an item number in the IPL. The figure of the IPL is given
at the start of each section.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Where the numbers in brackets have a number
before the item, for example (10-125), this refers to an item number
in a different figure in the IPL. For this example, "10" refers to
the IPL figure and "125" to the item in that figure.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
