<title>Procedure:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="026"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-026-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the IUL (Ref. IPL Fig. 5-270, 6-265, 15-50) from
the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and 6) and the Dot Door Installation
(Ref. IPL Fig. 15):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the IUL (5-270, 6-265, 15-50).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the IUL (5-270, 6-265, 15-50)
at connector P8.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the IUL (5-270, 6-265,
15-50).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-001-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the TTL Indicator (Ref. IPL Fig. 5-275, 6-270, 15-55)
from the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and 6) and Dot Door Installation
(Ref. IPL Fig. 15):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the TTL Indicator (5-275, 6-270, 15-55).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the TTL indicator (5-275, 6-270,
15-55) connector D43P from the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connectors
P3 and P4.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the TTL indicator (5-275,
6-270, 15-55).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-002-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Reading Light (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-10, 8-10) from
the Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook and loop fasteners, remove
the nylatch plungers (25-60, 25-120), the nylatch grommet (25-65,
25-125) and collect the drip shields (25-55, 25-115) from the drip
shield installations (25-50, 25-110).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners, remove two hexagon
head screws (5-185, 6-185), two flat washers (5-190, 6-190) and collect
the cushion assembly (5-180, 6-180) from the bed infill installation
(5-175, 6-175).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners, remove one or
two countersunk head screws (22-265), one or two flat washers (22-270)
and collect the side cladding assembly (22-260) from the seat recess
claddings installation (22-1).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the reading light (7-10, 8-10)
connector P30 from the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connector
J5.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove three socket head screws (7-15, 8-15)
and collect the reading light (7-10, 8-10).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-003-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Hall Effect Sensor (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-20, 8-20)
from the Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the hall effect sensor (7-20, 8-20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the hall effect sensor (7-20,
8-20) connector P1 from the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connector
J3.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (7-25,
8-25), one hexagon nut (7-30, 8-30) and collect the hall effect sensor
(7-20, 8-20).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-004-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Main PCU (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-35, 7-35A, 8-40A,
8-40B) from the Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook, loop fastener and the duotec
fastener, remove and collect the central beam cover assembly (25-175)
from the under-seat drip tray assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive loop fastener and the double-sided
tapes, remove one hexagon head screw (23-105), one flat washer (23-110),
one countersunk head screw (23-115), one bush (23-120) and collect
the forward console cladding assembly (23-100) from the kick strip
and seals cladding installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fastener,
remove two countersunk head screws (24-235), two countersunk finishing
washers (24-240) and collect the FWD console cladding assembly (24-230)
from the kick strip and seals cladding installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook, loop and the duotec fasteners,
remove three countersunk head screws (24-260), three countersunk finishing
washers (24-265) and collect the AFT tray table cladding assembly
(24-255) from the N-aisle cladding Installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one or two countersunk head screws
(24-320), one or two counter-sunk finishing washers (24-325) and collect
the tray table panel (24-315) from the N-aisle cladding Installation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two pan head screws (12-10), two flat
washers (12-15) and collect the footwell panel assembly (12-5) from
the cocktail table assembly (12-1).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove three hexagon head screws (12-45,
12-50), three flat washers (12-55) and collect the armrest panel (12-40).
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the main PCU (7-35, 7-35A, 8-40A,
8-40B) connector J1 from the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connector
P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two socket head screws (7-40, 8-45),
two flat washers (7-45, 8-50) and collect the main PCU (7-35, 7-35A,
8-40A, 8-40B).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-005-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the RGBW Light (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-70, 8-80) from the
Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the RGBW light (7-70, 8-80).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the RGBW light (7-70, 8-80) connector
P1 from the harness assembly (7-110, 8-120) at connector J12.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the RGBW light (7-70,
8-80).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-006-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the RGBW Light (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-75, 7-75A, 8-85,
8-85A, 8-85B, 8-85C) from the Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the RGBW light (7-75, 7-75A, 8-85, 8-85A, 8-85B,
8-85C).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the RGBW light (7-75, 7-75A, 8-85,
8-85A, 8-85B, 8-85C) connector P1 from the harness assembly (7-130,
8-140) at connector J6.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the RGBW light (7-75,
7-75A, 8-85, 8-85A, 8-85B, 8-85C).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
