confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-018-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Monitor (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-270, 8-260) from the
Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the FWD fascia installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (20-10)
and collect the bracket assembly (20-5) from the FWD fascia installation.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four countersunk head screws (20-20),
four flat washers (20-25) and collect four monitor spacers (20-15).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the monitor (7-270, 8-260) from
the harness assembly (7-285, 8-275) at connector P10.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four socket cap head screw (7-275,
8-265) and collect the monitor (7-270, 8-260).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
