<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="024"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-024-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Actuator (Ref. IPL Fig. 13-65) from the Privacy
Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>HOLD THE ACTUATOR DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the actuator (13-65).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the manual override assembly (13-20)
and disconnect the actuator (13-65) from the harness assembly (7-500B,
8-65) connector P15 at J15.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (13-70),
two flat washers (13-75) and one hexagon nut (13-80) and collect the
actuator (13-65).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="025"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-025-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Actuator (Ref. IPL Fig. 13-230) from the Privacy
Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>HOLD THE ACTUATOR DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the actuator (13-230).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the actuator assembly (13-105) and
disconnect the actuator (13-230) from the harness assembly (8-495)
connector P13 at J13.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove and collect the actuator (13-230).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="027"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-027-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Literature Pocket Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 20-85)
from the FWD Fascia Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 20):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access, remove two hexagon head screws (20-60) and collect
the trim panel assembly (20-55) from the FWD fascia installation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (20-90),
four flat washers (20-95) and collect the literature pocket assembly
(20-85).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="028"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-028-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Facia Panel (Ref. IPL Fig. 20-125) from the
FWD Fascia Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 20):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the facia panel (20-125).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two hexagon head screws (20-45), two
flat washers (20-50) and collect the locking bracket (20-40) from
the FWD fascia installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Hold the grip on the bottom edge of the facia
panel.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pull the facia panel out of three bottom
clips.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pull the facia panel downward to release
the top edge of the panel from below the lip of the grab handle.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="029"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-029-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Canopy Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 5-135, 6-135)
from the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the Canopy Installation (5-135, 6-135).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Move the suite door to forward position.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove two countersunk head screws (28-100)
and collect the aisle capping assembly (28-95) from the canopy installation.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Get access, disengage the self-adhesive duotec
fasteners (28-345) and the transfer tape (28-340), remove and collect
the diffuser (28-335) from the cover assembly (28-330).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove five hexagon head screws (28-110,
28-115), five flat washers (28-120) and collect the grab handle (28-105)
with the trim panel assembly (28-125).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the harness assembly (8-125, 8-140)
at connectors J10, J11 and J6.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove six hexagon head screws (28-195, 28-200),
eleven flat washers (28-205, 28-210), five hexagon self-locking nuts
(28-215) and collect the sub canopy assembly (28-190).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Tilt the canopy and remove it from the shell.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="030"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-030-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Aisle Capping Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 28-225)
from the Canopy (Ref. IPL Fig. 28):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the aisle capping assembly (28-225).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the harness assembly (7-70, 8-80)
at connector J11.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (28-230),
two countersunk head screws (28-235), two countersunk head screws
(28-240), eight flat washers (28-245), four hexagon self-locking nuts
(28-250) and collect the aisle capping assembly (28-225) from the
canopy installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="031"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-031-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Meal Table Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5-155, 6-155)
from the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the N-aisle cladding Installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive hook, loop and the duotec fasteners,
remove three countersunk head screws (24-260), three countersunk finishing
washers (24-265) and collect the AFT tray table cladding assembly
(24-255) from the N-aisle cladding Installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one or two countersunk head screws
(24-320), one or two counter-sunk finishing washers (24-325) and collect
the tray table panel (24-315) from the N-aisle cladding Installation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Deploy the tray table and remove the seven
countersunk head screws (11-10, 11-15), three socket cap head screws
(11-20), three flat washers (11-25) and collect the meal table (11-5)
from the meal table assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="032"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-032-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Folding Armrest Installation (Ref. IPL Fig.
5-165) from the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Get access to the N-aisle cladding Installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners and double-sided
tape, remove two countersunk head screws (24-55), two countersunk
washers (24-60) and collect the under-aisle arm pad cladding (24-50)
from the N-aisle cladding Installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove four hexagon head screws (18-10, 18-15),
four flat washers (18-20) and collect the folding armrest assembly
(18-5) from the folding armrest installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="010" seq="033"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="12000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-010-033-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Removal of the Upper Console Stowage Installation (Ref. IPL
Fig. 5-145, 6-145) from the Furniture Assembly:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING REMOVAL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING REMOVAL, IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Open the stowage door assembly (17-90) to get better access.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners, remove one hexagon
head screws (22-115), two countersunk head screws (22-120), two countersunk
finishing washers (22-125) and collect the seat surround cladding
assembly (22-110) from the seat recess claddings installation (22-1).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disconnect the hall effect sensor (7-20,
8-20) connector P1 from the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connector
J3.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove one countersunk head screw (7-25,
8-25), one hexagon nut (7-30, 8-30) and collect the hall effect sensor
(7-20, 8-20).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>SEPARATION OF HOOK AND LOOP FASTENERS MUST BE DONE
CAREFULLY TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Disengage the self-adhesive duotec fastener, remove ten hexagon
head screws (17-70, 17-75, 17-80), ten flat washers (17-85) and collect
the structure stowage assembly (17-65) from the upper console stowage
installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-13000" revdate="20260617">
<title>INSTALLATION</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-410-801-a01" revdate="20260617">
<title>General</title>
<topic>
<warning><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM
THE ELECTRICAL SUPPLY BY THE approved PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY
THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS
ARE TO BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION
THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation,
IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE
UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT THERE IS A GAP BETWEEN THE
ACTUATOR AND THE SUITE STRUCTURE. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION
THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><?Pub Dtl><para>MAKE SURE THAT THERE IS A GAP BETWEEN THE
ACTUATOR MOVING PARTS, THE ELECTRICAL HARNESSES AND THE SUITE STRUCTURE.
IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE
UNIT.</para></caution>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attaching parts with wear or damage must
be replaced before LRU installation.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>When Loctite thread locking compound is used,
apply Loctite activator unless LRU installation procedure instructions
are different.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>A full list of fasteners with specified torque
values is given in the <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-26-62-8000">pgblk-25-26-62-8000</refint> pageblock.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>When fasteners are hand tightened make sure THAT you
do not tighten too much. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>When torque values are not specified, the parts are to be &ldquo;hand
tightened&rdquo;:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>You must make sure that each of the mating
surfaces are fully together and cannot turn and are not loose.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>You must think about the material type, for
example soft trim or plastic parts.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>For adjustment procedures, refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-26-62-1000">pgblk-25-26-62-1000</refint>.
</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The numbers in brackets, for example (125),
refer to an item number in the IPL. The figure of the IPL is given
at the start of each section.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Where the numbers in brackets have a number
before the item, for example (10-125), this refers to an item number
in a different figure in the IPL. For this example, "10" refers to
the IPL figure and "125" to the item in that figure.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>During installation, the actuator must be
properly adjusted with the suite structure to make sure of the full
privacy screen movement.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Make sure that the override cable is installed
into the override mechanism and adjust the override cable correctly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-410-802-a01" revdate="20260617">
<title>Installation of LRUs</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To install LRUs.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>List of LRUs:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
