<title>Procedure:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="053"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-053-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the IUL (Ref. IPL Fig. 5-270, 6-265, 15-50)
to the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and 6) and the Dot Door
Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 15):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Install the IUL (5-270, 6-265, 15-50).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the IUL (5-270, 6-265, 15-50) at
connector P8.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="028"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-028-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the TTL Indicator (Ref. IPL Fig. 5-275, 6-270,
15-55) to the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and 6) and Dot Door
Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 15):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Install the TTL indicator (5-275, 6-270, 15-55).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the TTL indicator (5-275, 6-270,
15-55) connector D43P to the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connectors
P3 and P4.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="029"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-029-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Reading Light (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-10, 8-10)
to the Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the reading light (7-10, 8-10) with three socket head
screws (7-15, 8-15).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the reading light (7-10, 8-10) connector
P30 to the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connector J5.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners,
attach the side cladding assembly (22-260) to the seat recess claddings
installation (22-1) with one or two countersunk head screws (22-265)
and one or two flat washers (22-270).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners,
attach the cushion assembly (5-180, 6-180) to the bed infill installation
(5-175, 6-175) with two hexagon head screws (5-185, 6-185) and two
flat washers (5-190, 6-190).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook and loop fasteners,
attach the drip shields (25-55, 25-115) to the drip shield installations
(25-50, 25-110) with nylatch plungers (25-60, 25-120) and the nylatch
grommet (25-65, 25-125).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="030"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-030-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Hall Effect Sensor (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-20,
8-20) to the Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the hall effect sensor (7-20, 8-20) with one socket cap
head screw (7-25, 8-25) and one hexagon nut (7-30, 8-30).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the hall effect sensor (7-20, 8-20)
connector P1 to the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connector J3.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="031"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-031-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Main PCU (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-35, 7-35A, 8-40A,
8-40B) to the Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the main PCU (7-35, 7-35A, 8-40A, 8-40B) with two socket
head screws (7-40, 8-45), two flat washers (7-45, 8-50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the main PCU (7-35, 7-35A, 8-40A,
8-40B) connector J1 to the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connector
P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the armrest panel (12-40) with three
hexagon head screws (12-45, 12-50) and three flat washers (12-55).
Torque the hexagon head screws (12-45) to 2.3 Nm (1.6 lbf.ft).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the footwell panel assembly (12-5)
to the cocktail table assembly (12-1) with two pan head screws (12-10)
and two flat washers (12-15). Torque the pan head screws (12-10) to
2.3 Nm (1.6 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the tray table panel (24-315) to the
N-aisle cladding Installation with one or two countersunk head screws
(24-320) and one or two counter-sunk finishing washers (24-325).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook, loop and the
duotec fasteners, attach the AFT tray table cladding assembly (24-255)
to the N-aisle cladding Installation with three countersunk head screws
(24-260) and three countersunk finishing washers (24-265).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener,
attach the FWD console cladding assembly (24-230) to the kick strip
and seals cladding installation with two countersunk head screws (24-235)
and two countersunk finishing washers (24-240).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN THE
CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Engage the self-adhesive loop fastener and the double-sided
tapes, attach the forward console cladding assembly (23-100) to the
kick strip and seals cladding installation with one hexagon head screw
(23-105), one flat washer (23-110), one countersunk head screw (23-115)
and one bush (23-120).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook, loop fastener
and the duotec fastener, attach the central beam cover assembly (25-175)
to the under-seat drip tray assembly (25-1).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="032"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-032-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the RGBW Light (Ref. IPL Fig. 7-70, 8-80) to
the Electrical Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 7 and 8):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Install the RGBW light (7-70, 8-80).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the RGBW light (7-70, 8-80) connector
P1 to the harness assembly (7-110, 8-120) at connector J12.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
