<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Install the next premium expansion unit (7-520, 8-520).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the next premium expansion unit (7-520,
8-520) connectors J4, J1 to the harness assembly (7-155, 8-165, 7-495,
8-490) at connectors P4, P1.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="051"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-051-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Actuator (Ref. IPL Fig. 13-65) from the
Privacy Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>HOLD THE ACTUATOR DURING INSTALLATION. IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the actuator (13-65) with one countersunk head screw
(13-70), two flat washers (13-75) and one hexagon nut (13-80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the manual override assembly (13-20)
and connect the actuator (13-65) to the harness assembly (7-500B,
8-65) connector P15 at J15.</para>
<note><para>Hold the actuator axle at anti-rotation rod end and actuator&rsquo;s
anchoring point.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="052"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-052-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Actuator (Ref. IPL Fig. 13-230) from the
Privacy Screen Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 13):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE THAT UNIT HAS BEEN ISOLATED FROM THE ELECTRICAL
SUPPLY BY THE APPROVED PERSONNEL. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS
THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY or death.</para></warning>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>HOLD THE ACTUATOR DURING INSTALLATION. IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THESE INSTRUCTIONS THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE PRODUCT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Install the actuator (13-230).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the actuator assembly (13-105) and
connect the actuator (13-230) to the harness assembly (8-495) connector
P13 at J13.</para>
<note><para>Hold the actuator axle at anti-rotation rod end and actuator&rsquo;s
anchoring point.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="054"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-054-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Literature Pocket Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig.
20-85) to the FWD Fascia Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 20):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the literature pocket assembly (20-85) with four hexagon
head screws (20-90) and four flat washers (20-95).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the trim panel assembly (20-55) to
the FWD fascia installation with two hexagon head screws (20-60).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="055"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-055-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Facia Panel (Ref. IPL Fig. 20-125) to the
FWD Fascia Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 20):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Push the facia panel upward to engage the top edge of the panel
below the lip of the grab handle.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Push the facia panel into three bottom clips.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Hold the grip on the bottom edge of the facia
panel.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the locking bracket (20-40) to the
FWD fascia installation with two hexagon head screws (20-45) and two
flat washers (20-50).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="056"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-056-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Canopy Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 5-135,
6-135) to the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Align the canopy with the shell and tilt it onto the mounting
points.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the sub canopy assembly (28-190) with
six hexagon head screws (28-195, 28-200), eleven flat washers (28-205,
28-210) and five hexagon self-locking nuts (28-215).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (8-125, 8-140)
at connectors J6, J10 and J11.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the grab handle (28-105) with the
trim panel assembly (28-125) with five hexagon head screws (28-110,
28-115) and five flat washers (28-120).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners
(28-345) and the transfer tape (28-340), attach the diffuser (28-335)
to the cover assembly (28-330).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the aisle capping assembly (28-95)
to the canopy installation with two countersunk head screws (28-100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Move the suite door to forward position.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="057"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-057-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Aisle Capping Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 28-225)
to the Canopy Installation (Ref. IPL Fig. 28):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the aisle capping assembly (28-225) to the canopy installation
with four hexagon head screws (28-230), two countersunk head screws
(28-235), two countersunk head screws (28-240), eight flat washers
(28-245) and four hexagon self-locking nuts (28-250). Torque the hexagon
screws (28-230) to 24.0 Nm (17.70 lbf.ft).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the harness assembly (7-70, 8-80)
at connector J11.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="058"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-058-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Meal Table Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5-155,
6-155) to the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5 and 6):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the meal table (11-5) to the meal table assembly the
seven countersunk head screws (11-10, 11-15), three socket cap head
screws (11-20) and three flat washers (11-25) and put the tray table
in the stowed position.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the tray table panel (24-315) to the
N-aisle cladding Installation with one or two countersunk head screws
(24-320) and one or two counter-sunk finishing washers (24-325).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive hook, loop and the
duotec fasteners, attach the AFT tray table cladding assembly (24-255)
to the N-aisle cladding Installation with three countersunk head screws
(24-260) and three countersunk finishing washers (24-265).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="059"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-059-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Folding Armrest Installation (Ref. IPL
Fig. 5-165) to the Furniture Assembly (Ref. IPL Fig. 5):</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Attach the folding armrest assembly (18-5) to the folding armrest
installation with four hexagon head screws (18-10, 18-15) and four
flat washers (18-20).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>MAKE SURE THAT DOUBLE-SIDED TAPE IS ATTACHED IN THE
CORRECT POSITION. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK
OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners and double-sided tape,
attach the under-aisle arm pad cladding (24-50) to the N-aisle cladding
Installation with two countersunk head screws (24-55) and two countersunk
washers (24-60).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="410" seq="060"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="13000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-410-060-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Installation of the Upper Console Stowage Installation (Ref.
IPL Fig. 5-145, 6-145) to the Furniture Assembly:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>NO RINGS, WATCHES OR ITEMS HANGING FROM BELTS ARE TO
BE WORN DURING installation. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE
IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS DURING installation, IF YOU
DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fastener, attach the structure
stowage assembly (17-65) to the upper console stowage installation
with ten hexagon head screws (17-70, 17-75, 17-80) and ten flat washers
(17-85).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Attach the hall effect sensor (7-20, 8-20)
with one countersunk head screw (7-25, 8-25) and one hexagon nut (7-30,
8-30).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Connect the hall effect sensor (7-20, 8-20)
connector P1 to the harness assembly (7-60, 8-65) at connector J3.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Engage the self-adhesive duotec fasteners,
attach the seat surround cladding assembly (22-110) to the seat recess
claddings installation (22-1) with one hexagon head screws (22-115),
two countersunk head screws (22-120) and two countersunk finishing
washers (22-125).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Close the cubby door (stowage door assembly)
(17-90).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="pgblk-25-26-62-15000" revdate="20260318">
<title>STORAGE (INCLUDING TRANSPORTATION)</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="550" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-550-801-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Storage</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This section gives instructions for the storage
limitations and transportation of the unit, and spare parts.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Tools, Fixtures and Equipment:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Consumables:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="530" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-530-001-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Packing:</title>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE that YOU USE APPROVED LIFTING POINTS and
applicable number of personnel TO move THE unit. if YOU DO NOT OBEY
THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF INJURY TO PERSONNEL AND DAMAGE
TO THE UNIT.</para></warning>
<caution><para>USE ONLY THE APPROVED PACKAGING CASE. IF YOU DO NOT
OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION, DAMAGE TO THE UNIT CAN OCCUR.</para></caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Put the unit in an applicable packaging case
and attach to a pallet.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="550" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-550-002-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Storage:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>DO NOT keep THE UNIT NEAR FLUIDS THAT CAN CAUSE CORROSION
OR DAMAGE. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF
DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT keep the unit NEAR SOURCES OF HEAT. IF YOU DO
NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT STACK the unit. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION
THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>Put the unit in a clean, dry storage area with a good supply
of air.</para>
<note><para>Keep the relative humidity below 80% with a temperature
range from 5.0 &ordm;C to 40.0 &ordm;C (41 &ordm;F to 104 &ordm;F).</para>
</note>
<note><para>IFE components can have their own storage requirements.
Contact IFE suppliers for more information.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Put the unit in a position where the identification
label can be clearly read.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="510" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-510-001-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Transportation:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>DO NOT STACK the unit. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY THIS INSTRUCTION
THERE IS A RISK OF DAMAGE TO THE UNIT.</para></caution>
<para>The unit in its packaging case with identification label must
be moved in the correct position. The wooden pallet must be at the
bottom.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="530" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-530-002-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Unit Lifting Points:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="540" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-540-001-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>After Storage:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do a functional check of the unit after storage.
Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-26-62-1000">pgblk-25-26-62-1000
</refint> and <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-26-62-5000">pgblk-25-26-62-5000
</refint>.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="550" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-26-62-550-003-a01" revdate="20260318"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Unit Storage Life Limits:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="550" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" chg="u"
key="task-25-26-62-550-802-a01" revdate="20260318">
<title>Storage of Spare Parts</title>
<topic>
<title>Reason for the Job:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This section gives instructions for the storage,
management of periodic checks and transportation of spare parts.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Spare parts must have a periodic check test
to make sure that they operate correctly. The time interval between
two periodic checks is different for each of the parts. No time limit
is specified to discard the parts if their periodic check test is
fully compliant.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up Information:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Tools, Fixtures and Equipment:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Consumables:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Job Set-up:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Not Applicable.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Procedure:</title>
<prclist1><?Pub Dtl>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>General Storage Requirements:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The equipment must be stored under the condition
as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Original individual package, hermetically
sealed with desiccant.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Warehouse temperature between 5.0 &ordm;C
to 40.0 &ordm;C (41 &ordm;F to 104 &ordm;F).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Humidity &lt; 80%.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Protected against the rain and contamination
(dust, sun light, sand etc).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Periodic Checks:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Refer to Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-26-62-550-001-a01"></refint> for details of periodic
test and check for each product.</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="26" subjnbr="62" func="550" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15000" id="table-25-26-62-550-001-a01">
<title>Periodic Check</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center" charoff="50" char="">
